{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition","id":1562353,"title":"FAQ on 6th edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-30T15:13:37-07:00","id":1562353,"title":"FAQ on 6th edition","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/vtm-sixth-edition-faq\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.ctfassets.net/u73tyf0fa8v1/6SK2guLFYLH8FnhJtNxmJG/ec236ccbdceca9697879a22073264d5e/worldofdarkness-top_bg_free_content.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=630&amp;fit=fill&amp;f=center\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/vtm-sixth-edition-faq\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade 6th Edition FAQ - Paradox Interactive </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/vtm-sixth-edition-faq\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/vtm-sixth-edition-faq </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> World of Darkness </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hello Vamily,<br /> <br /> Thank you for the amazing reception to the announcement of Vampire: The Masquerade 6th Edition. We\u2019re so happy to finally share the alpha playtest with you!<br /> <br /> We know many of you have questions about what we\u2019re doing, and we\u2019ll do our best to answer them in the upcoming months. We\u2019ve got many dev diaries coming to cover these topics in-depth, but for now we wanted to put together a brief FAQ to cover some of the most commonly asked questions that we\u2019ve seen from the community.<br /> <br /> Note that we\u2019re still in early development and a lot of things are still subject to change. If you have more questions, don\u2019t hesitate to reach out to us on our social media channels or on the World of Darkness Discord.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>General White Wolf Questions:</u></b><b> Why are we doing a 6th Edition?</b><br /> <br /> We want to create a solid baseline to support various styles of play, and a strong kickoff point for settings that will come after we\u2019ve created the new Vampire: The Masquerade book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Does this mean all 5th Edition products are out-of-date/not usable at my table?</b><br /> <br /> The 6th Edition line of books will have different mechanics, but many of the same characters and metaplot advancements will remain relevant. That means that, while not fully backwards-compatible, much of the lore in the 5th Edition books will carry over to the 6th Edition books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What about Mage, Changeling etc - are they not receiving 5th editions?</b><br /> <br /> They are not, but that doesn\u2019t mean that some of them won\u2019t get some attention in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What about Werewolf and Hunters - are they receiving new editions already?</b><br /> <br /> At the moment the White Wolf devs are fully focused on the new Vampire: The Masquerade edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>V6-specific Questions:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Will we have to learn new systems, i.e. Hunger mechanics vs Blood pool?</b> Yes, there will be new systems and mechanics to learn, such as \u201cDrama\u201d, \u201cQuickening\u201d, \u201cChoose Your Pain\u201d, \u201cDevil\u2019s Bargain\u201d and the new \u201cBeast/Nature\u201d tracker. But don\u2019t worry, playing and running the game are both easier and faster. You need fewer steps and less prep to jump right in, and the rules help you push play forward without friction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Will there be more metaplot progression?</b><br /> <br /> Yes. The history of the World of Darkness will be preserved, advanced and represented in the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What\u2019s Drama?</b><br /> <br /> Storytellers now have a resource called \u201cDrama\u201d that they can spend to complicate the PCs\u2019 circumstances or introduce new twists into the Story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What\u2019s Quickening?</b><br /> <br /> Quickening is a new mechanic that rewards players for rolling well, giving them a resource they can spend to improve their chances in future situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Will I be able to use my V5 dice at the table?</b><br /> <br /> No, V6 uses a different system to count successes and failures, so we use regular D10 dice. We\u2019ve also made changes to the Hunger system, so the Hunger dice are not relevant to V6.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Where did my Health and Blood Points go?</b><br /> <br /> Health and Blood Points have been combined into a single resource called Vitae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What\u2019s the Humanity Scale?</b><br /> <br /> The Humanity tracker has been updated to the Humanity Scale, which tracks the inner struggle between your monstrous and humane sides, as they constantly press their urges onto you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How does physical and social conflict work now?</b><br /> <br /> Physical and social conflict share a unified procedure, making both equally important and supported by the rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How will the Discipline powers change?</b><br /> <br /> Each Discipline will have multiple powers, and many Discipline powers now scale with you, growing in power as you gain dots. The alpha playtest shows off many of these new powers, and the final book will include powers for each Discipline up to 5 dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>How many clans will be in the final book?</b><br /> <br /> There will be 14 clans total in the book; the alpha playtest includes 7 so far (Brujah, Gangrel, Lasombra, Ministry, Nosferatu, Toreador, and Ventrue).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Can I play as the different stages of Vampirism?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, the final book will include rules for playing a ghoul, a duskborn, a neonate, an ancilla, a caitiff, or an elder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What about playing as Sabbat or other sects?</b><br /> <br /> In V6 you will be able to align with the Camarilla, the Anarchs, the Sabbat, Independents or The Unbound.<br /> <br /> <b>Is there a release date yet?</b><br /> <br /> No, not yet. We are still in the alpha phase of development and want to ensure we can polish the material and implement the valuable feedback we\u2019re receiving before we announce specifics like a release date or cost. </div> </div> </div>I really wish they'd stop trying to make vamily a thing,,,,,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness/og-image.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness Nexus - Digital TTRPG Toolset </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Official Digital Toolset for World of Darkness on Demiplane </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> couple of notes from playtest docs as well<br /> <br /> -necromancy and oblivion appear to be re-seperated Oblivion appears to be obtenerbration<br /> <br /> -Health and hunger are merged.<br /> <br /> -protean appears to merged with Animalism (!)<br /> <br /> -a new disciplines called corruption and Tellurgy are present<br /> <br /> -the clan of death is again being refered to as clan Giovanni,<br /> <br /> -viss is back<br /> <br /> -a lot of supplementary mechanics are being tied directly to your clan outside of discipline and flaw, clan beasts seem to have a specific flavour<br /> <br /> -some clans can choose one of the core disciplines to be a different one.<br /> <br /> Honestly not sure what to make of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-30-2026, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T15:39:05-07:00","id":1562356,"title":"","content":"<ul><li><b><i><i>Beast and Nature Tracker</i>:</i></b> The inner struggle between the Beast and the remains of your mortal conscience is represented by the Beast and Nature Tracker. Every night, both sides of you fight for dominance. It\u2019s up to you to decide which side you feed and which side you try to contain.</li> <li><b><i><i>Frenzy</i> and <i>Outburst</i> Rules:</i></b> When you ignore one side of your internal struggle for too long, its impulses can grow too strong for you to resist. In these situations, you risk partially losing control of your character, who is compelled to act in ways to satiate the neglected side.</li> </ul>At a glance, this system sounds like the coolest addition. Go too bestial and your Humanitas can frenzy as your conscience screams that this is lower than it's willing to go.<br /> <br /> Demeanor's gone, since Vampires are liars and manipulators and their demeanors can be anything they imitate, but Nature remains, and is part of the mechanic for how the Vampire's human side imposes itself. During Outburst, the Vampire's impulses reflect their Nature, and in Frenzy, their impulses reflect their clan curse.<br /> <br /> I have a soft spot for clever and elegant attempts to impose order on chaos (I was born that way, my moon sign is Virgo), and someone was cooking when they came up with this. It's very aesthetically pleasing to me, on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-31-2026, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T15:50:41-07:00","id":1562357,"title":"","content":"Couple reverts are interesting, couple of new ideas are head-scratch inducing (clan traits? Do we want to be like D&amp;D?) but all in all it's all so early version that's hard to be too invested one way or another.<br /> <br /> Case in point for D&amp;D0fication: NPCs have Levels. Competence levels that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":".  Edit 07-30-2026, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T16:15:52-07:00","id":1562358,"title":"","content":"It's a pretty small thing, but I can't really get myself past the wealth resources, but vehicles as a separate resource you have to put points into. But then I've never really been into separating off things you can spend money to have as a separate thing to spend points on from spending points on money. I suppose they could just clarify that you can in fact spend money on goods and services. It otherwise just feels odd and almost punitively granular, especially in a game whose only really clearly embodied statement seems to be wanting a simplified and streamlined experience.<br /> <br /> Other minor little bits and bobs: I'm amused at them basically giving into &quot;fine, vampires can have sex and enjoy sex&quot; without the grudging/passive aggressiveness that has accompanied that previously.<br /> <br /> I'm in favour of it taking being close to a bonfire to trigger fire fear frenzy as an explicit thing. Better for historical games certainly. As far as, &quot;Fine, your supernatural monster can just make a normal defense roll to dodge bullets&quot;, a lot of it seems to be very &quot;we're going to try to lean into things people expect from general modern vampire media experiences at this point&quot;.<br /> <br /> Otherwise honestly I was cold to a bunch of it. The rules seem to be saying that you're now very, very limited in how many total discipline dots you can have, which I'm pretty bleah on. I mean it's certainly hitting some personal preferences that the SI is not being treated as much of a thing from what little info there is, and that touchstones seem to have gone the way of all flesh (I think there were ways to salvage it, but the v5 implementation was awful, and that showed in the ceaseless parade of the majority of suggested ideas for use the books would keep giving for them being to use them to threaten and punish players). I'm not really into no passive bonuses from disciplines anymore, or sectioning off some powers as clan only. <br /> <br /> People super into V5 are probably going to be irked that it's not really anything like V5, people who don't want an extremely streamlined VtM experience (which seems to be its goal) are not going to be happy with that. People who are just desperate to hear the Sabbat are an official playable option again will be happy about that. People who prefer VtM to... how to put it, be about VtM, in the way that D&amp;D isn't really about fantasy overall at this point so much as it is about itself, will likely not be thrilled by some of this stuff (I know people who lost their shit about even grudging &quot;vampires can have sex&quot; for instance when previous editions would note such, in some way)<br /> <br /> Feels like an extremely mixed bag at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T01:24:51-07:00","id":1562362,"title":"","content":"The fact that at Beast 2 and higher, if your character has sex, it can put you into torpor is fucking hilarious. Is it likely to happen? No, but its the fact that it can at all that makes it funny LOL.<br /> <br /> Also using Blush of Life now hurts you unless you're Mortal 2 or over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In fact there are now a bunch of powers that injure you if you use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T03:15:19-07:00","id":1562363,"title":"","content":"I've not yet downloaded the alpha, cos I don't want to deal with Demiplane right this second, but I'm cautiously optimistic. Some of this stuff can change. Janky rules hopefully being first on the list. It's likely just because I can play Sabbat again, but some of the ideas they've mentioned also feel like things I've advocated on this very board (are they reading all our old threads? I hope so!).<br /> <br /> Disciplines are probably my least favourite part of what's been discussed, but I can always change those. And I like that Vicissitude is its own thing again, and that Obtenebration isn't Necromancy. Though someone said Tremere get Necromancy now, so maybe it's just that all blood magic is now Necromancy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T03:52:28-07:00","id":1562364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562363#post1562363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not yet downloaded the alpha, cos I don't want to deal with Demiplane right this second, but I'm cautiously optimistic. Some of this stuff can change. Janky rules hopefully being first on the list. It's likely just because I can play Sabbat again, but some of the ideas they've mentioned also feel like things I've advocated on this very board (are they reading all our old threads? I hope so!).<br /> <br /> Disciplines are probably my least favourite part of what's been discussed, but I can always change those. And I like that Vicissitude is its own thing again, and that Obtenebration isn't Necromancy. Though someone said Tremere get Necromancy now, so maybe it's just that all blood magic is now Necromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get the playtest pack from Drivethru <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/publisher/1/white-wolf/category/58715/vampire-the-masquerade-playtest\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/publ...erade-playtest</a><br /> <br /> Many things can and will change. The only question is will they change for the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Oh and yes, Obtenebration and Vicissitude are back but Protean is in Animalism now so... :P <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T04:39:13-07:00","id":1562366,"title":"","content":"If they bring the Paths back we can have Sabbat again, but with the new monstrosity/mortal track we cannot, so we shall see. Because all monsters are increasingly mindless, the post human weirdness that makes the sabbat fun is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T05:38:51-07:00","id":1562367,"title":"","content":"The whole Giovanni becoming Hecata was a pretty interesting plot point and one of the things I liked about 5E. The Giovanni were always a little too niche and stereotypical so merging them in with some other clans overall made things more interesting to me. Hopefully it's just a name rebranding and they're keeping everything else. Though, if anything is get retconned I'll bet it would be the Harbringer's lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T06:29:44-07:00","id":1562368,"title":"","content":"Harbinger lore was always a bit messy, they're cappadocians but a super special type, they're kinda wraiths they hate the giovanni because they stole their revenge etc etc. Imo they should have said they're surviving cappodicians from differant places and they hate the giovanni because the giovanni tried to wipe them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T09:39:42-07:00","id":1562369,"title":"","content":"Really interested in v6, looks apetizing to me. Also welcome back in good graces my siblings in the Sabbat, you have been missed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":25163,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","user":"Crytash2","date":". 07-31-2026, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T11:39:16-07:00","id":1562372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562366#post1562366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they bring the Paths back we can have Sabbat again, but with the new monstrosity/mortal track we cannot, so we shall see. Because all monsters are increasingly mindless, the post human weirdness that makes the sabbat fun is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The emphasis on the vampire's human nature in the alpha playtest ruleset seems at first glance like reframes the Sabbat as having cultivated the very worst of humanity in themselves for philosophical reasons while the Beast just cares about Beast things, which... tracks, actually? Like, that's fair! And it splits the proverbial baby by preserving their antagonist vibe for those who prefer it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T14:11:41-07:00","id":1562373,"title":"","content":"First thing to say: didn't knew this Demiplane thing, wish I hadn't. I hate sites that are excessively heavy to load just because bad code or safetyporn.<br /> <br /> Second: they forgot to put in the Diablerie rules that the victim must be lower Gen than you. As it's now, you can dig on 10 Thin Bloods and get to 3rd Generation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562356#post1562356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demeanor's gone, since Vampires are liars and manipulators and their demeanors can be anything they imitate</div> </div> </div> </div>Demeanor's gone because it was stupid since 1st edition. Absolutely no one works in the way the old Nature/Demeanor rules described.<br /> <br /> I'm on the fence about the Humanity Scale. The idea is good for A vampire game, I'm not sure if it is for VtM. But it's certainly an improvement over V5. Away with the morality play of Legacy and the Grimdark Slope of V5, now we have a Forsaken-style Harmony balance.<br /> <br /> The idea that morality will be further removed from this is also interesting and I hope it gets through. This will basically make the Paths and Roads playable again even if without rules. I do want rules for them, but this is already something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562357#post1562357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(clan traits? Do we want to be like D&amp;D?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Any problem? And from everything there, is it that what you thought D&amp;D-like?<br /> <br /> Yes, there's a lot of DnD influence very clearly, and some of it isn't very good, but most I am ok with. It was about time they started picking the good parts of other games instead of being too pedantic to mingle with the plebe.<br /> <br /> I do think some clear influence on terminology has to go for the sake of immersion, though. It is minor, but I can't seriously call the 14th and 15th Generations &quot;Duskborn&quot;.<br /> <br /> NPC levels aren't a bad idea in itself, but I think this is not yet the best approach. And the tiers of play as Difficulty guidelines don't really work in a game where dice pools vary so much.<br /> <br /> Clan Traits I'm on the fence, but I think they can work. Particularly I liked the idea of Merits that do the work of particular Discipline Powers or Devotions, and most Clan Traits are that. The Ministry getting the effects of Serpentis that way, I really like the idea.<br /> <br /> But I seriously have no idea why D&amp;D when this is one of the oldest and most used mechanics in TTRPG history. I know it's just a joke, but still.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pretty small thing, but I can't really get myself past the wealth resources, but vehicles as a separate resource you have to put points into.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird. I'm not sure if as bad as it seems at first, but it's really weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose they could just clarify that you can in fact spend money on goods and services.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the idea, though.<br /> <br /> What they made into Physical Assets are pretty big things during play: vehicle, property, haven and repository. Those aren't just expensive, IME they're indeed the most immediately and universally relevant things a character can own with direct impact on the game.<br /> <br /> And during downtime you can move dots around those, so you're &quot;buying and selling&quot;. I'd say it's less that a wealthy character can't get those things, and more that in play they'll be less reliable.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, weird, but I'll give it a try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules seem to be saying that you're now very, very limited in how many total discipline dots you can have, which I'm pretty bleah on.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're actually the same as always, just spelled in a confusing manner.<br /> <br /> You can buy as many as you want and can afford, but only to the top level of your Generation, like always.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's certainly hitting some personal preferences that the SI is not being treated as much of a thing from what little info there is, and that touchstones seem to have gone the way of all flesh</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be so hasty, this is just an Alpha test. The thing as saw is a glimpse of the mechanics they want to hammer down, not anything to do with the actual setting or the final game.<br /> <br /> I've seen this style of development before, the playtests really let out a lot of stuff, they're not demonstrations of the product.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really into no passive bonuses from disciplines anymore, or sectioning off some powers as clan only.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the passive bonus being gone is good. I understand the appeal, but they mostly made for boring Disciplines that felt more necessary than interesting.<br /> <br /> Felt like that since my first contact with VtM almost 30 years ago, but I got used to it. Now after the initial shock, I think it's for the best.<br /> <br /> The sectioning off powers I'm not sure. I think it depends on the powers, mostly, how bad I'll feel about it, and if those Traits can be &quot;taught&quot; through blood just like Disciplines can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562358#post1562358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">people who don't want an extremely streamlined VtM experience (which seems to be its goal)</div> </div> </div> </div>So they say.<br /> <br /> Not sure if you noticed, but the overall structure is mostly the same, and the main differences come from using CoD dice rolls.<br /> <br /> I'm not feeling it all that streamlined, yet. Not to a point I can confidently say isn't just because this is a playtest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562362#post1562362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also using Blush of Life now hurts you unless you're Mortal 2 or over.<br /> <br /> In fact there are now a bunch of powers that injure you if you use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>More that damage taken is always instantly healed. Legacy you'd have 10 BP + 7 HB, so 17 dmg to torpor if you're healing, but 6 of those are penalized, so 11 clean &quot;hp&quot;. V5 has 10 BP + 3 HB + Stamina, so 14 to 18 dmg if healing, but it's unreliable and you can end up with only 9 to 13, and still risks penalty. This playtest gives us 10 + Stamina Vitae, so 11 to 15 of dmg without penalty. And without mending/turn limits.<br /> <br /> Considering what Kindred are, I think Vitae for health makes enough sense. It's not your body's structure what hold you together, it's the Curse, and the Blood animates you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562363#post1562363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines are probably my least favourite part of what's been discussed, but I can always change those. And I like that Vicissitude is its own thing again, and that Obtenebration isn't Necromancy. Though someone said Tremere get Necromancy now, so maybe it's just that all blood magic is now Necromancy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere can choose between Necromancy and Thaumaturgy, or something to this effect, they are not really in this playtest. Also TB Alchemy is gone, apparently.<br /> <br /> I think you may like the Disciplines, though not as much as VtR2nd. The system is mostly like V5, but with the following changes:<br /> <br /> 1. Some powers became Merits that use level in a Discipline as prerequisite. Serpentis is back almost completely in this way. Those are cheap to buy and include a lot of &quot;dead weight&quot; that did too little or were too passive.<br /> <br /> 2. We can buy powers freely. Not only that, they are actually cheaper than the Discipline dot. So you get a Power at level X for free when you buy Dot X, then buy new level X powers for way less.<br /> -- In Clans are \u00d75<br /> -- Out of Clan \u00d76<br /> -- New Power \u00d72<br /> <br /> 3. Many powers now scale with the Discipline, either because your dots are used in the effect or because they have a &quot;Maturing&quot; effect that you can access to certain Discipline levels. For example, Aspect of the Beast gives you any single bestial trait you want, but at 3 dots you can get two at once and at 5 dots, three at once.<br /> <br /> Overall I see potential. Tentatively optimistic is indeed the word, but I think at least foundation for it we have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562366#post1562366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they bring the Paths back we can have Sabbat again, but with the new monstrosity/mortal track we cannot, so we shall see. Because all monsters are increasingly mindless, the post human weirdness that makes the sabbat fun is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's easier.<br /> <br /> The mindless thing was removed. Now you're functional all the way. Also the scale isn't moral oriented, at least not as much, so you can have the Path followers no problem, with the whole range of weirdness.<br /> <br /> In this Playtest, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562367#post1562367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Giovanni becoming Hecata was a pretty interesting plot point and one of the things I liked about 5E. The Giovanni were always a little too niche and stereotypical so merging them in with some other clans overall made things more interesting to me. Hopefully it's just a name rebranding and they're keeping everything else. Though, if anything is get retconned I'll bet it would be the Harbringer's lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata as social construct was good, for the reasons you gave. The Hecata as all lines of Necromancy suddenly being the same thing unless you buy a patch with a Loresheet was an abomination.<br /> <br /> And I hope they don't retcon anything, I like the gonzo origin of the Lamia and think something can still be done about the Harbingers without removing the &quot;ghosts of Kaimakli&quot; backstory. Even because we'll have now their childer, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T15:15:38-07:00","id":1562383,"title":"","content":"After going over the playtest material, I can say V6 is not for me. I'll just go back to VtM20 since it at least requires less house ruling to make workable and get rid of PTSD/CPTSD trigger issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T16:39:48-07:00","id":1562389,"title":"","content":"This is edition is already absolutely insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T17:02:18-07:00","id":1562390,"title":"","content":"WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WHAT?<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition removed??! Holy crap!<br /> <br /> I'm just freaking baffled here! They're doing away so many things V20 players hated, while in the same turn alienating V5 fans even MORE.. <br /> <br /> I love that the SI are gone, but what is the reasoning behind this after it was so big in V5??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T19:07:29-07:00","id":1562393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562390#post1562390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Inquisition removed??! Holy crap!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an Alpha Playtest. It has no plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T19:53:09-07:00","id":1562395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562393#post1562393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an Alpha Playtest. It has no plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has some light plot in the technology section that makes the SI come off as far less of a thing, is what I was referring to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many abandoned modern technology altogether to stay out of its reach, but soon enough, Kindred figured out ways around it. The rise of AI and the post-truth era has since helped to repair the damage that all the surveillance did to the secrets of the undead. </div> </div> </div>And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surveillance is still a fact of unlife for the most part, but because so much of it now feeds on content scraped from the internet, it has filled with slop and grown less reliable by the year. Are vampires behind that too? The confusion has forced the Inquisition to commit a lot of errors, which has cost them dearly in resources. </div> </div> </div>There's also bits in other places like references to the Beckoning as something that is now over. There's *some* setting and plot touches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T19:57:01-07:00","id":1562396,"title":"","content":"And the &quot;younger vampires forgetting the lessons of the Second Inquisition&quot; in the same tech section, that section makes it come off like treating the SI as something past its heyday (which someone could argue might not make a ton of sense, but that would be a different discussion, the material as is just seems to have this lean)<br /> <br /> To reiterate, I said this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the SI is not being treated as much of a thing from what little info there is, </div> </div> </div>I didn't say &quot;looks like they were removed completely&quot; I said &quot;not being treated as much of a thing from what little info there is&quot;. There's some info, it has the lean it has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 07-31-2026, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T20:33:28-07:00","id":1562398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562390#post1562390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WAIT WHAT?<br /> <br /> I love that the SI are gone, but what is the reasoning behind this after it was so big in V5??</div> </div> </div> </div>Why it's the bane of every government institution. Sudden Funding cuts./s<br /> <br /> And the cams have nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:39:41-07:00","id":1562405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562396#post1562396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say &quot;looks like they were removed completely&quot; I said &quot;not being treated as much of a thing from what little info there is&quot;. There's some info, it has the lean it has.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but my answer to you was just to not be too hasty, as things can change wildly.<br /> <br /> You quoted my response to another poster who took this information a lot more seriously and extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T22:57:45-07:00","id":1562408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562405#post1562405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but my answer to you was just to not be too hasty, as things can change wildly.<br /> <br /> You quoted my response to another poster who took this information a lot more seriously and extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, quoting you was mostly just for wanting to note there is a some measure of plot in the playtest so far in reference to the notion of there being none.<br /> <br /> It could certainly change by the middle or end of things, or even just in a month. Right now what we have ranges from &quot;no more Beckoning&quot; to &quot;notably reduced Inquisition&quot; in dribs and drabs. There's some other small pieces of setting stuff besides.<br /> <br /> The rest was just not wanting what I said to be taken to &quot;the Inquisition is dead&quot; in some discussion forum broken telephone thing after seeing the &quot;SI has been removed?&quot; thing in the other post, sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T23:06:19-07:00","id":1562411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562393#post1562393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an Alpha Playtest. It has no plot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the Beckoning is apparently gone. Whatever type of Playtest this is... definitely has metaplot changes from the onset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T23:14:13-07:00","id":1562413,"title":"","content":"<b>Cults of the Blood Gods </b>was one of the best supplements ever done and the people at OPP did their absolute best to make a stupid seeming idea (combine all these Bloodlines into one clan) into a fantastic story concept.<br /> <br /> They succeeded beyond my wildest dreams and it is one of my all time favorite supplements, up there with Chicago by Night 1&amp;5 as well as LTSRR.<br /> <br /> Undoing this just seems both spiteful and stupid.<br /> <br /> Especially since as Europeans they might note how weird it is we have &quot;Clan John.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank"