won't.<br /> <br /> This is an early playtest, they won't release this version or anything like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the larger changes as a whole with sixth edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T05:09:14-07:00","id":1562425,"title":"","content":"<img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_2158_1785585931809_246\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2158\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2158\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=2158&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> They clearly have plans to change the metaplot and Beckoning being done is one of them. It is also not surprising as Ericsson mentioned that Beckoning ending was the plan from the get go. Granted the other bulletpoints say nothing of substance really. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562419#post1562419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, we won't.<br /> <br /> This is an early playtest, they won't release this version or anything like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they may change the decisions that they already made for the playtest but I will reiterate: they won't change them if they won't hear criticism (fill out the feedback form, people). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T11:19:33-07:00","id":1562435,"title":"","content":"So Vampire: The Masquerade, a Skill-based game, now has less skills than Dungeons and Dragons, a Class-based game.<br /> Riiiiight\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T23:42:04-07:00","id":1562458,"title":"","content":"The current AI-drenched irl status quo, where every news story and photo has to be treated with suspicion until proven real, didn't exist when 5th Edition was conceived, and the idea that the flood of misinformation made discrediting Masquerade breaches easier is a funny bit of satire. I love it.<br /> <br /> The end of the Beckoning could be a rich source of ominous horror. The elders came back, and they would very much like their positions back and that's going to be exciting and complicated, but also there's no telling what kind of ancient monsters are hiding behind their eyes.<br /> <br /> Another reaction to Paradox's handling of 5th Edition that I like: &quot;The Tattered Facade&quot; supplement essentially retcons the whole Baali bloodline out of existence, replacing them with Baali as a name for a kind of wight. The V6 playtest material adds a new discipline, Corruption, which is essentially a less corny version of Daimonion, enabling a Storyteller-created sect of apostates to take the old bloodline's place if the retcon isn't counter-retconned back into the world of V6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-02-2026, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T00:53:28-07:00","id":1562460,"title":"","content":"I've read some thorough critiques of this V6 alpha playtest from a few people and find myself agreeing with them. This is so full of bad ideas that throwing it all out and starting anew is likely a better idea than trying to fix something with this many issues. A lot of which shouldn't have even made it to the alpha stage in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T02:16:39-07:00","id":1562463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562460#post1562460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read some thorough critiques of this V6 alpha playtest from a few people and find myself agreeing with them. This is so full of bad ideas that throwing it all out and starting anew is likely a better idea than trying to fix something with this many issues. A lot of which shouldn't have even made it to the alpha stage in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as much as I don't like many things from the playtest and agree that changes can be made I would not hold my breath for WW to start from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T02:41:05-07:00","id":1562466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562373#post1562373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Actually it's easier.<br /> <br /> The mindless thing was removed. Now you're functional all the way. Also the scale isn't moral oriented, at least not as much, so you can have the Path followers no problem, with the whole range of weirdness.<br /> <br /> In this Playtest, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, Monstrous is tied to Clan, and past Monstrous 3 you become a wight, so you are always interacting with Humanity. But this is an alpha, and I might be reading it wrong or not getting something, did have to re-read and you are right about the mindless thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T04:00:11-07:00","id":1562470,"title":"","content":"So it looks like V5 is basically getting the 4E D&amp;D treatment, where most of the changes introduced in that edition are being rolled back in the new edition. <br /> <br /> Honestly a lot of these metaplot changes don't really even make sense. It's not like the Second Inquisition, which is formed up from intelligence agencies from around the planet and can get away with dropping bombs on NATO countries will just say, &quot;Pack it up boys, we caught all the vampires. We're done forever.&quot; <br /> <br /> t this point, I think the best thing for V6 is to simply say that V5 never happened and have it be a direct continuation from V20, because it looks like that's basically what they want to do anyway. That would let it avoid all of the gymnastics they're going to have to do to try and walk back all of the setting changes introduced in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T04:17:17-07:00","id":1562471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562470#post1562470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly a lot of these metaplot changes don't really even make sense. It's not like the Second Inquisition, which is formed up from intelligence agencies from around the planet and can get away with dropping bombs on NATO countries will just say, &quot;Pack it up boys, we caught all the vampires. We're done forever.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It could go the way what Mithras and de Camden pulled<br /> Simply <i>use</i><i>d and manipulated</i> the Second Inquisition<br /> It would be hilariously easy to get hold on the key pieces on the board and let it simply fade from the mind<br /> Intelligence agencies shown how one on the top can decide the course of actions - just see J. Edgar Hoover<br /> It was a half-assed thing anyway in the eyes of the Governments IF they took it seriusly - old guards out ,new in and in and in few months the whole thing run out of steam and the dust settle<br /> It is believable<br /> Project Stargate ran for ~25 years and...? Today is just a shurg, not many even know it existed, despite it is &quot;common knowledge&quot; <br /> The SI never went public, ran a what? Few years tops with full power? Somwhere I had a time line of it<br /> I don't think it is that unbelievable after the Camarilla restructured itself and cleared out the problems, it shelved it<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T04:46:06-07:00","id":1562472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562470#post1562470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly a lot of these metaplot changes don't really even make sense. It's not like the Second Inquisition, which is formed up from intelligence agencies from around the planet and can get away with dropping bombs on NATO countries will just say, &quot;Pack it up boys, we caught all the vampires. We're done forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>part of the problem with the 2nd inquisition was it was often more of a plot device than a faction. It was a goverment (which goverment? I doubt israel and the vatican are sharing notes) conspiracy which had the power of an actual goverment. It was a conspiracy but could draw on highest tier resources without blowback. It was relying on the brittleness of the masquarade but constantly re enforced it. It was apparantly 'bad' abut its targets were worse.<br /> <br /> It was an existential tier threat to vampires which they have no real response to but its business as usual in most cities<br /> <br /> You cant write that forever if you want a plot which doesnt revolve the inevitability of your extinction. I mean they had a magic gas which kills vampires but doesnt kill humans. Even if you cant just soak every city in it, thats game over","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-02-2026, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T06:56:31-07:00","id":1562479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562460#post1562460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read some thorough critiques of this V6 alpha playtest from a few people and find myself agreeing with them. This is so full of bad ideas that throwing it all out and starting anew is likely a better idea than trying to fix something with this many issues. A lot of which shouldn't have even made it to the alpha stage in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562466#post1562466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, Monstrous is tied to Clan, and past Monstrous 3 you become a wight, so you are always interacting with Humanity. But this is an alpha, and I might be reading it wrong or not getting something, did have to re-read and you are right about the mindless thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monstrous is tied to Clan + Frenzy + killing + other things the ST wants. More importantly, how you being there influence your character is mostly Clan + being a predator in the broadest sense. Mechanically it's just a few penalties + a few bonuses.<br /> <br /> You don't become a Wight past Monstrous 3. If you go past Monstrous 3, instead you lose access to 1 dot of Humanity (recoverable). Only after you lose all dots of Humanity you'll be at risk of becoming a Wight.<br /> <br /> Humanity is tied to Nature + living with mortals as a normal person, even a shitty one. It has an Outburst, which is basically a Nature-oriented &quot;Frenzy&quot; just as able to push you towards it. If you remember the list of Natures from Legacy, which is what's being used, you can be quite an abhorrent, despicable, psychopathic asshole in accordance to it. Mechanically it's just another set of penalties and bonuses.<br /> <br /> Same mechanics to lose the character, and if you get a dot blocked all you need is to fall to it again. Instead of changing, you unblock the dot and that's it. The scale doesn't cost XP, ever, it just requires clear actions in order to move to any side.<br /> <br /> And the whole thing is made in such a way that you can with relative ease move to any side on purpose, and being at a side actually pushes you slightly to the other, not to fall more. So the system is volatile to both sides with a slight gravitation to center. Also being built with the goal of every position giving balanced benefits and drawbacks (if the balance is right is for the actual tests to say).<br /> <br /> Want to play an old Path? Just chose or make a fitting Nature to represent it. Now moving the scale is a matter of indulging your Beast in the way you prefer or living up to the tenets of your Path. Depending on the Path wouldn't this mean the same action could fulfill both? Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562470#post1562470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it looks like V5 is basically getting the 4E D&amp;D treatment, where most of the changes introduced in that edition are being rolled back in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, though D&amp;D 5th didn't rolled up all of it, just most of it, and has the excellent idea of not using stupid language for what remained. I expect something similar for V6.<br /> <br /> But I don't think keeping V5 mostly canon will be that much gymnastics. I'm with Shadeprowler here.<br /> <br /> V5 has been toning down the SI since the early supplements, to begin with. The bombing of Vienna, as insufferably idiotic as it was, kind of also was their heyday, not their standard.<br /> <br /> And their existence is very high maintenance. It isn't unheard of some institution or internal coalition becoming abnormally powerful within a government, and those frequently lose to the high cost and high friction eventually.<br /> <br /> The SI becoming weaker as context changes and sustaining efforts become untenable is not weird. It's actually the most realistic thing after everything they done for no meaningful return.<br /> <br /> Meaningful return here is important. Really, the SI gets what out of it? Vampires' assets are already publicly in the hands of living people, there's no political or strategic gain, no control of useful resources, technology or intelligence. Vampires are a blip in the statistics of violence, and the way they manipulate society isn't that much different from politicians and rich people doing the same all the time. They're actually killing potential partners for their bosses. And all they get is satisfaction?<br /> <br /> If anything I would quietly tone down their too big to be real feats and let them be there as a loose network of rogue agents. A very soft retcon similar to how Revised repeatedly toned down the Ravnos culling as it became clear that the initial reports of destruction was more than unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:02:53-07:00","id":1562481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562471#post1562471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could go the way what Mithras and de Camden pulled<br /> Simply <i>use</i><i>d and manipulated</i> the Second Inquisition<br /> It would be hilariously easy to get hold on the key pieces on the board and let it simply fade from the mind<br /> Intelligence agencies shown how one on the top can decide the course of actions - just see J. Edgar Hoover<br /> It was a half-assed thing anyway in the eyes of the Governments IF they took it seriusly - old guards out ,new in and in and in few months the whole thing run out of steam and the dust settle<br /> It is believable<br /> Project Stargate ran for ~25 years and...? Today is just a shurg, not many even know it existed, despite it is &quot;common knowledge&quot;<br /> The SI never went public, ran a what? Few years tops with full power? Somwhere I had a time line of it<br /> I don't think it is that unbelievable after the Camarilla restructured itself and cleared out the problems, it shelved it</div> </div> </div> </div>The way SI was described and acted it made a lot of sense to assume outside forces were involved, possibly even vampires. Not that it would be a new development, elders already did that with the first Inquisition giving them tips where to target their undead rivals. I understand the disappointment if one loves SI but it winding down or dissolving is not ridiculous. And you can always have former agents who form a shadowy organization and trying to keep up the good work a'la Society of St. Leopold so that is all good in my book. Granted I have no strong feelings about SI as a person who is not playing V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:51:57-07:00","id":1562488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562479#post1562479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Monstrous is tied to Clan + Frenzy + killing + other things the ST wants. More importantly, how you being there influence your character is mostly Clan + being a predator in the broadest sense. Mechanically it's just a few penalties + a few bonuses.<br /> <br /> You don't become a Wight past Monstrous 3. If you go past Monstrous 3, instead you lose access to 1 dot of Humanity (recoverable). Only after you lose all dots of Humanity you'll be at risk of becoming a Wight.<br /> <br /> Humanity is tied to Nature + living with mortals as a normal person, even a shitty one. It has an Outburst, which is basically a Nature-oriented &quot;Frenzy&quot; just as able to push you towards it. If you remember the list of Natures from Legacy, which is what's being used, you can be quite an abhorrent, despicable, psychopathic asshole in accordance to it. Mechanically it's just another set of penalties and bonuses.<br /> <br /> Same mechanics to lose the character, and if you get a dot blocked all you need is to fall to it again. Instead of changing, you unblock the dot and that's it. The scale doesn't cost XP, ever, it just requires clear actions in order to move to any side.<br /> <br /> And the whole thing is made in such a way that you can with relative ease move to any side on purpose, and being at a side actually pushes you slightly to the other, not to fall more. So the system is volatile to both sides with a slight gravitation to center. Also being built with the goal of every position giving balanced benefits and drawbacks (if the balance is right is for the actual tests to say).<br /> <br /> Want to play an old Path? Just chose or make a fitting Nature to represent it. Now moving the scale is a matter of indulging your Beast in the way you prefer or living up to the tenets of your Path. Depending on the Path wouldn't this mean the same action could fulfill both? Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is not what paths ever where. They are posthuman philosophy and that is the point (yes you could misuse them and make it the path of doing what I was going to anyway, but to me the interesting thing was trying, imperfectly to play something fundamentally not human) . A sabbat vampire would not have humanity (except some neonates, maybe) They have the Paths that totally replace what their humanity was. If you 'just take an appropriate nature' you are on humanity, the philosophy is a sham, and they are just slightly less boing anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T10:24:28-07:00","id":1562493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562463#post1562463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, as much as I don't like many things from the playtest and agree that changes can be made I would not hold my breath for WW to start from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I don't have my hopes up here. There are a few things I think can be kept, but most... Not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562479#post1562479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. When people pointed out something I'd not noticed myself, I even went to check. So my opinion aligns both with people I'd agree and disagree a lot with in regards to V5. In fact the more I've learned and noticed, the less I like the alpha overall. Just things like the HP+BP is now Vitae is gonna cost this edition a lot of sales if they keep it. I've even shown things to friends I know and so far its been near universal rejection (only one felt positive about the alpha).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T11:17:17-07:00","id":1562496,"title":"","content":"So Outstar confirmed that Giovanni overtook the Hecata, The details of the event TBA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T15:14:57-07:00","id":1562507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562496#post1562496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Outstar confirmed that Giovanni overtook the Hecata, The details of the event TBA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats a shame, i'd prefer they just break from the heceta if they're going with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T16:14:07-07:00","id":1562515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562507#post1562507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats a shame, i'd prefer they just break from the heceta if they're going with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't not like the idea of Hecata as a clan and Nagaraja are not even of the same blood so it made even less sense. But V6 seems to be a bit Going Back on our Previous Decisions: The Movie what with the SI being downplayed, Beckoning ending and now this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T01:49:01-07:00","id":1562540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562496#post1562496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Outstar confirmed that Giovanni overtook the Hecata, The details of the event TBA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest explanation for that is that the Giovanni realized what Lazarus and the Harbringers of Skulls were up to, the Hecata had a mini-civil war and kicked them the hell to the curb, and then the Giovanni had the numbers and power to wrest control of their clan back given that they would massive outnumber the remaining Samedi, Nagaraja and Lamia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T02:59:47-07:00","id":1562543,"title":"","content":"To be fair the Hecata was never really a Clan, more like a thrird sect, with members with interest in Death in any shape or form<br /> The Nagaraja for example had nothing to do with the Cappadocians. They were a cult of mortal death-mages known as the Idran and the Idran belonged to the Chakravanti\u2014a ancient magical tradition focused on death, reincarnation, and karma (which later basically evolved into the <i>Euthanatos </i>) and used Settite vitate to become vampires<br /> The Samedi on the other hand are either that or either that, maybe Infitiores, maybe the offspirngs of Troglodytia, maybe the Baron was indeed a Death God (not unheard of in WoD) or they are a Drowned Legcy<br /> The Pisanob? Same<br /> So the Giovanni making moves or even Augustus resurfacing (he was after all not dead in V5, just presumed to be dead) and doing some housecleaning is not that out of the left field","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 08-03-2026, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T06:04:42-07:00","id":1562548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562543#post1562543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair the Hecata was never really a Clan, more like a thrird sect, with members with interest in Death in any shape or form<br /> The Nagaraja for example had nothing to do with the Cappadocians. They were a cult of mortal death-mages known as the Idran and the Idran belonged to the Chakravanti\u2014a ancient magical tradition focused on death, reincarnation, and karma (which later basically evolved into the <i>Euthanatos </i>) and used Settite vitate to become vampires<br /> The Samedi on the other hand are either that or either that, maybe Infitiores, maybe the offspirngs of Troglodytia, maybe the Baron was indeed a Death God (not unheard of in WoD) or they are a Drowned Legcy<br /> The Pisanob? Same<br /> So the Giovanni making moves or even Augustus resurfacing (he was after all not dead in V5, just presumed to be dead) and doing some housecleaning is not that out of the left field</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact they were but the V5 system treats them as a clan. You can see that in the write up of Gretchen Vogt in Courts of the Damned (p. 141). In that we see Clan: Hecata. Not clan Giovanni, not clan Nagaraja or whatever. I agree that treating Hecata as a quasi-sect makes more sense but it's not what V5 is doing. And yes, Nagaraja's presence is the perfect example why making them a clan did not make any sense. So I appreciate you acknowledging the faults of making Hecata a clan but it's indisputable that V5 treats them as a clan. <br /> <br /> Giovanni taking over Hecata is not surprising. After Lasombra joined Camarilla by dropping their clanmates to Camarilla's axe and how Sabbat was nuked from the orbit nothing is unexpected. My only issue is, as much as I am not a fan of Hecata in V5, that it seems that they are trying to undo a questionable decision in V5 by a questionable decision in V6. But as many things in WoD, I am not opposed by the idea, the truth is in the pudding or writing in this case. I have not been against Gangrel exodus from the Camarilla, same as Schismatics joining Camarilla, Brujah leaving and Lasombra joining. Out of the four I feel like only Schismatics development was well written and made sense. YMMV of course. <br /> <br /> I know however that V5 fans are raging against that change so it's kinda funny how Gehenna is cyclical <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T07:09:34-07:00","id":1562550,"title":"","content":"There were rumblings of a new necromantic sect in BJD (the same book to hint the Clan of Death might not be quite so disunited after all), so the Hecata as a sect would make the most sense. However, even then, CotBG said that the Giovanni still referred to themselves by their family name. How many Kindred really know a Samedi anyway? This isn't a change to most vampires; there were Giovanni before and they're still around and going by the same name now. It's entirely possible the Hecata remain as a sect, with or without the Giovanni as members. It's also possible the Harbingers struck against the Giovanni and the latter were forced to severe their new ties to the rest of the &quot;Clan&quot; of Death.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't mind them rolling back V5 metaplot (most of it was super vague anyway), or deciding some of it is no longer canon. A new edition gives you the ability to do that if you want to. However, I don't think they will. I think it'll be more &quot;soft backpedalling&quot; to give people more of the traditional metaplot. A setting where nearly every single famous elder is dead isn't really very fun if you want to refocus on the metaplot and are going to make elder play possible from day one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Slight copy edits 08-03-2026, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T07:26:00-07:00","id":1562551,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd do with the Lasombra: Have a bunch of Sabbat infiltrators inside the Camarilla now. The genuine defectors would panic as they try to figure out which of their clanmates is a traitor, but they'd be unable to risk losing the support of their Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> peers more generally. Meanwhile, the moles would be carefully setting up their assassinations and strategic coups, with some willing to play the (really) long game.<br /> <br /> This would fit the timeline of a resurgent Sabbat, its crusaders glutted on elder vitae, returning to reclaim their turf. Within the Black Hand, I wouldn't have Jalan-Aajav meet his end at the hands of the SI, but if he did, there's always the new <i>hulul</i> (Nizzam al-Latif, per Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand), leading an exultant Assamite <i>antitribu</i>. Failing that, there's also the one and only Dastur Anosh, who's faked his death so many times he could be Fatima at this point and we wouldn't know (not that I'm seriously suggesting that).<br /> <br /> In London, Monty Coven could do as BJD suggested, and set himself up as head of the British Isles. Or, if he's truly dead or set on independence, there's always Lady Astor (<i>Giovanni Chronicles III</i>, <i>Ventrue Chronicle</i>) who's been biding her time. What better time than in the wake of the SI's purge of the Camarilla? Or there's her chief rival, Doctor Streck, the anarchist warlord who somehow manages to disappear every time the actual fighting breaks out. Meanwhile, on the continent, Strohmann, the Nosferatu <i>antitribu</i> who likely smuggled the first Samedi to the Americas on slave ships, has been building his forces in Central Europe.<br /> <br /> Montreal would be fairly straightforward. Per BJD, Ezekiel was infected by Blood Rot, and one possible outcome was that the Sabbat would allow the Camarilla to take over, wait till the Ivory Tower Kindred contracted the disease, and then sweep back in. I wasn't fan of the idea that Metathiax, or at least his monstrous servants, was just a vozhd in V5; that was already a retcon, and a silly one at that. What would happen if the Camarilla were the ones who had to deal with infernalism for a change, though? Maybe some of the fleeing Camarilla forces had already been corrupted before they left. That'd certainly be interesting.<br /> <br /> I'm keen to see how V6 squares the circle. Since V5 was so at odds with prior editions anyway, and was quite happy to completely reimagine things (e.g., the Baali), I don't see why V6 can't be permitted the same leeway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Clarify 08-03-2026, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T07:53:11-07:00","id":1562554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562550#post1562550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were rumblings of a new necromantic sect in BJD (the same book to hint the Clan of Death might not be quite so disunited after all), so the Hecata as a sect would make the most sense. However, even then, CotBG said that the Giovanni still referred to themselves by their family name. How many Kindred really know a Samedi anyway? This isn't a change to most vampires; there were Giovanni before and they're still around and going by the same name now. It's entirely possible the Hecata remain as a sect, with or without the Giovanni as members. It's also possible the Harbingers struck against the Giovanni and the latter were forced to severe their new ties to the rest of the &quot;Clan&quot; of Death.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't mind them rolling back V5 metaplot (most of it was super vague anyway), or deciding some of it is no longer canon. A new edition gives you the ability to do that if you want to. However, I don't think they will. I think it'll be more &quot;soft backpedalling&quot; to give people more of the traditional metaplot. A setting where nearly every single famous elder is dead isn't really very fun if you want to refocus on the metaplot and are going to make elder play possible from day one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although it would be an idea enjoyed by some of the old fans it would cause an uproar of V5 enjoyers so it would not be a sensible decision. And more than that, they have already stated that V5 did nothing wrong and they are going to continue the metaplot of V5 (as anemic as it was). <br /> <br /> The Sabbat development I am curious to see because the way they nuked Sabbat from the orbit in V5 their return as a functional org is not something you can handwave. It needs a lot of explanation so I wonder how they are going to square that circle. <br /> <br /> As you say, the retcons and reimagining are nothing new, they were even done before V5. Just think how Nictuku evolved from bunch of boogeymen Nosferatu to a Bloodline as suggested in Libellus Sanguinis IV to a fully playable Bloodline in DV20. Or how &quot;Black Hand...&quot; based on one of the most controversial books of the gonzo era (DSOTBH) is one of my favourite books for VtM ever. So the potential is there, the question is if they are skilled enough to seize it. Let's hope beyond hope. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T14:18:19-07:00","id":1562579,"title":"","content":"I'm with adambeyoncelowe about the Hecata and I think it is kind of overblown the &quot;they're a clan&quot; take.<br /> <br /> V5 made them mechanically so and it sucks and is stupid, but in lore they're clearly just an alliance. Since the &quot;unification&quot; is explained as magic, not as it being always there, I don't think the Nagaraja being there is that much of a stretch anyway. If you accept that a ritual made them share Disciplines and Weakness in the first place, why's adding the adopted cousing any more weird?<br /> <br /> And the Giovanni being &quot;back&quot; may be just that: the book will present the Hecata as a sect and the Giovanni as a clan.<br /> <br /> Though I'd go wild and use the Cappadocians instead, formalizing the return of the Lost Clans. It's not as if that would really change anything important.<br /> <br /> My actual question then drifts to: what will they make out of the Bloodlines? Will we see their full return?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T15:10:02-07:00","id":1562582,"title":"","content":"I really would like the cappadocians back. They're my favourate clan by a mile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T15:13:38-07:00","id":1562584,"title":"","content":"If you ask me then no, I do not accept it's magic. This is one of the reasons why I dislike the whole Family Reunion thing. It's clearly done for the sake of mechanics and makes little sense in-world. If it was just a gathering of fellow necromancer vampires or a new sect I could swallow it hook line and sinker. But it being a magic ritual seems to be a handwave to explain why it does not make sense. It's magic so we do not have to explain it. <br /> <br /> Nagaraja being included is not a big deal in itself, it's just another thing that makes the whole thing unbelievable. If it is Family Reunion then Nagaraja are out of place because they are not cousins, unlike Lamia, Samedi or Giovanni they never had any connection in previous editions to Cappadocians other than their interest fascination with death.<br /> <br /> As for the Bloodlines: well, no idea. They did not hint at it but anything is possible. It would go against their streamlining tendencies but it's not as if they were super consistent in this area earlier and in the playtest. New splats are easy way to sell books so that would point towards their future inclusion. On the other hand Bloodlines with no unique Disciplines might defeat the purpose but maybe they can handle that trough bloodline traits? It is an interesting question: What will they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T16:12:31-07:00","id":1562590,"title":"","content":"The SI works as an idea but the execution seemed really conflicted.<br /> <br /> They knew about vampires but didn't tell anyone. They had mass surveillance and the vampires didn't but they didn't autowin, except when they did. The masquerade was broken but also not. They were beyond an existential threat to kindred society but also just mooks in swat gear for pcs to kick their butts. <br /> <br /> If you toned down the discrepancies there is lots of useful stuff you could do with them.<br /> <br /> Massive alterations to clans run into the issue all of them have fans that wants to keep playing them. See gangrel leaving the camarilla being pointed out in near every owod sourcebook and it being ignored by everyone I've ever played with. Ravnos to. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T16:23:13-07:00","id":1562592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562479#post1562479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have you read it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Monstrous is tied to Clan + Frenzy + killing + other things the ST wants. More importantly, how you being there influence your character is mostly Clan + being a predator in the broadest sense. Mechanically it's just a few penalties + a few bonuses.<br /> <br /> You don't become a Wight past Monstrous 3. If you go past Monstrous 3, instead you lose access to 1 dot of Humanity (recoverable). Only after you lose all dots of Humanity you'll be at risk of becoming a Wight.<br /> <br /> Humanity is tied to Nature + living with mortals as a normal person, even a shitty one. It has an Outburst, which is basically a Nature-oriented &quot;Frenzy&quot; just as able to push you towards it. If you remember the list of Natures from Legacy, which is what's being used, you can be quite an abhorrent, despicable, psychopathic asshole in accordance to it. Mechanically it's just another set of penalties and bonuses.<br /> <br /> Same mechanics to lose the character, and if you get a dot blocked all you need is to fall to it again. Instead of changing, you unblock the dot and that's it. The scale doesn't cost XP, ever, it just requires clear actions in order to move to any side.<br /> <br /> And the whole thing is made in such a way that you can with relative ease move to any side on purpose, and being at a side actually pushes you slightly to the other, not to fall more. So the system is volatile to both sides with a slight gravitation to center. Also being built with the goal of every position giving balanced benefits and drawbacks (if the balance is right is for the actual tests to say).<br /> <br /> Want to play an old Path? Just chose or make a fitting Nature to represent it. Now moving the scale is a matter of indulging your Beast in the way you prefer or living up to the tenets of your Path. Depending on the Path wouldn't this mean the same action could fulfill both? Yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> That is not what paths ever where. They are posthuman philosophy and that is the point (yes you could misuse them and make it the path of doing what I was going to anyway, but to me the interesting thing was trying, imperfectly to play something fundamentally not human) . A sabbat vampire would not have humanity (except some neonates, maybe) They have the Paths that totally replace what their humanity was. The 'Humanity Frenzy' makes It worse.<br /> <br /> It maybe my kind of neuro spicy but don't pretend the same set of rules with the same terms are something different by choosing a nature that a human of humane vamp could take.<br /> <br /> Rules are the skeleton the story hangs on, lore is the squishy bits, if you are missing the rules the lore flops about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T16:24:25-07:00","id":1562593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562590#post1562590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI works as an idea but the execution seemed really conflicted.<br /> <br /> They knew about vampires but didn't tell anyone. They had mass surveillance and the vampires didn't but they didn't autowin, except when they did. The masquerade was broken but also not. They were beyond an existential threat to kindred society but also just mooks in swat gear for pcs to kick their butts.<br /> <br /> If you toned down the discrepancies there is lots of useful stuff you could do with them.<br /> <br /> Massive alterations to clans run into the issue all of them have fans that wants to keep playing them. See gangrel leaving the camarilla being pointed out in near every owod sourcebook and it being ignored by everyone I've ever played with. Ravnos to.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there's this thing in Werewolf where there are a lot of enemies to face, but how some of them work at cross-purposes. If you're going heavily into the Technocracy influence angle, the same underlying faction that is funneling all this support to uncovering vampires is also pushing forward LLM slop that promotes a post-truth, ruined information society where no one believes anything on the main information display because it's &quot;obviously fake.&quot; This proceeds to corrupt the information in the mass surveillance system that was worrying vampires, and ends up having the techno-people biting themselves in the ass, not unlike any two given Wyrm factions in W:tA jockeying for position, one-upping each other, engaging in mutual sabotage, and ruining their own efforts long enough for Garou to regroup, possibly even make a truce with Fera, and stick it to the corrupter's minions in both of these factions. The heads of the hydra are often busy snapping at each other, and this helps to make victory possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:29:02-07:00","id":1562600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562590#post1562590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SI works as an idea but the execution seemed really conflicted.<br /> <br /> They knew about vampires but didn't tell anyone. They had mass surveillance and the vampires didn't but they didn't autowin, except when they did. The masquerade was broken but also not. They were beyond an existential threat to kindred society but also just mooks in swat gear for pcs to kick their butts.<br /> <br /> If you toned down the discrepancies there is lots of useful stuff you could do with them.<br /> <br /> Massive alterations to clans run into the issue all of them have fans that wants to keep playing them. See gangrel leaving the camarilla being pointed out in near every owod sourcebook and it being ignored by everyone I've ever played with. Ravnos to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gangrel exodus was bad writing trying to fix other bad writing. <br /> <br /> Gangrel were one of the seven founding clans of the Camarilla since the first VtM corebook. Some might be autarkis, some a bit anarch but most are Camarilla. It did not make much sense that clan made of of vagabonds, travellers and lone wolfs would in majority be involved in the biggest vampiric society in the world. So in this respect the exodus was a decent idea. But Revised went from one extreme to another and now most of Camarilla Gangrel were leaving because Xavier got his ass handed to him by Hazimel and he thought he was an Antediluvian. It was a decent idea to get most Gangrels outside Camarilla in theory but in-game it did not make sense that clan made out of individualists packs the bags and leaves just because Justicar of their clan said so. I understand impressionable youths and even some elders but many Gangrels had positions in the Camarilla so they would not necessarily be open to a &quot;Camarilla, they don't care about us&quot; spiel.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is that as controversial as Gangrel departing the Camarilla was in Revised Paradox decided to do the same thing with Brujah in V5. But guess they needed to make anarchs interesting and show how badass they are. And now with Gangrel, Brujah, Setites and Tzimisce the sect was interesting (except not really, anarchs are still Camarilla lite in V5 with no strong hooks). <br /> <br /> And Ravnos... well, they were victims of ToJ, blood for the Blood God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T18:08:20-07:00","id":1562602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562584#post1562584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ask me then no, I do not accept it's magic. This is one of the reasons why I dislike the whole Family Reunion thing. It's clearly done for the sake of mechanics and makes little sense in-world. If it was just a gathering of fellow necromancer vampires or a new sect I could swallow it hook line and sinker. But it being a magic ritual seems to be a handwave to explain why it does not make sense. It's magic so we do not have to explain it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where I say you're too attached to the rules.<br /> <br /> In the Family Reunion the main goal achieved is the gathering of fellow necromancers and the sect they formed. Family like in the same way the Mafia is family like.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the OoC reason it happened, in the lore the ritual was secondary, and even if kept it could have whatever other effect you want, maybe even being just a formal ceremony to seal the deal.<br /> <br /> You don't like the magic? Throw it away and you're left with a perfectly serviceable new sect without changing anything else about the whole deal.<br /> <br /> And the name is just a name. It makes perfect sense for the Giovanni to call such an event the Family Reunion: they're mostly Cappadocians and family references is the Giovanni thing. It would also make sense to accept the Nagaraja because that's just a name and you don't turn your back on a useful ally just because they don't fit the theme of your party.<br /> <br /> What I do is exactly this. I keep the Family Reunion wholesale, ignore the clan unification and there's no kink to hammer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562590#post1562590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See gangrel leaving the camarilla being pointed out in near every owod sourcebook and it being ignored by everyone I've ever played with. Ravnos to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those two were ignored by the authors themselves.<br /> <br /> You're never told about where those Gangrel were or what they were doing, they're simply nonexistent after departing, and every city still has Gangrel as usual, the books themselves saying if you make a Gangrel, you're probably one of those who remained.<br /> <br /> Literally everything kept runing business as usual for Gangrel presence except they didn't had a Justicar anymore.<br /> <br /> Each book also reduced the impact on the Ravnos. They're almost wiped, then they're very reduced, then they took a heavy hit, then it was kind of a big deal, then most survived but have the scars or what happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562592#post1562592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not what paths ever where.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It maybe my kind of neuro spicy but don't pretend the same set of rules with the same terms are something different by choosing a nature that a human of humane vamp could take.<br /> <br /> Rules are the skeleton the story hangs on, lore is the squishy bits, if you are missing the rules the lore flops about.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that exactly what Paths were: the transhumanist philosophy you take to replace your Humanity. Make your chosen Path into a Nature and you literally replaced your human side with the Path.<br /> <br /> Second, Nature = human is just a convention. You can interpret then in inhuman ways for whatever definition of inhuman you want.<br /> <br /> Third, those are not the same set of rules, that's the whole point. Not that you're not using the same Humanity Scale, but that this is not old Humanity. This rule is altogether distinct from what the old Camarilla would call Humanity. A character following a Nature that represents a transhumanist philosophy is doing exactly the same thing the old Paths did.<br /> <br /> And fourth, rules are tools. They're dramatic systems that the story interprets. They totally must be appropriate for whatever they'll represent, but you shouldn't put too much stock on them as ontological statements about the story.<br /> <br /> My suggestion wasn't just to get appropriate Natures. Turn a Path into a Nature. That's not hard at all, just use the old description of its ethics. That won't be a &quot;Nature a human could follow&quot;, it would literally be the Path. Done. A few Paths may still have some kinks, but very minor and easy to hammer down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T01:51:16-07:00","id":1562618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562602#post1562602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's where I say you're too attached to the rules.<br /> <br /> In the Family Reunion the main goal achieved is the gathering of fellow necromancers and the sect they formed. Family like in the same way the Mafia is family like.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the OoC reason it happened, in the lore the ritual was secondary, and even if kept it could have whatever other effect you want, maybe even being just a formal ceremony to seal the deal.<br /> <br /> You don't like the magic? Throw it away and you're left with a perfectly serviceable new sect without changing anything else about the whole deal.<br /> <br /> And the name is just a name. It makes perfect sense for the Giovanni to call such an event the Family Reunion: they're mostly Cappadocians and family references is the Giovanni thing. It would also make sense to accept the Nagaraja because that's just a name and you don't turn your back on a useful ally just because they don't fit the theme of your party.<br /> <br /> What I do is exactly this. I keep the Family Reunion wholesale, ignore the clan unification and there's no kink to hammer.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of the golden rule, thank you. That is beside the point which is criticism towards the Family Reunion. Just because I can ignore a metaplot/rule change does not make the change any better.<br /> <br /> The bottom line is this, anything can be changed in a RPG setting or it's mechanics. The thing with V5 is, at least for me, there are too many things I have to change or ignore that using the system or the setting is not worth it. Sabbat, Lasombra deal with Camarilla, Family Reunion, Beckoning, Disciplines being smashed together, no rules for elder vampires - it's just too many things that I have to ignore, change or create from scratch to make it work. If I like something I can poach it for games I am playing in the older editions. Like my mate is doing now in a game of VtDA he is running. He bought a lot of V5 books and he liked Tzimisce being fantasy dragons and Salubri having addictive blood so that's what is happening in his game. <br /> <br /> And sure, if Hecata was an alliance of convenience I still would not care for it personally but I would have no substantive criticism against it other than - I don't vibe with it. Like I said many times - V5 is dragged down by ideas that my be interesting on paper but they suffer from poor execution. And Hecata is a perfect example of that. YMMV. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T02:24:49-07:00","id":1562619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562602#post1562602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> First, that exactly what Paths were: the transhumanist philosophy you take to replace your Humanity. Make your chosen Path into a Nature and you literally replaced your human side with the Path.<br /> <br /> Second, Nature = human is just a convention. You can interpret then in inhuman ways for whatever definition of inhuman you want.<br /> <br /> Third, those are not the same set of rules, that's the whole point. Not that you're not using the same Humanity Scale, but that this is not old Humanity. This rule is altogether distinct from what the old Camarilla would call Humanity. A character following a Nature that represents a transhumanist philosophy is doing exactly the same thing the old Paths did.<br /> <br /> And fourth, rules are tools. They're dramatic systems that the story interprets. They totally must be appropriate for whatever they'll represent, but you shouldn't put too much stock on them as ontological statements about the story.<br /> <br /> My suggestion wasn't just to get appropriate Natures. Turn a Path into a Nature. That's not hard at all, just use the old description of its ethics. That won't be a &quot;Nature a human could follow&quot;, it would literally be the Path. Done. A few Paths may still have some kinks, but very minor and easy to hammer down.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that does not compute as a way of looking at it for me. Like at all, that would just be 'humanity but weird' Not the completely different way of looking at the world and a different way of dealing with frenzy, with all the culture and ideology that went with that. I am not claiming it's invalid, I am claiming it doesn't work at all to make me able to use it for verisimilitude. If you can, go have at an good luck, it literally is antithetical to how rules feel to me, to me they ARE the simulation of the world, as integral to it as the lore, when Lore and rules disagree, I have mental work to do to make it fit for me. Again this is not a value judgement it's explaining how I function (or honestly dysfunction sometimes), (this btw is why you may have seen me argue dice roles as accessibility tools if I am trying to be a charismatic character let me set out a framework and roll for it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 08-04-2026, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T05:31:36-07:00","id":1562629,"title":"","content":"Can't say I'd refer to sabbat philosophy as transhuman given that's an actual real life philosophy that's part of the humanism branch. I'd borrow a term from Eclipse Phase instead and call them exhuman philosophies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T06:21:44-07:00","id":1562631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562618#post1562618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Hecata is a perfect example of that. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think they're the worse example, not the better, because they're actually the opposite: the idea is horrible, but the execution made for a usable plot.<br /> <br /> More importantly I find it weird to want to get rid of this plot entirely rather than just the bad original reason. That's why I don't care about the Hecata still being a thing: for me it has no relation with the problem, not in a new edition.<br /> <br /> Put bluntly: I want them to undo the uniformity of death lines. I don't want them to undo the Family Reunion plot. I'm not talking about V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562619#post1562619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that does not compute as a way of looking at it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get it. I'm autistic and an activist for the cause so I know hundreds of variations of this. Mine unfortunately makes me want to make things as stupidly clear as possible, being misunderstood is really a problem for me, and I do get passionate (partly also because of my own neuro-spice).<br /> <br /> And while I can get behind not liking the rule, I completely disagree with &quot;that would just be 'humanity but weird' Not the completely different way of looking at the world and a different way of dealing with frenzy, with all the culture and ideology that went with that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Old Paths were exactly the same thing: they're mechanically Humanity, but with a different set of sins slapped on. Everything else is lore and interpretation. Even the alternate Virtues: not only are there plenty Paths that don't use them, Conscience and Conviction are mechanically identical, and Instinct is so conceptually close to Self-Control that even VDA 20 gave up on gatekeeping Riding the Wave behind it, making Instinct from worse than Self-Control to worse Self-Control.<br /> <br /> What I'm proposing is to transpose those same lore and interpretations fully to Humanity Scale using the literal Paths as a special set of Natures with the same in-lore requirements as they had before.<br /> <br /> Don't work for you? That's ok. But not the weird outlook with the culture and ideology that comes with it? Bullshit. It literally is. Not the transhumanist philosophy? Bullshit. Since their first iteration the philosophy is the requirement to follow and explanation for why the rolls are made when they're made.<br /> <br /> From a lore standpoint it's exactly what Paths were. I can concede it's not what they were for rules and maybe not the absolutely best translation, but partly that's because the role they had in rules doesn't exist within Humanity Scale: it's just as much not what Humanity ever was, so much so that it accommodates Paths' philosophies without leading you to Wightdom, so what they were \u2013 ways to have a monstrous vampire without Losing dots in the morality meter and becoming a Wight \u2013 isn't a thing.<br /> <br /> More importantly your original point \u2013 bringing their Sabbat back \u2013 is already perfectly feasible without need for new Path rules, even if it can be better done with new Path rules. I'm not saying at any point that they shouldn't make them, just that Humanity Scale works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T06:26:36-07:00","id":1562633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562629#post1562629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I'd refer to sabbat philosophy as transhuman given that's an actual real life philosophy that's part of the humanism branch. I'd borrow a term from Eclipse Phase instead and call them exhuman philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call them anything because the best fits in the strict sense depend on the Path, they have no common philosophical reference even if in the Sabbat most have a common goal of &quot;inhuman liberation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't fixate on the &quot;inhumanity&quot;, either from both actual philosophy and psychology they're all perfectly human as moral systems, things only a human would think about, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T07:14:29-07:00","id":1562638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562618#post1562618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lasombra deal with Camarilla,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's really easy to downplay. The largest chunk of the lasombra was still sabbat, a lot of lasombra would have died on the way over and their position is so weak they're roughly 9th in line for embracing rights at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T08:29:34-07:00","id":1562645,"title":"","content":"It looks like in the V6 Vitae and Healt are merged, and the only way to heal wounds is to feed on mortals.<br /> This puzzles me a lot since it implies your character might walk aroud with a hole on his head or chest until he drinks some blood.<br /> This is not a breach into the Masquerade? Don't you think it's really odd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 08-04-2026, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T08:33:23-07:00","id":1562646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562645#post1562645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like in the V6 Vitae and Healt are merged, and the only way to heal wounds is to feed on mortals.<br /> This puzzles me a lot since it implies your character might walk aroud with a hole on his head or chest until he drinks some blood.<br /> However, this is not a breach into the Mascquerade? Don't you think it's really odd?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah it has a LOT of problems like that. Ranging from what you brought up to silly things like Fortitude now hurting you to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:53:46-07:00","id":1562664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562629#post1562629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say I'd refer to sabbat philosophy as transhuman given that's an actual real life philosophy that's part of the humanism branch. I'd borrow a term from Eclipse Phase instead and call them exhuman philosophies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to remember to call them posthuman, which, yea same place. Could totally see a Tzimisce becoming one of those weird multi morph ego choir hunting packs for instance, or the ones that absorb every ego they can into a gestalt entity then prune it to purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562645#post1562645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like in the V6 Vitae and Healt are merged, and the only way to heal wounds is to feed on mortals.<br /> This puzzles me a lot since it implies your character might walk aroud with a hole on his head or chest until he drinks some blood.<br /> This is not a breach into the Masquerade? Don't you think it's really odd?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't like the scheme either, but I think what it is trying to do is turn healing via vitae from a process into an automatic assumption, so no, the hole healed but you are less animated as your vitae diminishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 08-04-2026, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T11:39:20-07:00","id":1562671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562638#post1562638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really easy to downplay. The largest chunk of the lasombra was still sabbat, a lot of lasombra would have died on the way over and their position is so weak they're roughly 9th in line for embracing rights at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree strongly here.<br /> <br /> The size of their population here or there is irrelevant, do as thy will.<br /> <br /> But the deal is the opposite of the Hecata: they wanted an ok goal (enough Lasombra in the Cam to make them playable, also formalize their small project of having 4 clans in each sect) that's also easy to ignore, as you stated, but to do that they added a infuriatingly badly thought, nonsensical and disruptive plot that makes any by-the-lore game have to deal with the Lasombra being complete idiots who in the Cam are now under unnecessarily harsh conditions for no gain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562645#post1562645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like in the V6 Vitae and Healt are merged, and the only way to heal wounds is to feed on mortals.<br /> This puzzles me a lot since it implies your character might walk aroud with a hole on his head or chest until he drinks some blood.<br /> This is not a breach into the Masquerade? Don't you think it's really odd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you assume a direct visual relationship.<br /> <br /> Think of it like you constantly healing damage rather than only healing when you feed, like Taggie said. Every wound that's not losing a limb gets healed in seconds, so that's what Vitae represents. And you go into torpor if you lose the last drop because Blood is, after all, what animates you.<br /> <br /> But this is just an early Playtests anyway, so don't think too hard about it now. It doesn't have the actual explanations yet and most mechanics will probably change a lot until it is actually released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T12:19:58-07:00","id":1562677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Sorry for some reason quoting isn't working for me. Anyway, you are right, this new system also does Humanity in a weird way, I care a lot less because that isn't what I play VTM for, but the hierarchies did serve a purpose in story, and actually could be used as decent markers and a guide to what a Vamp at each level was roughly like. The Natures without a lot of work don't do that, and I can't see how they would ever do that, with monstrosity being a clan influenced factor, not a personal morality factor, if they took over how monstrosity manifested via a beast nature, and for a path you could take both the same, just expressing differently (Path of the Beast having a monstrosity that was an immediate prey seeking and a path out burst that was stalking a cainite to prepare traps etc) . but as you rightly say, this is an Alpha, and that idea is not satisfying, but it is me trying to save something. Oh and the type of spice: no idea, been on the waiting list for a proper diagnosis for years, but adult support is a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T12:20:41-07:00","id":1562678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562671#post1562671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree strongly here.<br /> <br /> The size of their population here or there is irrelevant, do as thy will.<br /> <br /> But the deal is the opposite of the Hecata: they wanted an ok goal (enough Lasombra in the Cam to make them playable, also formalize their small project of having 4 clans in each sect) that's also easy to ignore, as you stated, but to do that they added a infuriatingly badly thought, nonsensical and disruptive plot that makes any by-the-lore game have to deal with the Lasombra being complete idiots who in the Cam are now under unnecessarily harsh conditions for no gain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Only if you assume a direct visual relationship.<br /> <br /> Think of it like you constantly healing damage rather than only healing when you feed, like Taggie said. Every wound that's not losing a limb gets healed in seconds, so that's what Vitae represents. And you go into torpor if you lose the last drop because Blood is, after all, what animates you.<br /> <br /> But this is just an early Playtests anyway, so don't think too hard about it now. It doesn't have the actual explanations yet and most mechanics will probably change a lot until it is actually released.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If that's the case, they should explain it better!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 08-04-2026, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T12:34:40-07:00","id":1562679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562678#post1562678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If that's the case, they should explain it better!</div> </div> </div> </div>Alpha document, so as much as it pains me, the systems are more like ideas than actual finished systems right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T13:45:30-07:00","id":1562686,"title":"","content":"I hate this response and it's coming back time and time again so I will repeat myself again, I am aware of the golden rule and I know I can change anything or ignore anything. It is similar to &quot;if you don't want to don't use it&quot; which is handwaving criticism instead of engaging with it. Nothing personal but I get this response so often that it's a bit annoying. <br /> <br /> And tho we often clash with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> we are in full agreement about the Lasombra plot. Bringing Lasombra to Camarilla was as good idea as making Gangrel and Brujah anarch, the problem lies in the atrocious writing that was used to justifyi it where Lasombra, cunning manipulators killed and sacrificed their clanmates to become second class citizens in Camarilla. Cue Bruce Wayne saying: It's just raises too many questions. <br /> <br /> And as I said elsewhere - there are too many things in V5 I have to downplay, ignore or change for me to use it. I will take it apart for scraps because there are still interesting ideas here and there. I am sure there will be those in V6 as well as much as I am doompilled about the changes in the playtest atm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T14:16:46-07:00","id":1562691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562677#post1562677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Sorry for some reason quoting isn't working for me. Anyway, you are right, this new system also does Humanity in a weird way, I care a lot less because that isn't what I play VTM for, but the hierarchies did serve a purpose in story, and actually could be used as decent markers and a guide to what a Vamp at each level was roughly like. The Natures without a lot of work don't do that, and I can't see how they would ever do that, with monstrosity being a clan influenced factor, not a personal morality factor, if they took over how monstrosity manifested via a beast nature, and for a path you could take both the same, just expressing differently (Path of the Beast having a monstrosity that was an immediate prey seeking and a path out burst that was stalking a cainite to prepare traps etc) . but as you rightly say, this is an Alpha, and that idea is not satisfying, but it is me trying to save something. Oh and the type of spice: no idea, been on the waiting list for a proper diagnosis for years, but adult support is a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that, within this Humanity Scale thing, having a Beast that's chosen like Nature is would be ideal. We could then have Natures and Beasts that most Vampires get, and Paths be special Beast and Nature options.<br /> <br /> And I'm still unsure about this whole thing. I mean, it's better than V5 Humanity, which is basically you falling all the time for the same things. With the Hierarchy of Sins you can have a good idea of where you as a player want to be and interpret the character accordingly. This new Scale is something else entirely. Good? I don't know. But will not play as VtM.<br /> <br /> My personal opinion is that if it remains, I'll effectively treat V6 as another game as VtR is. I may come to like it, but when I want to play VtM it will be V20.<br /> <br /> On support for adults, yeah. I was almost 30 when I got my diagnosis of autism, the whole process was a nightmare. Thankfully at the end my health plan (similar to a health insurance, but way easier to use by force of law) covered the diagnosis. It would otherwise have cost something close to $ 1000, and that's because it was cheap. Usually it's more, up to $ 3000. And remember, that's because healthcare in Brazil is way cheaper than in the US.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562678#post1562678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, they should explain it better!</div> </div> </div> </div>What Taggie said.<br /> <br /> This is a Playtest. It's not a product, not V6 and not a preview, it's a &quot;throw everything at the wall, let people try and say what they think, then back to the lab&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a part of development we don't usually see and they're inviting the community to participate, but putting it bluntly: this is not a game, it's work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562686#post1562686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate this response and it's coming back time and time again so I will repeat myself again, I am aware of the golden rule and I know I can change anything or ignore anything. It is similar to &quot;if you don't want to don't use it&quot; which is handwaving criticism instead of engaging with it. Nothing personal but I get this response so often that it's a bit annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't meant that, I'm also repeating myself because I'm trying to be clearer:<br /> <br /> You are right to not wanting to play V5, I am aware this is the tip of the iceberg of V5 problems and I'm not at all talking about V5.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is V6, and that wanting V6 to get rid of the Family Reunion doesn't make a lot of sense because, for V6, those are unrelated problems.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of the trait unification and keep the Family Reunion plot. That's my preferred outcome.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of both. I don't want that, but can accept.<br /> <br /> They can keep both. That's really bad.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of the Family Reunion and still have all death lineages with the same traits. That's worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> None of those have shit to do with golden rule because I'm not talking about how you run your game, I was commenting on wanting the plot out of V6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T15:00:15-07:00","id":1562693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562551#post1562551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'd do with the Lasombra: Have a bunch of Sabbat infiltrators inside the Camarilla now.</div> </div> </div> </div>This hadn't occurred to me, but now that you've got me thinking on it, I love the idea of the Amici Noctis moving heaven and hell to find safe harbor within the Ivory Tower in the hopes of draft-dodging their way out of a suicidal Gehenna War - only to see their elders come back from that war, flexing Dominate and Vaulderie bonds. The inability to know who to trust would be palpable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T15:10:56-07:00","id":1562694,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t have any questions, but I\u2019m really looking forward to 6th edition and I like the idea of the Salubri finally being recognized as the fourteenth clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T15:38:45-07:00","id":1562695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562671#post1562671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree strongly here.<br /> <br /> The size of their population here or there is irrelevant, do as thy will.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're very relavant. Clans numbers to a degree, reflect practical power. They're not the only factor but if you're outnumbered 5 to 1 against the ventrue hypothetically then you're on a major backfoot and may not even be present a lot of the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T15:56:37-07:00","id":1562698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562695#post1562695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they're very relavant. Clans numbers to a degree, reflect practical power. They're not the only factor but if you're outnumbered 5 to 1 against the ventrue hypothetically then you're on a major backfoot and may not even be present a lot of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point, if not agree, but we have different approaches to clans so apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> But my main point is that, especially with the almost nonexistent plot development of V5, it's something you can mess with at will without much of a problem to conciliate with lore. It's also less revolting.<br /> <br /> Literally they could just say the Camarilla side outpaced the Sabbat after years of Embraces and no one paid enough attention to notice before.<br /> <br /> And seriously, I'd get rid of the whole clan/sect tie as a named thing. Better than force a balance of 4/sect excluding the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Heck, just say the Lasombra are more common among Cam than Anarchs and Independents, since that was the actual point and the Sabbat would be canonically out of the picture anyway.<br /> <br /> Every option works since there's zero official plot that relies on the Lasombra being so much more numerous in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> They didn't even got a Justicar, those are still the same seven clans as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T16:47:22-07:00","id":1562703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562691#post1562691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't meant that, I'm also repeating myself because I'm trying to be clearer:<br /> <br /> You are right to not wanting to play V5, I am aware this is the tip of the iceberg of V5 problems and I'm not at all talking about V5.<br /> <br /> What I'm talking about is V6, and that wanting V6 to get rid of the Family Reunion doesn't make a lot of sense because, for V6, those are unrelated problems.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of the trait unification and keep the Family Reunion plot. That's my preferred outcome.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of both. I don't want that, but can accept.<br /> <br /> They can keep both. That's really bad.<br /> <br /> They can get rid of the Family Reunion and still have all death lineages with the same traits. That's worst case scenario.<br /> <br /> None of those have shit to do with golden rule because I'm not talking about how you run your game, I was commenting on wanting the plot out of V6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh damn, sorry for misunderstanding, I missed quoting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> but since I @'d you it looked as if I was responding to you in the first paragraph. My bad. <br /> <br /> As far as the metaplot changes in V6 it's hard to assess what is the reasoning for them, whether it's player's feedback or someone on the team hating Hecata or just a natural development. As far as we know at this point all the options you outlined are possible so we will see what's what in due time. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T17:02:18-07:00","id":1562704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562698#post1562698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Lasombra) They didn't even got a Justicar, those are still the same seven clans as always.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not exactly true. Because V5 is back to VtM's mysterious and enigmatic past we do not know who is Justicar at present. <br /> <br /> Lucinde is said to be Justicar for unlife... and possibly Juliet Parr is Malkavian Justicar. The rest is just rumors. Some say that Lucinde is the only remaining Justicar, some say that a Justicar to represent smaller bloodlines and antitribu was or will be chosen soon, some say that Tegyrius is Banu Haqim Justicar. The last Gangrel Justicar is rumored to either disappear to join the Gehenna War or join anarchs as a spy for Camarilla. Oh, one of the rumors says that Tremere got two Justicars. <br /> <br /> In other words, nothing concrete. There might be no Justicars, 7 or any other number of them. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T21:50:58-07:00","id":1562711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562704#post1562704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is not exactly true. Because V5 is back to VtM's mysterious and enigmatic past we do not know who is Justicar at present.<br /> <br /> Lucinde is said to be Justicar for unlife... and possibly Juliet Parr is Malkavian Justicar. The rest is just rumors. Some say that Lucinde is the only remaining Justicar, some say that a Justicar to represent smaller bloodlines and antitribu was or will be chosen soon, some say that Tegyrius is Banu Haqim Justicar. The last Gangrel Justicar is rumored to either disappear to join the Gehenna War or join anarchs as a spy for Camarilla. Oh, one of the rumors says that Tremere got two Justicars.<br /> <br /> In other words, nothing concrete. There might be no Justicars, 7 or any other number of them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To a friend I described the difference between WOD and Chronicles was basically the latter was a toolbox while the former was a defined setting.<br /> <br /> I STRONGLY prefer the defined setting.<br /> <br /> I think Paradox hates defining it so they leave it as undefined and generic as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T01:47:41-07:00","id":1562720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562711#post1562711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To a friend I described the difference between WOD and Chronicles was basically the latter was a toolbox while the former was a defined setting.<br /> <br /> I STRONGLY prefer the defined setting.<br /> <br /> I think Paradox hates defining it so they leave it as undefined and generic as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, you can see that a lot in the generic approach to the world and many aspects that are just &quot;whatever you feel like&quot;. Like how every Chronicle outside of Fall of London is happening in non descript or made up place. <br /> <br /> Though, to be fair to Paradox, as much as Courts of the Damned does not say much concrete words about current Justicars they have write ups on couple of movers and shakers of V5 for both Camarilla and Anarchs. Not only that but they also have full stats for peeps like Victoria Ash, Agata Starek or Hesha Ruhadze. <br /> <br /> And I am with you on defining the setting. If I have prewritten NPCs, metaplots or cities I can use them or disregard them in whatever degree I feel like. Whereas if there is nothing feeling out those blank spaces I always need to fill in the blanks whether I want to or not. But Paradox prefers those things to be vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T05:53:54-07:00","id":1562767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562711#post1562711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Paradox hates defining it so they leave it as undefined and generic as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>which is self defeating when you're relying on brand to sell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T07:06:55-07:00","id":1562771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562767#post1562767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> which is self defeating when you're relying on brand to sell.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. I just saw someone pointing out how it's a missed opportunity that we did not get anything like Lore of the Clans in V5 that would give clans some spice, present different factions or history and legends. And everytime I was trying to come up with some examples of V5 doing flavour and lore I would be running into Onyx Path. Chicago by Night, Cults of the Blood Gods, Forbidden Religions... I guess it would be unfair because there was also Fall of London and all the metaplot included in Camarilla and Anarchs books but I think it's fair to say that the rich lore of VtM has been woefully underutilized in V5. So cheers to V6 that is going to write &quot;a love letter&quot; to that rich lore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T15:09:50-07:00","id":1562796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562771#post1562771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes. I just saw someone pointing out how it's a missed opportunity that we did not get anything like Lore of the Clans in V5 that would give clans some spice, present different factions or history and legends. And everytime I was trying to come up with some examples of V5 doing flavour and lore I would be running into Onyx Path. Chicago by Night, Cults of the Blood Gods, Forbidden Religions... I guess it would be unfair because there was also Fall of London and all the metaplot included in Camarilla and Anarchs books but I think it's fair to say that the rich lore of VtM has been woefully underutilized in V5. So cheers to V6 that is going to write &quot;a love letter&quot; to that rich lore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A GAMES INFORMER journalist once interviewed the head of Ubisoft and kept annoying the hell out of him because he was asking about two things:<br /> <br /> 1. What do you have planned for the modern day story of Assassins Creed<br /> 2. What do you have planned for the stealth gameplay<br /> <br /> The problem being that the interviewer THOUGHT he was giving soft ball questions. In fact, he had really pissed off the guy because the answers were:<br /> <br /> 1. Nothing. We want to focus exclusively on the history bits.<br /> 2. Nothing. We're switching to level based RPG combat.<br /> <br /> Which is essentially how it comes off with Paradox. They wanted to make a system for generic vampire Elders, Ancilla, and Hunters but not actually detail the elaborate backstories of, say, Felicity Price or Victoria Ash.<br /> <br /> They were going all in on system and toolkit versus lore.<br /> <br /> Which is problematic when a huge chunk of the fandom is lore junkies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T07:40:14-07:00","id":1562830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562796#post1562796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A GAMES INFORMER journalist once interviewed the head of Ubisoft and kept annoying the hell out of him because he was asking about two things:<br /> <br /> 1. What do you have planned for the modern day story of Assassins Creed<br /> 2. What do you have planned for the stealth gameplay<br /> <br /> The problem being that the interviewer THOUGHT he was giving soft ball questions. In fact, he had really pissed off the guy because the answers were:<br /> <br /> 1. Nothing. We want to focus exclusively on the history bits.<br /> 2. Nothing. We're switching to level based RPG combat.<br /> <br /> Which is essentially how it comes off with Paradox. They wanted to make a system for generic vampire Elders, Ancilla, and Hunters but not actually detail the elaborate backstories of, say, Felicity Price or Victoria Ash.<br /> <br /> They were going all in on system and toolkit versus lore.<br /> <br /> Which is problematic when a huge chunk of the fandom is lore junkies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, funny because in one of the recent reviews Yathzee, of Zero Punctuation and Fully Ramblomatic fame, was talking how Ubisoft at one point completely abandoned the future story bits because they either had no idea or willingness to develop that element. <br /> <br /> And I think the comparison works because AC also has shifted into a game that has strayed further and further from its roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T15:58:00-07:00","id":1562851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562830#post1562830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think the comparison works because AC also has shifted into a game that has strayed further and further from its roots.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but not necessarily bad, there's a lot of important differences. Phipps got it right as an analogy, but also what was the problem.<br /> <br /> AC changed because as time went on both the interest of these team changed and the players followed suit. And as a videogame you don't have things like &quot;my character/game isn't compatible with the new release!&quot;<br /> <br /> Videogames are independent installments, and no new game will cater to all previous fans anyway. That's not to say it couldn't have been bad, but that it would be another dynamic.<br /> <br /> But WoD has a lot of other complexities and needs, and they DID commit severe errors in the new storyline by not wanting to do things the players not only felt very strong about, but even weren't too specific. A simple &quot;advance the plot and those characters in a coherent way&quot; shouldn't be rocket science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T02:55:56-07:00","id":1562868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562698#post1562698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get your point, if not agree, but we have different approaches to clans so apples and oranges.<br /> <br /> But my main point is that, especially with the almost nonexistent plot development of V5, it's something you can mess with at will without much of a problem to conciliate with lore. It's also less revolting.<br /> <br /> Literally they could just say the Camarilla side outpaced the Sabbat after years of Embraces and no one paid enough attention to notice before.<br /> <br /> And seriously, I'd get rid of the whole clan/sect tie as a named thing. Better than force a balance of 4/sect excluding the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Heck, just say the Lasombra are more common among Cam than Anarchs and Independents, since that was the actual point and the Sabbat would be canonically out of the picture anyway.<br /> <br /> Every option works since there's zero official plot that relies on the Lasombra being so much more numerous in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> They didn't even got a Justicar, those are still the same seven clans as always.</div> </div> </div> </div>True I do prefer clan as culture, which inevitably has political ramifications. you don't really 'need' to explain lasombra presence full stop &quot;most lasombra are Sabbat some are cam or Anarch&quot; works fine, the defection is mostly for 5th's framing rather than in game praxis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And seriously, I'd get rid of the whole clan/sect tie as a named thing. Better than force a balance of 4/sect excluding the Sabbat. </div> </div> </div>It's fun flavouring and ads depth to the setting, you can easily have your cake and eat it with clans vs sect, half the fun of playing antitribu is seeing clan culture through the lens of the Sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T22:31:06-07:00","id":1562892,"title":"","content":"WHY is <i>&quot;Drama&quot;</i> a mechanic, instead of a narrative device? Do game masters not know how to <i>&quot;fudge their rolls&quot;</i> anymore?<br /> <br /> <b>But on a more positive note: </b>I noticed they say we can align with the Sabbat again.<br /> <br /> So, good. V6 writers realized who the best faction is, and brought them back into play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T11:53:51-07:00","id":1562900,"title":"","content":"Well, took a look at StrangeAdventures' video break down of character creation, and I'm not gonna lie. This looks like a significant improvement over V5.<br /> <br /> Having clan specific traits that provide exclusive bonuses and penalties to their disciplines is a very interesting spin on things.<br /> <br /> I can see it being used to highlight the clans' reputations, such as Brujah being renowned for their heavy emphasis on physical violence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if I interpreted this correctly, it sounds like they took another mechanic from Requiem, in that regardless of your generation, you can eventually gain access to elder powers (6 to 9 dots) by just surviving long enough. You don't explicitly need to diablerize people, but it does expedite the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> ALSO, it looks like you aren't limited to just choosing 5 powers from each discipline this time around. Much like old Blood Sorcery rituals, your level of mastery determines what rank of powers you're allowed to buy within each category. But you can have as many as you want, provided you earn enough EXP to afford them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T18:23:56-07:00","id":1562910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562868#post1562868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun flavouring and ads depth to the setting, you can easily have your cake and eat it with clans vs sect, half the fun of playing antitribu is seeing clan culture through the lens of the Sword.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but was there a need for a balance between groups? My problem was how they went through pains to have 4 Cam, 4 An, 4 Ind, 2 trump clans and block the Sabbat from being majority at any clan because... Reasons?<br /> <br /> I don't find the classic Antitribu definition interesting, but that's besides the point. Instead it's just that this 4/4/4/0 spread was seriously stupid and unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Simpler take that actually acknowledges lore:<br /> <br /> 1. Gangrel became Independent. They don't care.<br /> <br /> 2. Brujah split between Cam and Anarch. They are too engaged to not care, and lumping them all as Anarchs seriously miss what the clan and its role in the Cam are about.<br /> <br /> 3. Lasombra are bigger on Cam than the other two.<br /> <br /> 4. Tzimisce split between Independent or Cam. They like Domain Traditions, but are not big on fancy bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> 5. Sabbat does its own thing, how many vamps are there is irrelevant. They mass Embrace and get mass cull if needed, so whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562892#post1562892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHY is <i>&quot;Drama&quot;</i> a mechanic, instead of a narrative device? Do game masters not know how to <i>&quot;fudge their rolls&quot;</i> anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause some RPGs have it and use it well. They are throwing ideas in the wall to see what stick, so Drama was added in the list.<br /> <br /> This is regular for playtests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562900#post1562900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, took a look at StrangeAdventures' video break down of character creation, and I'm not gonna lie. This looks like a significant improvement over V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is. It also needs improvement, but that is the point anyway.<br /> <br /> Clan traits are good. Made a Setite, they turned the whole Serpentis set into Traits that you buy as Merits. Works very well, didn't need the full weight of a Discipline, accomplished the work flawlessly.<br /> <br /> Powers are quite like rituals. You pay \u00d75/\u00d76 on Discipline dots that come with a power like V5, but your dots also count for other things. If you just want a new power for a level you have, \u00d73. Awesome, though may genuinely get too powerful, we'll see.<br /> <br /> But no, they didn't use Requiem's &quot;age suffices&quot; system. The opposite, actually, we're back to Generation alone. It's just that they used same language from V5 Char Gen that confuses Gen and Age and so its kinda dense to understand. But essentially back to Legacy, except for this test they're in simplified brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:14:36-07:00","id":1562922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562910#post1562910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Powers are quite like rituals. You pay \u00d75/\u00d76 on Discipline dots that come with a power like V5, but your dots also count for other things. If you just want a new power for a level you have, \u00d73. Awesome, though may genuinely get too powerful, we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Caitiff having 3 randomly chosen disciplines also sounds like it can be a lot of fun. There's still the possibility of allowing you to power game, but now it relies on luck of the draw, instead of players just snatching up the strongest combo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562910#post1562910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But no, they didn't use Requiem's &quot;age suffices&quot; system. The opposite, actually, we're back to Generation alone. It's just that they used same language from V5 Char Gen that confuses Gen and Age and so its kinda dense to understand. But essentially back to Legacy, except for this test they're in simplified brackets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, that's annoying. I hate when they use Age and Generation interchangeably. Because it makes it difficult to tell if a Methuselah is a 4th generation vampire, or somebody who's been around for 1,000 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T23:54:07-07:00","id":1562927,"title":"","content":"Character creation looks so much easier, yeah. V5 was a mess of arrays, choices, and prerequisites. It's much simpler here. Though, I still think they should go for flat XP costs like on VTR2e. I can't wrap my head around why they haven't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T00:36:02-07:00","id":1562931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562922#post1562922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Caitiff having 3 randomly chosen disciplines also sounds like it can be a lot of fun. There's still the possibility of allowing you to power game, but now it relies on luck of the draw, instead of players just snatching up the strongest combo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a fan of that. It may work for some, but should be an optional rule. RNG like this works against character investment in my personal experience. Better to let the player make a character they actually want to play than let RNGesus screw them over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T03:29:20-07:00","id":1562935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562922#post1562922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caitiff having 3 randomly chosen disciplines also sounds like it can be a lot of fun. There's still the possibility of allowing you to power game, but now it relies on luck of the draw, instead of players just snatching up the strongest combo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aww, that's annoying. I hate when they use Age and Generation interchangeably. Because it makes it difficult to tell if a Methuselah is a 4th generation vampire, or somebody who's been around for 1,000 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on Caitiff, at least in principle. I can see the lack of control becoming a problem outside a few gimmicky chronicles, but at first glance I do feel like complete free choice wasn't as much of a Caitiff feel.<br /> <br /> For Generation they do have a couple lines where they specifically address that if you want to make a recently Embraced 6th Gen or something like that, you'll create the char by the rules of their Generation, not age, so the actual focus is well established even if buried in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562927#post1562927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Character creation looks so much easier, yeah. V5 was a mess of arrays, choices, and prerequisites. It's much simpler here. Though, I still think they should go for flat XP costs like on VTR2e. I can't wrap my head around why they haven't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thoroughly agree.<br /> <br /> If anything, V5 did had the best char gen approach for a game using scaling costs, but that starts, of course, with the dubious decision of going for scaling costs.<br /> <br /> But the requisites tree was kinda annoying with all the Amalgams, for now V6 has chargen going mostly smooth. I mean, for a pre-Alpha Playtest it was seamless. The only hiccup I found was that it is possible to distribute your Discipline dots in a way that buying all your starting allotment of Clan Traits is impossible.<br /> <br /> Found out because Ministry has many of them currently requiring Corruption, so not taking it results in an &quot;illegal&quot; sheet. But that's minor for this stage.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about what they'll make with the property and vehicle Backgrounds, what their plans are. It's weird, but intriguing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562931#post1562931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a fan of that. It may work for some, but should be an optional rule. RNG like this works against character investment in my personal experience. Better to let the player make a character they actually want to play than let RNGesus screw them over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially agree, but I think a compromise may be reachable.<br /> <br /> From the top of my head I'd say two of your choice plus one at random may make for a more interesting way of playing Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Older editions did it by making their cost in the middle, but now OoCs are getting a slight discount, so something has to balance Caitiff other than either making them too perfectly versatile or too screwed by having everything Out of Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T04:02:58-07:00","id":1562937,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13674_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13674\" data-vbnamecard=\"13674\">Amalasuintha</a> But that's actually how they're supposed to be presented in the lore. In addition to having no clan weaknesses that anybody can identify, they also have a capacity to just spontaneously manifest disciplines without the need for an instructor.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, many players saw this as an opportunity to pick their disciplines based on overpowered synergy, so that they could power game the chronicle.<br /> <br /> And for a game that's supposed to be focused on telling stories, having a player at the table who's looking for ways to break the system kind of ruins the fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562935#post1562935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agree on Caitiff, at least in principle. I can see the lack of control becoming a problem outside a few gimmicky chronicles, but at first glance I do feel like complete free choice wasn't as much of a Caitiff feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know if you're familiar with the Ioverse gaming channel, but they have a system where they randomly generate their character's race / class / attributes through dice rolls.<br /> <br /> Which often leads to hilarious results. Like Timmy, the halfling child who's player fully expected him to die in the campaign. But by the end of it, he was not only referred to as &quot;Goblin Slayer Jr.&quot; but was the only party member who survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T05:49:16-07:00","id":1562949,"title":"","content":"I think the Setites having parseltongue as a clan trait is kind of cute.<br /> <br /> Like, you wake up as a newly embraced member of the Ministry, and your pet python, who saw the whole thing, is freaking out trying to understand how you're still alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T07:48:06-07:00","id":1562951,"title":"","content":"They need more Natures. None of the Natures I see really fits the Sabbat missionary I want to make in the playtest game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T07:58:16-07:00","id":1562952,"title":"","content":"The good news about Natures is that V20 (and any edition other than V5) has a whole bunch you can choose from. And there are Wiki pages with huge lists of them, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Copy edits for grammar 08-10-2026, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T09:33:05-07:00","id":1562964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562951#post1562951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They need more Natures. None of the Natures I see really fits the Sabbat missionary I want to make in the playtest game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't you homebrew one or use something from Legacy? I've seen the form and they're not testing the individual items yet, just the overall idea, so that should be simple.<br /> <br /> They need more everything for now, and we will probably not see a big variety of anything until the actual game release in a year or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T10:29:22-07:00","id":1562967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562935#post1562935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Partially agree, but I think a compromise may be reachable.<br /> <br /> From the top of my head I'd say two of your choice plus one at random may make for a more interesting way of playing Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Older editions did it by making their cost in the middle, but now OoCs are getting a slight discount, so something has to balance Caitiff other than either making them too perfectly versatile or too screwed by having everything Out of Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is one of those things where I personally will never compromise for the simple reason that I don't find interesting and it makes me lose interest in the character because -I- didn't craft them into what I wanted them to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1562937#post1562937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13674_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13674\" data-vbnamecard=\"13674\">Amalasuintha</a> But that's actually how they're supposed to be presented in the lore. In addition to having no clan weaknesses that anybody can identify, they also have a capacity to just spontaneously manifest disciplines without the need for an instructor.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, many players saw this as an opportunity to pick their disciplines based on overpowered synergy, so that they could power game the chronicle.<br /> <br /> And for a game that's supposed to be focused on telling stories, having a player at the table who's looking for ways to break the system kind of ruins the fun.</div> </div> </div> </div> That may be the case in the lore, but it shouldn't be in chargen. This is one of those times were I come down hard on the side of separating the story and mechanics from one another. I wouldn't have it as an ST nor would I accept it as a player.<br /> <br /> Also I must note that I don't really care if some powergame their starting disciplines. That's up to the ST to decide whether it should be allowed or not. Hence why I say rolling for them should be an optional rule and not the de facto rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T12:58:34-07:00","id":1562973,"title":"","content":"We'll see if it even survives to the next Playtest.<br /> <br /> O think it may be covered with archetype packages like the Sire Types, with the option of switching one of the Disciplines with another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T21:21:53-07:00","id":1563082,"title":"","content":"Might be considered a hot take, but I kind of like how they scaled down the selection of skills.<br /> <br /> Figuring out where to spend my 11 Primaries, 7 Secondaries, and 5 Intermediaries always felt like more of a chore for me when creating characters.<br /> <br /> It seems like character creation became far more simpler this time around. As well as possibly being quicker to get through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T01:38:48-07:00","id":1563084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563082#post1563082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be considered a hot take, but I kind of like how they scaled down the selection of skills.<br /> <br /> Figuring out where to spend my 11 Primaries, 7 Secondaries, and 5 Intermediaries always felt like more of a chore for me when creating characters.<br /> <br /> It seems like character creation became far more simpler this time around. As well as possibly being quicker to get through?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind fewer Skills if there are fewer Attributes, too (e.g., Strength, Dexterity, Charisma, Resolve, Intelligence, Wits\u2014using the name Resolve instead of Composure means each Attribute has a different letter, making it easier for quick notation). But 9 Attributes versus 13 Skills seems unbalanced. And I'm not a huge fan of all the specialisations\u2014especially not with the character sheet layout. You kinda need multiple lines below each Skill to list them, or things will get cramped pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> In the end, I think they'll go back to something like 27 Skills and 9 Attributes, just because it's what people expect. But who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-14T04:11:30-07:00","id":1563086,"title":"","content":"I think the number of skills isn't the actual problem.<br /> <br /> The classic list has been there since 1st Ed and, seriously, it has always been clunky and uneven.<br /> <br /> Some have obvious uses, some have wide application, some have clear rules, some are highly useful in their areas.<br /> <br /> And some are not. Many have weird overlaps in application, while the game never even tried to tell what to do when that happens. Ambiguous rules, narrow fields, fuzzy applications, or just plainly useless outside very niche situations.<br /> <br /> We have an Academics skill that should cover all &quot;Humanities&quot;, but we also have Finances for reasons, a skill most seem to think to be about making money, which is actually the one thing it shouldn't do, and whose actual uses are all about accounting, except maybe Economic Analysis/Theory that may or may not be here or in Academics.<br /> <br /> CoD has a very similar number of skills, but has a far more solid list. WoD tried to solve it with even more skills and it only worsened the issue.<br /> <br /> But based on the form, I think they may be working on it, but not yet testing, which would mean what we saw is a placeholder list, not an attempt at a definitive solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T02:27:19-07:00","id":1563119,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my immediate thought was that it was like the V5 playtest's three Attributes. They don't need all the Skills in there if they're just focusing on other rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T18:03:21-07:00","id":1563130,"title":"","content":"Considering that 4-5 dots is supposed to represent the peak of human achievements, that would mean it's logical to assume most people wouldn't exceed 3 dots in anything on their character sheet. Limited to 2 dots for your average NPC.<br /> <br /> <br /> 11, 7, 5 sounds like way too much of a spread. I don't even have that many skills in real life, nor do I know of anybody else who does.<br /> <br /> Shrinking the selection and focusing more on specialties seems much more reasonable than making everybody function as a jack of all trades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T18:55:15-07:00","id":1563133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563130#post1563130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that 4-5 dots is supposed to represent the peak of human achievements, that would mean it's logical to assume most people wouldn't exceed 3 dots in anything on their character sheet. Limited to 2 dots for your average NPC.<br /> <br /> <br /> 11, 7, 5 sounds like way too much of a spread. I don't even have that many skills in real life, nor do I know of anybody else who does.<br /> <br /> Shrinking the selection and focusing more on specialties seems much more reasonable than making everybody function as a jack of all trades.</div> </div> </div> </div>PCs are heroes. This is a staple of TTRPG and was already in 1991. They're well above average. I'd say most people don't have a single 3 in the sheet, or only one, especially if Specialties give extra dice (being equivalent to another dot).<br /> <br /> That said, though, you got it inverted. Shrinking the selection is what will make characters even more Jack of All Trades, because that means each dot covers more actions.<br /> <br /> What I think ideal is to have more ways to work with specialties like CoD does, so you can add up specialties and other things to rely on them more than on base skill dots. In CoD you can use Merits and overlapping Specialties to have things like +2 dice when repairing cars and +1 on any skill when it's related to cars, so you have a decent 3 in practice while keeping Crafts at 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-15T20:41:26-07:00","id":1563136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563133#post1563133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PCs are heroes. This is a staple of TTRPG and was already in 1991. They're well above average. I'd say most people don't have a single 3 in the sheet, or only one, especially if Specialties give extra dice (being equivalent to another dot).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true in a classical fantasy setting, but WoD is supposed to take place in our world, in the modern era.<br /> <br /> We don't have Conan-esque dungeon divers, going around slaughtering hordes of monsters with a battle axe.<br /> <br /> We have Joe-Shmoe from accounting, who buys groceries on a financial budget.<br /> <br /> <br /> A neonate who was hastily embraced during their highschool / college years is not going to have 4 dots in mental or social skills. Just ask anybody who's ever found themselves reliving an embarrassing memory. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T01:41:05-07:00","id":1563137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563136#post1563136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true in a classical fantasy setting</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this is true in literature across the board, doubly so in RPGs, and IIRC is stated directly in most corebooks for VtM.<br /> <br /> Lestat, Victor Frankenstein, Axel and Otto Lidenbrock, Holmes, Watson, the Losers Club, the love triangle from Twilight. Even when such characters are conceptually common people thrown in exceptional circumstances, they're not really regular, anything but. What drives the story is how those extraordinary situations also reveal their extraordinary traits.<br /> <br /> This is not to say the PCs didn't had ordinary lives before. But they have never been meant to be average. Sure, they still have space to grow a lot, but they already begin as a cut above even among equals, in this case among other Neonates.<br /> <br /> Reasons for that abound, but most boil down to it being fun and easier to run. You want the PCs to succeed where their peers would fail, and to feel powerful and competent enough to do and see impressive things, even if their final fate is dark.<br /> <br /> Of course, stories of truly unremarkable people are perfectly possible and can be quite fun. But they're also quite more specific and hard to run properly, so very few RPGs focus standard char gen on them.<br /> <br /> You know two that actually do that? Paranoia and Call of Cthulhu. You know what they have in common? Both assume you'll start play with at least 3 extra characters ready, because they have extremely high mortality rates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T10:22:12-07:00","id":1563145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563137#post1563137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, this is true in literature across the board, doubly so in RPGs, and IIRC is stated directly in most corebooks for VtM.<br /> <br /> Lestat, Victor Frankenstein, Axel and Otto Lidenbrock, Holmes, Watson, the Losers Club, the love triangle from Twilight. Even when such characters are conceptually common people thrown in exceptional circumstances, they're not really regular, anything but. What drives the story is how those extraordinary situations also reveal their extraordinary traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now why'd you have to go and say something disgusting, like referencing <i>Twilight?</i><br /> <br /> Personally, I'd have gone with <i>True Blood</i> as an example.<br /> <br /> Start out with a bunch of hicks living in some podunk town...<br /> <br /> and by the end of the series, they're getting into fights with the spiritual reincarnation of Lilith, and the literal king of faeries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-16T19:37:50-07:00","id":1563150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563145#post1563145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now why'd you have to go and say something disgusting, like referencing <i>Twilight?</i><br /> <br /> Personally, I'd have gone with <i>True Blood</i> as an example.<br /> <br /> Start out with a bunch of hicks living in some podunk town...<br /> <br /> and by the end of the series, they're getting into fights with the spiritual reincarnation of Lilith, and the literal king of faeries.</div> </div> </div> </div>'cause I needed a bad lit example somewhere in the list, give it variety and I didn't want Harry Potter (which I thought on adding no less than 3 times, I admit).<br /> <br /> Also, didn't watch True Blood, but thanks to my ex wife I did watch all Twilight movies without puke.<br /> <br /> I must say, though: it's not a complete waste of your time. There are some genuinely good setting elements and designs between the dumb plot and horrendous prose.<br /> <br /> Kudos to the main actors too. Their work was top notch, they hit the level of asinine idiocy of the characters to the T. Especially Edward, as different from Bella Swan in her role as Kristen Stewart, Robert Pattinson was acting the whole time. He is not, in fact, like that.<br /> <br /> Jokes aside, it seems that Kristen Stewart got considerably better after hearing that in Snow White she interpreted Bella Swan again. I think there's nothing like a really bad movie to show you have to change something in your career.<br /> <br /> But seriously tho, the structure of the vampiric society in Twilight and several tidbits of how they work is genuinely worth exploring with an actually good story. And yes, I do include the shiny sparkles. As a way to justify emotionally complex and overly powerful predators to not prey at day, that's literally brilliant. But as the wise Megamind says, presentation matters, so... Yeah...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T15:24:00-07:00","id":1563196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563150#post1563150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, didn't watch True Blood, but thanks to my ex wife I did watch all Twilight movies without puke.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was afraid it was just going to be another sappy, vampire romance, soap opera, but it turned out rather decent. Had a lot of darker elements to it than I expected. Like there being a trailer park full of werepanthers, who were forced to engage in incest, because they were on the verge of extinction.<br /> <br /> Anyways, a brief synopsis of the setting is that vampires have managed to produce a form of synthetic blood which they can safely consume. Which means that after mass producing the synthetic, they no longer need to feed on humans, so a group calling themselves <i>&quot;The Authority&quot;</i> goes public and announces to the world vampires exist.<br /> <br /> Not all vampires liked this, since The Authority did not seem to consult anybody on the subject beforehand. While there are also no small amount of humans out there who still consider them monsters and have organized into vampire slaying hate groups.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but all the other supernatural creatures of the world don't have the same kind of safety net that synthetic blood provides, so they are still trying to conceal their existence from the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-17-2026, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T06:27:23-07:00","id":1563220,"title":"","content":"Sounds cool, and I guess this Authority has some shady stuff going on for them, too, given the obvious power play.<br /> <br /> Is someone exploring exclusive control over the synthetic blood production? Or is it really distributed to ensure the new status quo?<br /> <br /> Twilight has a number of cool ideas, as I said. It is more based in the idea of nomadic vampires, so they're fewer but far more well traveled, which means relevant interactions and conflicts aren't restricted by immediate area like a VtM city.<br /> <br /> Instead of a Camarilla you have the Volturi as a coven that runs the world from a small town in Italy and enforce their Masquerade, but their method is pure brutality: if you're careless enough for the Volturi to know of a breach of their laws, they go to your place and annihilate everyone they're not satisfied with, vampire or not.<br /> <br /> Covens are small bands. The Volturi are the largest with 30+ members total, the second largest was 7 before growing to 9 and the third a whopping 5. Most vampires are lone predators or covens of 2 or 3. It's a pretty different but interesting dynamic where you have small, tight local groups focusing on their own local stuff, but when vampire society is an issue it's very globally connected.<br /> <br /> Powers are another curious take. Becoming a vampire absurdly amplifies personal abilities. For most it's physical stuff, and they're quite overpowered from the get go, but any small supernatural power increases several orders of magnitude. With a more variable approach to what kinds of powers one can have, this means vampires with special powers are completely unpredictable on top of rare.<br /> <br /> Overall I think for real the bones can be used to build a solid setting. The story is trash, not that I have any problem with watered romance to be very clear, it's just the kind of annoyingly badly thought that you don't expect from a mediocre writer of juvenil literature, but from a mediocre 14yo. But the setting is creative and the ideas and concepts are pretty ok.<br /> <br /> It's unfortunate that all the good bits take a back seat to the asinine plot, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T13:42:13-07:00","id":1563232,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Surprisingly, no, The Authority have genuinely noble intentions. They're the ones who invented the True Blood synthetic, and then had it mass produced around the world. Their leader was disgusted with the way vampires had been conducting themselves, and decided that he was going to force them to become more civilized, whether they liked it or not. He's even established alliances with the human military to create a new branch of law enforcement that deals specifically with out of control vampires.<br /> <br /> The reason why other vampires hate The Authority, is because their previous existence allowed them to avoid consequences for their monstrous behavior. They covered up evidence of murder, they could glamour people into becoming their slaves, real blood tastes much better than the synthetic stuff. They were free to engage in all kinds of hedonistic debauchery without anyone to keep them in check.<br /> <br /> But now that the truth is out, unlife isn't so care free anymore. Even worse, the federal government knows about their existence now, which means vampires have to do humiliating shit, like paying taxes again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T16:24:14-07:00","id":1563237,"title":"","content":"So what's the possibility that white wolf will haphazardly staple Foraken 2e's Harmony bar onto every 6e product?<br /> <br /> Like I could see it working for Chagling as a straggle between Glamor and Banal and maybe W6 as a revised harano &amp; hauglosk. But I don't know if would work for mage or Hunter for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T18:14:12-07:00","id":1563238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563237#post1563237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the possibility that white wolf will haphazardly staple Foraken 2e's Harmony bar onto every 6e product?<br /> <br /> Like I could see it working for Chagling as a straggle between Glamor and Banal and maybe W6 as a revised harano &amp; hauglosk. But I don't know if would work for mage or Hunter for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I'd say no, but as you pointed out it can actually work surprisingly well for some lines.<br /> <br /> Not all. I know your current cynicism over the Playtest, but I'd wait a second round at least before trying any guesses at tendencies. For now we don't know if it will stick even in VtM.<br /> <br /> Something in that vibe for others? Werewolf shouldn't have as a main thing, but can have it for Harano/Hauglosk if used sparingly, only for big pressures or long periods of stress.<br /> <br /> Changeling, sure. Wraith too. Maybe Demon? I'm not as sure, but possible. Hunter can get something on the struggle of fighting monsters without becoming one, especially if we get the Imbued back.<br /> <br /> Mage I seriously doubt, Mummy I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T23:07:42-07:00","id":1563242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563238#post1563238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At first I'd say no, but as you pointed out it can actually work surprisingly well for some lines.<br /> <br /> Not all. I know your current cynicism over the Playtest, but I'd wait a second round at least before trying any guesses at tendencies. For now we don't know if it will stick even in VtM.<br /> <br /> Something in that vibe for others? Werewolf shouldn't have as a main thing, but can have it for Harano/Hauglosk if used sparingly, only for big pressures or long periods of stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I trust the development with Harano or Hauglosk. They'd have to show that they can cover the bases of the classic game before they run off trying to inject angst into everything.<br /> <br /> I think that it would be better as a very temporary tracker between Rage and Calm, which is going to be a volatile state that would be better served by a slider than writing down and erasing points. And no permanent failure states! Not for that tracker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changeling, sure. Wraith too. Maybe Demon? I'm not as sure, but possible. Hunter can get something on the struggle of fighting monsters without becoming one, especially if we get the Imbued back.<br /> <br /> Mage I seriously doubt, Mummy I don't know. </div> </div> </div>I suppose that you could make some variation on the Quintessence vs. Paradox tracker of old. For the Mummy games... are we talking Mummy 2e, or the Resurrection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T00:10:02-07:00","id":1563243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563242#post1563242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I trust the development with Harano or Hauglosk. They'd have to show that they can cover the bases of the classic game before they run off trying to inject angst into everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that or White wolf could just turn Harano and Hauglosk into a Drama like meta currency and leave the outburst in the control of the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T10:53:49-07:00","id":1563252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563242#post1563242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I trust the development with Harano or Hauglosk. They'd have to show that they can cover the bases of the classic game before they run off trying to inject angst into everything.<br /> <br /> I think that it would be better as a very temporary tracker between Rage and Calm, which is going to be a volatile state that would be better served by a slider than writing down and erasing points. And no permanent failure states! Not for that tracker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose that you could make some variation on the Quintessence vs. Paradox tracker of old. For the Mummy games... are we talking Mummy 2e, or the Resurrection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both options could work, if they would actually manage this well is something I don't feel I can guess, yet. It's a new team, new circumstances, let's wait and see. My point for now is just that it <i>could</i> work.<br /> <br /> For Mummy I'd say Resurrection, a full splat and with the improved Spell of Life.<br /> <br /> Mage... Yes, depending on how they make it, it could be used to represent Quintessence Pool vs Permadox. One thing I always found weird was the reliance on the Avatar Background for your natural pool of Quint. I understand why, but it's weird nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T13:32:48-07:00","id":1563265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563243#post1563243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that or White wolf could just turn Harano and Hauglosk into a Drama like meta currency and leave the outburst in the control of the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>ST control? Are we back in the 90s again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both options could work, if they would actually manage this well is something I don't feel I can guess, yet. It's a new team, new circumstances, let's wait and see. My point for now is just that it <i>could</i> work.<br /> <br /> For Mummy I'd say Resurrection, a full splat and with the improved Spell of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Amenti had Balance as a matter of importance, I guess if you really needed to you could have some kind of &quot;worldliness&quot; counterbalance. That, or it's a balance of spirit vs flesh like in Forsaken, with one netting you faster return to life if you die and the other giving you better spiritual interaction capabilities. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage... Yes, depending on how they make it, it could be used to represent Quintessence Pool vs Permadox. One thing I always found weird was the reliance on the Avatar Background for your natural pool of Quint. I understand why, but it's weird nonetheless. </div> </div> </div>That's the &quot;everyone needs a power stat background!&quot; part of the WoD that Vampire started with Generation. Of course, W:tA has none, and so vampire felt that it had to make bizarre-ass power up rules from drinking Garou with Pure Breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T13:47:34-07:00","id":1563266,"title":"","content":"If V6 is attempting to shift the setting back to its previous status quo, while still keeping elements of V5's lore in place, then I'm going to presume those rumors about the Nosferatu building a new Schrecknet may prove to be true.<br /> <br /> One with new and improved security measures, to mitigate the chance of such a large scale breach happening again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T16:29:03-07:00","id":1563268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563265#post1563265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Amenti had Balance as a matter of importance, I guess if you really needed to you could have some kind of &quot;worldliness&quot; counterbalance. That, or it's a balance of spirit vs flesh like in Forsaken, with one netting you faster return to life if you die and the other giving you better spiritual interaction capabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the &quot;everyone needs a power stat background!&quot; part of the WoD that Vampire started with Generation. Of course, W:tA has none, and so vampire felt that it had to make bizarre-ass power up rules from drinking Garou with Pure Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, Ma'at. I never got to read Resurrection, but I have enough basic Egyptology to get it.<br /> <br /> Yes, if they go for it there's actually a lot of ways they can work in Balance scales while keeping with the spirit of the game.<br /> <br /> And by the way, I don't think Werewolf should have a Harano/Hauglosk scale as an Angst Metter, even because my impression is that it's reducing the angst factor even in VtM. But I'm really leaning into the idea that a reworked Hauglosk could help explain the intransigence of Elder status quo in the Nation.<br /> <br /> Dump the idea of Hauglosk making Nazis. But Hauglosk makes misanthropes, kin abusers, purity obsession, all the good stuff each tribe is known for.<br /> <br /> On power stats, WtA didn't got a BG but got an Ability. Primal-Urge as a Talent figures among the worst ideas in its history, especially among those who stayed for several editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T16:30:12-07:00","id":1563269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563266#post1563266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If V6 is attempting to shift the setting back to its previous status quo, while still keeping elements of V5's lore in place, then I'm going to presume those rumors about the Nosferatu building a new Schrecknet may prove to be true.<br /> <br /> One with new and improved security measures, to mitigate the chance of such a large scale breach happening again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Highly probable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T17:34:15-07:00","id":1563273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563266#post1563266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If V6 is attempting to shift the setting back to its previous status quo, while still keeping elements of V5's lore in place, then I'm going to presume those rumors about the Nosferatu building a new Schrecknet may prove to be true.<br /> <br /> One with new and improved security measures, to mitigate the chance of such a large scale breach happening again.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the approach White wolf is taking with V6 I'm honestly carious how they're going to deal with W5 and to lesser extent H5 since they're so divergent from legacy counterparts. Like former I could see the Cult purging most of they more extreme members and rebrand back to the Get and I guess for the latter you can go full Vigil and have the imbued one of the many hunter types the player can join along with the SI which is nerfed due to getting hit with a funding cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T05:19:21-07:00","id":1563277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563273#post1563273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's the approach White wolf is taking with V6 I'm honestly carious how they're going to deal with W5 and to lesser extent H5 since they're so divergent from legacy counterparts. Like former I could see the Cult purging most of they more extreme members and rebrand back to the Get and I guess for the latter you can go full Vigil and have the imbued one of the many hunter types the player can join along with the SI which is nerfed due to getting hit with a funding cut.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alas, I fear that doing such may prove a sign of incompetence on their part.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-W5:</b> &quot;The nazi's are dead. All of them. The Get purged the entire lot.<br /> <br /> <b>During W5:</b> &quot;The Get are exclusively Nazi's. So much, in fact, that they abandoned the Garou Nation and are no longer a playable option.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>W6:</b> &quot;The Nazi's are dead... again! Turns out that not everyone in the tribe agreed with their ideology and rose up to purge their ranks.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, however, there is one circumstance where they could turn the situation around. They've already straight up stated that W5 was a reboot of the game, instead of a continuation of it. So, with that in mind, W6 could be the turning point in which the the less radicalized Get decide to clean house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T05:50:04-07:00","id":1563278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563277#post1563277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alas, I fear that doing such may prove a sign of incompetence on their part.<br /> <br /> <b>Pre-W5:</b> &quot;The nazi's are dead. All of them. The Get purged the entire lot.<br /> <br /> <b>During W5:</b> &quot;The Get are exclusively Nazi's. So much, in fact, that they abandoned the Garou Nation and are no longer a playable option.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>W6:</b> &quot;The Nazi's are dead... again! Turns out that not everyone in the tribe agreed with their ideology and rose up to purge their ranks.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, however, there is one circumstance where they could turn the situation around. They've already straight up stated that W5 was a reboot of the game, instead of a continuation of it. So, with that in mind, W6 could be the turning point in which the the less radicalized Get decide to clean house.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is also two other options:<br /> <br /> 1) Since V5 was a reboot they might ignore it altogether and theoretical W6 could be a continuation of some elements of Revised/W20.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2) They can ignore Werewolf and Hunter altogether. This I think is less likely since they have already a playerbase for both systems but I am not sure how big that playerbase is and I have not listened to the panels about the future of WoD6 but it might be telling that W6 and H6 were nowhere to be found on that future system consideration screen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T06:22:09-07:00","id":1563279,"title":"","content":"AFAIK they didn't cited plans for Werewolf of Hunter yet, instead they talked about Mage and Changeling. But that's probably to compensate the fans who were waiting for their WoD5 versions, not a lack of interest in doing the other two.<br /> <br /> The most probable path with W6 will be going back to Legacy lore and ignoring W5, since W5 was another setting altogether. That's way simpler and less stupid than making the Cult become the Get.<br /> <br /> H5 isn't so divergent of its Legacy counterpart, it's just that its counterpart isn't in any way HtR. I'm kinda annoyed with people saying that as if Hunters Hunted wasn't a thing. H5 is faithful to Legacy as far as the groups it covers go within the SI plot.<br /> <br /> It's lame what they did to the Imbued. It's really disrespectful with the title of Reckoning. But it is not comparable with W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T06:41:19-07:00","id":1563280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563279#post1563279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK they didn't cited plans for Werewolf of Hunter yet, instead they talked about Mage and Changeling. But that's probably to compensate the fans who were waiting for their WoD5 versions, not a lack of interest in doing the other two.<br /> <br /> The most probable path with W6 will be going back to Legacy lore and ignoring W5, since W5 was another setting altogether. That's way simpler and less stupid than making the Cult become the Get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly w6 going back to the legacy wta setting is easy solution though I suspect that white wolf won't do that for some stupid arbitrary reasons like &quot;reducing fan confusion&quot; and/or a futile attempt at retaining W5 fans.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the saddest thing parawolf could do is to dig up the corpse of the cancelled hunter version of W5 and try to graft as much of the setting onto w6 to try and make a good game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-20-2026, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T06:42:20-07:00","id":1563281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563278#post1563278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there is also two other options:<br /> <br /> 1) Since V5 was a reboot they might ignore it altogether and theoretical W6 could be a continuation of some elements of Revised/W20.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2) They can ignore Werewolf and Hunter altogether. This I think is less likely since they have already a playerbase for both systems but I am not sure how big that playerbase is and I have not listened to the panels about the future of WoD6 but it might be telling that W6 and H6 were nowhere to be found on that future system consideration screen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was V5 a reboot?<br /> <br /> I call W6 as such, because they explicitly stated it was so in the introductory section of their book. But I'm unfamiliar with V5 doing the same.<br /> <br /> Also, from what I've looked up of 6th edition so far, they've said that lore from 5th edition will still be relevant in 6th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T06:51:48-07:00","id":1563282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563279#post1563279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's lame what they did to the Imbued. It's really disrespectful with the title of Reckoning. But it is not comparable with W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with getting rid of the Imbued is that without them, the Hunters don't stand a chance. Taking down a vampire might make you feel like a bad ass, but in the grand scheme of things, they are small fry compared to <i>literally anything else.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Delirium, The Mists, true magic, Lores, Gifts, Cantrips...<br /> <br /> That's not something you can fight with sawed off shotgun and a 'can do' attitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T07:24:13-07:00","id":1563283,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute.<br /> <br /> Diablerie now lowers your generation by at least 1 step, regardless of whatever generation your victim was?<br /> <br /> That just made the Sabbat and the Assamites infinitely more dangerous!<br /> <br /> But on the plus side....<br /> <br /> *loads stake launcher with malicious intent*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T10:09:04-07:00","id":1563284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563281#post1563281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was V5 a reboot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typo, probably, they meant W5 was a reboot.<br /> <br /> V5 is not and officially assumes all the Revised lore as still standing, it just advanced the story, its quality notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> W5 is likely to be ignored if the current path is followed consistently. The setting was a failure even among players of the edition, it's widely regarded as shallow and incomplete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563282#post1563282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with getting rid of the Imbued is that without them, the Hunters don't stand a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is not a problem as far as setting goes. And it isn't as if the Imbued were nearly enough to cover the gap, they're still way weaker than any other splat.<br /> <br /> The goal of the setting isn't wage war against the other gamelines and come on top. It's to tell the stories of more or less common people drawn to the supernatural side of the world and deciding to take action despite the odds. That's as true for Hunters Hunted, The Vigil or Imbued in the real Hunter the Reckoning.<br /> <br /> Players of hunters are in it for the challenge of finding human solutions to superhuman threat. And remember that different gamelines are not the same setting, so any power that's too much of a problem can simply be ignored.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it's the opposite, though, because having access to the modern world without the strange limitations and needs of supernatural beings is still a functional asset.<br /> <br /> Let's just say that Ravnos only needed as much firepower in the Week of Nightmares because it was a written tale without dice rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T10:10:16-07:00","id":1563285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563282#post1563282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with getting rid of the Imbued is that without them, the Hunters don't stand a chance. Taking down a vampire might make you feel like a bad ass, but in the grand scheme of things, they are small fry compared to <i>literally anything else.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Delirium, The Mists, true magic, Lores, Gifts, Cantrips...<br /> <br /> That's not something you can fight with sawed off shotgun and a 'can do' attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your talking about something completely different than <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>. It's in-world repercussions vs the feelings of the players/IP consistency.<br /> <br /> Look, they could have said that Messengers have disappeared suddenly and Imbued lost their powers. They could have make it Hunter: the Revengence or whatever. Instead they not only retconned Imbued out of existence without even a nod to their existence they also called the system Hunter: the Reckoning even if it has little in common with the original system for Imbued other than monster hunting. <br /> <br /> And no, the problem with retconning Imbued out of the setting is not that without them Hunters do not stand a chance. That's not a problem especially in a setting where the governments are aware of vampires existence, most of the elder vampires &quot;went to the East&quot;, Werewolves are so depressed that they are pretty non\\threatening and all the other supernaturals might as well not exist. Besides whether it was Hunters Hunted or Reckoning, hunter games were always about madmen and vigiliantes who were facing impossible odds and their doom was all but ascertained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T10:12:21-07:00","id":1563286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563283#post1563283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie now lowers your generation by at least 1 step, regardless of whatever generation your victim was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> Including Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> Make a regular starting 13th Gen. Embrace 10 Thin Bloods. Profit.<br /> <br /> Keep doing for the XP to max out your Ante level Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T13:50:09-07:00","id":1563290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563284#post1563284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 is likely to be ignored if the current path is followed consistently. The setting was a failure even among players of the edition, it's widely regarded as shallow and incomplete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly this comes down to what upper management thinks of W5. Sure they might mandate the end of the W5 setting and maybe force Renegade to release a apcolypse book to clear the board for w6 back to legacy edition.<br /> <br /> There's equal chance that the management might still keep w5 setting while trying to bring back the legacy to try and appease the old heads for an arbitrary reason like &quot;IP consistency&quot; and/or they Really uncomfortable with the concept of kinfolk and metis and going back to legacy means bring them back which would render it a no starter in they eyes.<br /> <br /> Based on parawolf past behaviour I'm going with the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T14:34:57-07:00","id":1563291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563286#post1563286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup.<br /> <br /> Including Thin Bloods.<br /> <br /> Make a regular starting 13th Gen. Embrace 10 Thin Bloods. Profit.<br /> <br /> Keep doing for the XP to max out your Ante level Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Antes vs Caine:</b> <i>&quot;Time for a rematch, old man!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Caine vs Antes:</b> <i>&quot;You kids have stat blocks, I don't...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Caine Wins!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T19:39:52-07:00","id":1563294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563290#post1563290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on parawolf past behaviour I'm going with the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox past behavior gated everything that didn't fit &quot;gritty street level Cam vs Anarchs&quot;. The last books backpedaled this. Their past behavior assumed their business side was solid and correct. The Playtest is commanded by a businesswoman from Wizards. Past behavior caused several failed projects and Bloodlines 2. They got backlash so heavy they had to literally promise they'd stop trying other videogame genres.<br /> <br /> What you're saying can happen. But assuming it, currently ignores how badly circumstances changed since Bloodlines 2 and even the most recent actual releases, both books and actual Playtest content.<br /> <br /> I dislike most things Paradox did until now, and I despise how they handled it all until recently. But at this moment there's zero actual reasons to expect they'll follow their old style, as they're both forbidden from doing so and demonstrably trying something different.<br /> <br /> For sure I think they can still butcher things, but at least will be newish errors, if it happens at all to that degree. Bashing an actual new situation for the sake of it doesn't seems conducive of a useful analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T21:14:58-07:00","id":1563295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563294#post1563294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For sure I think they can still butcher things, but at least will be newish errors, if it happens at all to that degree. Bashing an actual new situation for the sake of it doesn't seems conducive of a useful analysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there's equal proof that Paradox would order a end of W5 to make room Re-reboot than there is that they will keep W5 while haphazardly graft on legacy elements to try and please everybody.<br /> <br /> We'll see when parawolf make it to W6, If this edition makes it to W6...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T03:27:27-07:00","id":1563301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition#post1562353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/world-of-darkness/news/vtm-sixth-edition-faq\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/g...th-edition-faq</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I really wish they'd stop trying to make vamily a thing,,,,,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://images.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness/og-image.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness Nexus - Digital TTRPG Toolset </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\"> https://app.demiplane.com/nexus/worldofdarkness </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Official Digital Toolset for World of Darkness on Demiplane </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> couple of notes from playtest docs as well<br /> <br /> -necromancy and oblivion appear to be re-seperated Oblivion appears to be obtenerbration<br /> <br /> -Health and hunger are merged.<br /> <br /> -protean appears to merged with Animalism (!)<br /> <br /> -a new disciplines called corruption and Tellurgy are present<br /> <br /> -the clan of death is again being refered to as clan Giovanni,<br /> <br /> -viss is back<br /> <br /> -a lot of supplementary mechanics are being tied directly to your clan outside of discipline and flaw, clan beasts seem to have a specific flavour<br /> <br /> -some clans can choose one of the core disciplines to be a different one.<br /> <br /> Honestly not sure what to make of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for reposting this. I\u2019m really looking forward to it, if only because it sounds like a vast improvement from V5 and maybe even a return to some of the principles of V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T08:21:28-07:00","id":1563304,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude was so overpowered that merging it with Thaumaturgy and Protean was a good idea.<br /> <br /> It's a simple change too.<br /> <br /> &quot;With Protean, you can change yourself. With Protean + Magic, you can change others.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T08:22:14-07:00","id":1563305,"title":"","content":"I know it's still early in development, but I kind of like the new change to the humanity system for V6.<br /> <br /> It may not be the same as the old <i>Paths of Enlightenment</i>, but it seems like there is a hell of a lot more leeway for you to play out your more monstrous side of being a vampire, without risk of becoming a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually, I've been watching reviews from play testers, and at least one of them said that it felt almost impossible for the players to actually reach that point, if they didn't want to; because humanity is now presented as freeform role play, instead of mechanical functionality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T08:25:22-07:00","id":1563306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563304#post1563304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude was so overpowered that merging it with Thaumaturgy and Protean was a good idea.<br /> <br /> It's a simple change too.<br /> <br /> &quot;With Protean, you can change yourself. With Protean + Magic, you can change others.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But you had to sacrifice options in Protean in order to obtain Vicissitude powers. So the merger forced you to choose between personal shapeshifting, or transforming other people instead.<br /> <br /> Which is ridiculous. Just keep them separate powers, if you're going to force people to pick one over the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T09:22:37-07:00","id":1563307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563305#post1563305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's still early in development, but I kind of like the new change to the humanity system for V6.<br /> <br /> It may not be the same as the old <i>Paths of Enlightenment</i>, but it seems like there is a hell of a lot more leeway for you to play out your more monstrous side of being a vampire, without risk of becoming a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually, I've been watching reviews from play testers, and at least one of them said that it felt almost impossible for the players to actually reach that point, if they didn't want to; because humanity is now presented as freeform role play, instead of mechanical functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the playtest set up to actually test that mechanic though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T11:35:02-07:00","id":1563310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563307#post1563307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the playtest set up to actually test that mechanic though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard to say, as it seems like your humanity rating kind of 'resets' at the start of each night. Somebody who's actually played the playtest would have to elaborate on that, as I'm just going off their reviews.<br /> <br /> Diablerie will shift you one step towards Monstrous, unless you are already at monstrous 2. In which case, it's an all you can eat soul buffet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T13:38:08-07:00","id":1563313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563304#post1563304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vicissitude was so overpowered that merging it with Thaumaturgy and Protean was a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it was overpowered. The lack of rules on how to handle it besides few tradeoffs more like made it ST dependant. It could really be powerful at some tables, but at others was quite underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Regardless, it was good to merge it because it was thematically redundant. Despite the many bad decisions on how to handle the details, V5 did ok with the approach to Disciplines, and Vis was its poster child. V6 may correct the main issue with the option to buy multiple powers, now, but let's see what they do to Vicissitude if they follow through with it being its own thing again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563305#post1563305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's still early in development, but I kind of like the new change to the humanity system for V6.<br /> <br /> It may not be the same as the old <i>Paths of Enlightenment</i>, but it seems like there is a hell of a lot more leeway for you to play out your more monstrous side of being a vampire, without risk of becoming a wight.<br /> <br /> Actually, I've been watching reviews from play testers, and at least one of them said that it felt almost impossible for the players to actually reach that point, if they didn't want to; because humanity is now presented as freeform role play, instead of mechanical functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still mechanical functionality, though, just not their same function. It's now about what you set for your character as their former self. There's some loss, but also some interesting space to explore how the Embrace changed you that didn't exist in Legacy, a look into the person you were rather than on a generic moral play about losing your soul.<br /> <br /> Now, to be honest Legacy was already pretty easy on not becoming a Wight. Losing the last dots of Humanity demanded some real effort. But I get it, with this system you can play a lot of variations on where your behavior sets you in the scale than just being low Humanity.<br /> <br /> And more importantly: we finally have a means to recover Humanity more clearly without using XP, which I always felt as a heavy problem with the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563307#post1563307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the playtest set up to actually test that mechanic though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is.<br /> <br /> On top of usual and new triggers, you mark the Nature and Beast trackers every night and you can mark any of them to get a Willpower point, so you'll be regularly pressed to take decisions about it.<br /> <br /> What changes is that you have options for how your character stays where you want. You can avoid sins/stains, as normal, but instead you can also engage your Beast/Nature to erase marks, and finally you can force yourself into Frenzy or Outburst to slide to where you want to be.<br /> <br /> And the feedback form has an entire page for this, so yes, they're looking into it in this test.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563310#post1563310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to say, as it seems like your humanity rating kind of 'resets' at the start of each night. Somebody who's actually played the playtest would have to elaborate on that, as I'm just going off their reviews.<br /> <br /> Diablerie will shift you one step towards Monstrous, unless you are already at monstrous 2. In which case, it's an all you can eat soul buffet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't reset, it actually worsens.<br /> <br /> Every night you get 1 extra mark on each track, so if you don't engage this system in any other way you'll be rolling for Frenzy and Outburst every 5 nights at least (every night if you resist, until you fail).<br /> <br /> And you still get marks for Diablerie, you just stop getting an automatic slide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T17:35:38-07:00","id":1563317,"title":"","content":"Well regardless of you're opinions on V6 humanity I would say this is a good replacement to W5's Harano and Haoglusk and white wolf would be really dumb if they don't implement it in W6.<br /> <br /> If there's a W6 in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T18:07:55-07:00","id":1563319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563317#post1563317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well regardless of you're opinions on V6 humanity I would say this is a good replacement to W5's Harano and Haoglusk and white wolf would be really dumb if they don't implement it in W6.<br /> <br /> If there's a W6 in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, RAGE is supposed to be a 'gift' from the Wyrm, correct?<br /> <br /> Which means that Wyrm Taint can be cleansed with werewolf depression! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T18:10:14-07:00","id":1563320,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Okay, so from what you're saying, it sounds like they need to improve the way these systems are worded. Because it seems like the play testers might be misinterpreting how the system is actually supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T18:21:00-07:00","id":1563321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563319#post1563319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm not mistaken, RAGE is supposed to be a 'gift' from the Wyrm, correct?<br /> <br /> Which means that Wyrm Taint can be cleansed with werewolf depression! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. The BotW notes that excessive, brutal rage is giving yourself over, but Rage wouldn't be a basic spirit stat for purely Weaver and Wyld spirits if it definitely and inextricably was of the Wyrm. Additionally, according to Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, page 52, Rage is the fury of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Thrall of the Wyrm didn't even exist in 1e, and for everything I could rake it across the coals for, W5 doesn't have Thrall of the Wyrm, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T18:29:27-07:00","id":1563322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563321#post1563321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. The BotW notes that excessive, brutal rage is giving yourself over, but Rage wouldn't be a basic spirit stat for purely Weaver and Wyld spirits if it definitely and inextricably was of the Wyrm. Additionally, according to Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, page 52, Rage is the fury of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Thrall of the Wyrm didn't even exist in 1e, and for everything I could rake it across the coals for, W5 doesn't have Thrall of the Wyrm, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's on Fan game I come across where Thrall of the Wyrm was reworked so it only happens when a garou rages under effects of Bane taint or they really intended to do those terrible actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T20:03:40-07:00","id":1563327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563320#post1563320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> Okay, so from what you're saying, it sounds like they need to improve the way these systems are worded. Because it seems like the play testers might be misinterpreting how the system is actually supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, they're using the phrasing &quot;marking off&quot; in a rather ambiguous way. But I'm pretty sure it's to increase marks rather than reducing them each night. I'd have to reread a lot, but IIRC there's one or two places where it is stated in clearer terms, but not in the actual rule, which sucks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if they had it correct it would be only one mark in each track, not a reset. That, at least, is exceedingly clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563321#post1563321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The BotW notes that excessive, brutal rage is giving yourself over, but Rage wouldn't be a basic spirit stat for purely Weaver and Wyld spirits if it definitely and inextricably was of the Wyrm. Additionally, according to Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, page 52, Rage is the fury of Gaia.<br /> <br /> Thrall of the Wyrm didn't even exist in 1e, and for everything I could rake it across the coals for, W5 doesn't have Thrall of the Wyrm, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thrall of the Wyrm still existed for most of the game, 1st edition isn't the best one to define any theme of the game (it's arguably the worst 1st edition from Legacy, and that says something), and more importantly, in a triatic theology it makes perfect sense for Rage to be a gift/trait from the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> None of that puts Rage within the <i>corrupted</i> Wyrm, though, so jokes aside it would remain a no, Rage isn't Wyrm taint and Harano doesn't cleanse it. Even because Harano is also Wyrm aligned (emotional decay and self-destruction).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T00:22:10-07:00","id":1563330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563327#post1563327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably, they're using the phrasing &quot;marking off&quot; in a rather ambiguous way. But I'm pretty sure it's to increase marks rather than reducing them each night. I'd have to reread a lot, but IIRC there's one or two places where it is stated in clearer terms, but not in the actual rule, which sucks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, even if they had it correct it would be only one mark in each track, not a reset. That, at least, is exceedingly clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was confused by how you gain a tick in both Monstrous and Humanity, and presumed that meant you were balancing out the scale.<br /> <br /> The new 'outburst' mechanic (a Humanity themed counterpoint to Frenzy) completely slipped my mind at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that is an interesting new spin on things. Your character can be so obsessed with the person they used to be, that it can cause them to rail against their Beast in dramatic fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T00:35:51-07:00","id":1563331,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's been some misunderstandings/misinformation going round, as certain people have said the Humanity trackers get wiped clean between sessions, which doesn't seem to be true from the actual rules packet. Which is a good thing, because otherwise you'd rarely ever frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T08:14:05-07:00","id":1563337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563330#post1563330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was confused by how you gain a tick in both Monstrous and Humanity, and presumed that meant you were balancing out the scale.<br /> <br /> The new 'outburst' mechanic (a Humanity themed counterpoint to Frenzy) completely slipped my mind at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, that is an interesting new spin on things. Your character can be so obsessed with the person they used to be, that it can cause them to rail against their Beast in dramatic fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast Frenzy isn't an actual Frenzy, either, despite the name. You still have normal Frenzy with the usual effects and it doesn't slide the scale.<br /> <br /> What Outburst and Beast Frenzy do is similar to V5 Clan Compulsions. Well, for now Beast Frenzy is literally the V5 Clan Compulsion. You get a guidance on how to behave, penalty when trying to do something else and a condition to end the state. Then you slide in the scale.<br /> <br /> On the marks, they're in the Beast and Nature tracks, not the scale. The tracks are to time the Frenzy/Outburst rolls. They only trigger when a track reaches 5, you can try to resist or Ride the Wave, if you roll and resist it erases 1 mark, going back to 4. If you Frenzy/Outburst, at its conclusion you slide in the scale.<br /> <br /> Marking both makes sense. They're both drives you carry within, they are not really opposite and they can be both neglected, so you can have a balanced vampire that fulfills regularly both without inner conflict, and a balanced one that lives from Frenzy to Outburst interspersed with a refusal or denial of who they are in both senses.<br /> <br /> And I agree it's a cool dynamic, even if it needs a little polish. It isn't what Humanity used to be about, it's a rough departure, but not a bad theme at all to pursue. If they decide to go back to a more traditional take, I'd say they could let both options in the book as equally valid play styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T10:11:08-07:00","id":1563343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563337#post1563337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I agree it's a cool dynamic, even if it needs a little polish. It isn't what Humanity used to be about, it's a rough departure, but not a bad theme at all to pursue. If they decide to go back to a more traditional take, I'd say they could let both options in the book as equally valid play styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think codifying what Humanity is has been a problem from the onset. Especially for neurodivergent people, who are biologically wired to view the world in a completely different perspective.<br /> <br /> Refocusing your Humanity to be the remaining vestiges of your mortal self is a far better approach to the situation, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Also, what you said about balancing the two extremes provides an interesting possibility for how they might reintroduce Golconda in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-22-2026, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T11:51:53-07:00","id":1563344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563343#post1563343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think codifying what Humanity is has been a problem from the onset. Especially for neurodivergent people, who are biologically wired to view the world in a completely different perspective.<br /> <br /> Refocusing your Humanity to be the remaining vestiges of your mortal self is a far better approach to the situation, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Also, what you said about balancing the two extremes provides an interesting possibility for how they might reintroduce Golconda in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that what the game was trying to encode is not exactly intuitive to explain in its context, and frankly, they chose the words for it poorly.<br /> <br /> Humanity with a Hierarchy of Sins is a key part of the Gothic side of the game. Not as in Goth counterculture, but the original two waves of Gothic Horror literature in the 18th and 19th centuries.<br /> <br /> One central element of Gothic is a naturalistic take on morality. It's not moral in the sense we usually understand of socially accepted morals or individual beliefs, but rather the notion that the most fundamental moral principles are so basic and intuitive we can say they exist as a fact, even if we can't explain why.<br /> <br /> Killing is bad. Stealing is bad. Violence is bad. Nuance matters and circumstances change everything, but no one with a healthy mind will deny those basic ideas. The Romans were a warlike people, as by the way the modern US is, too, and many other nations. But if you asked a Roman, just as if you ask a US citizen, war is a necessary evil, not a good thing. So to Gothic the first point is this: Good and Evil are real, but not in the way we rationalize and rather in their basic principles.<br /> <br /> Gothic's second point is a naturalistic reward to Good and Evil. The villain will terrorize and horrify. They'll harm, kill, maim. Yet in the end they'll pay. The villain will fall. Their victims will suffer, but those who escape and are good will have the opportunity to live a happy life. Those who are like the villain will suffer torment in life even as they torment others, and in the end will meet a horrible and solitary end.<br /> <br /> Again, though, Gothic is naturalistic, and this is key: these who live doing good will have good lives because they don't make unnecessary enemies, because they don't obsess over their whims, they don't live in frustration. They do good to others band that increases the chance that they'll get goodness in return. Isn't perfect, but is a positive balance. The villain will suffer because the natural consequences of their actions will get them. They're despised. Their obsessions can only grow. Their failings will follow them. Not because the world wants to punish them, though, but because their actions are building up to this.<br /> <br /> Finally, it's a morality play about choices, this is the third point that closes it all. Gothic Horror is based in the premise that most of the time the difference between Good and Evil is clear. It's not always big, but it's usually clear. And while choosing Good may be hard or inconvenient, it is ultimately feasible: you'll have to give up on something, but you can live without it. You may have to suffer or face hardships, but they're not unsurmountable. The Gothic villain is evil in the end because they chose evil, and they kept this choice again and again. Good people don't live easy lives, they choose to do right rather than convenient and the reward isn't instantaneous. But in the end it's the villain whom doomed themselves.<br /> <br /> In this interplay, the Gothic plays complex and traditional morals and adages as frequently being excuses to chose poorly. The villain will rarely recognize themselves as a villain. They are victims of the circumstances, they're just upholding honor, or proper norms, or science in the second wave. They are full of legitimate reasons to have chosen what they did, because no horror is greater than to face the fact you're the one responsible for your choices and their consequences. Society in the Gothic is full of false maxims about how hard it is to do good, just to release people from guilty over their bad choices.<br /> <br /> Legacy VtM plays this trope, and one of the main mechanics for it is Humanity. Having it high feels good. Your reward is mostly to be satisfied with yourself. Lowering it gets you ever closer to a terrible end. The undead are all the time telling each other about how the Beast gnaws at your mind and slowly draws you to the bottom. But the actual rules tell another story by design. Avoiding Frenzy is hard, but doable. Feeding safely just requires that you do frequently in small sips, which is inconvenient, but sustainable. You can avoid all the sins in the Hierarchy if you simply chose to do so, and while that'll make your life harder, rarely will you be really required to do any of them.<br /> <br /> None of those are problems with the rules, they are exactly the intention: staying good is meant to be feasible, it was in your reach all along. The fluff on Humanity being a slippery slope? It was an unreliable narrator for a reason: <b>he is lying</b>. To you the reader, probably to himself, to all Kindred and with all Kindred. The punchline is that Vampiric society isn't horrible because they're damned, damnation is just something they keep parroting to live with their choices. Their society is horrible because they're selfish assholes in a purely mundane way, even if the consequences, not the cause, are magically amplified.<br /> <br /> Within this proposal, this vision of gothic horror and dramatic theme, Humanity had a specific role that was never about morality in a social or religious sense, it was about the price of choosing power and convenience over basic decency. The game was too obtuse, though, and failed terribly to convey this goal. Which is not a problem unique to VtM in the WoD. And this new Humanity Scale covers another theme entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T06:02:14-07:00","id":1563364,"title":"","content":"That theme of supernatural monsters doing totally (in)human evil is at the foundation of WoD. Despite their protestation of not being human anymore or ever Cainites, garou or mages are still painfully human: shortsighted, greedy, envious hypocrites who do bad shit not because of divine curse or cosmic god of entropy but this is how they explain away their evil. <br /> <br /> Anarchs are saying how much better they are than Camarilla and how equal and inclusive they are but at the end of the day they use similar structures of powers and in many cases anarch Barons are as authoritarian as their Prince counterparts. Garou have the noble goal of stopping the forces of decay and destruction but most often they just spend time bickering or openly attacking each other or Fera in general. There might have been some good intentions at the forming of Cabal of Pure Thought and modern Technocracy but they are mostly swallowed by a fascist need for uniformity and control. <br /> <br /> So it's interesting how V6 is going to approach this theme and where it's going to put a focus in their approach to the setting and mechanical workings of it. Can't be worse than V5, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T15:40:03-07:00","id":1563379,"title":"","content":"Just realized something else about V6 mechanics that needs to be addressed: <b>making your Vitae count as your health bar.</b><br /> <br /> This needs to be changed, because otherwise it would imply that vampires do not naturally reconstitute themselves anymore. It also implies that vampires no longer have access to blood healing anymore.<br /> <br /> If your Vitae and your health bar are one in the same, and you have blood healing, then that would mean the vampire can enter an infinite feedback loop of spending and replenishing their blood over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T15:49:02-07:00","id":1563380,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it can't be worse, but would definitely take an extra effort to do so.<br /> <br /> The only splat I'd say that really manages to do inhuman evil outside the Evil Forces\u2122 of Baali, Wyrm and Nefandi is Changeling. Of all lines, the Fae are genuinely build to facilitate a player that does utterly despicable shit for reasons a human would not have an analogous drive.<br /> <br /> All the others aren't just human evils in the sense of being literary metaphors, the games literally rely thematically on their failings being entirely human despite their negation of such. It's just that the choice of first person narrator, while immersive, makes it kinda obtuse as you get the in-character evasive justification rather than the direct explanation of the themes.<br /> <br /> So, in a nutshell:<br /> <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> has as main conflict selfish decisions justified by a Beast that's real, but has only a fraction of the strength they say.<br /> <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> has as main conflict a military leadership that's too proud of its role and prestige to accept they messed up and must admit their failings to move forward.<br /> <b>Demon: the Fallen</b> is about how war fucks up a soldier, literally. The whole problem is Torment, and behind all the poetic descriptions it's &quot;just&quot; regular PTSD. The main conflict is about how those powerful spirits are trying to cope with good old trauma, with all the regular responses to trauma, including misanthropy, reliving, negation, dissociation, and even their own way of seeking therapy.<br /> <br /> Mage and Changeling are harder to point one main conflict because they're more thematically open, so while all lines have other conflicts and perspectives to follow, those two are hard to fix any option as being the main one.<br /> <br /> Wraith, Mummy and Hunter I don't know enough to say much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T15:58:32-07:00","id":1563381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563379#post1563379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just realized something else about V6 mechanics that needs to be addressed: <b>making your Vitae count as your health bar.</b><br /> <br /> This needs to be changed, because otherwise it would imply that vampires do not naturally reconstitute themselves anymore. It also implies that vampires no longer have access to blood healing anymore.<br /> <br /> If your Vitae and your health bar are one in the same, and you have blood healing, then that would mean the vampire can enter an infinite feedback loop of spending and replenishing their blood over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>We discussed that already repeatedly.<br /> <br /> Bottom line, it's actually as if healing with Vitae were automatic, constant and without led turn limit. Don't try to think the fluff on the old terms and the description part will actually be ok.<br /> <br /> The problem is if mechanically it will work well, and overall we're seeing a lot of complaints all over, it seems to be either the most polemic or outright least liked change, even worse than the Drama points despite how popular they are as bashing target.<br /> <br /> Can't say for sure because this is only surface observation, not the actual feedback form data, so take this with a grain of salt, but it's likely that they'll either reword the mechanic, change it substantially or drop entirely.<br /> <br /> Anyway just visualize like those movies where the vampire heals wounds in seconds and are already pristine and fine. When the juice to do that is over, you're too screwed for damage to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T19:30:40-07:00","id":1563393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563380#post1563380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it can't be worse, but would definitely take an extra effort to do so.<br /> <br /> The only splat I'd say that really manages to do inhuman evil outside the Evil Forces\u2122 of Baali, Wyrm and Nefandi is Changeling. Of all lines, the Fae are genuinely build to facilitate a player that does utterly despicable shit for reasons a human would not have an analogous drive.<br /> <br /> All the others aren't just human evils in the sense of being literary metaphors, the games literally rely thematically on their failings being entirely human despite their negation of such. It's just that the choice of first person narrator, while immersive, makes it kinda obtuse as you get the in-character evasive justification rather than the direct explanation of the themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To hear the Galliard Group describe it, the Fae are sociopathically concerned with their own personal needs and desires. They follow a <i>&quot;fuck you, got mine&quot;</i> attitude towards the rest of the world, which is only emphasized by the fact they're out here assimilating the souls of children in order to save themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563380#post1563380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Demon: the Fallen</b> is about how war fucks up a soldier, literally. The whole problem is Torment, and behind all the poetic descriptions it's &quot;just&quot; regular PTSD. The main conflict is about how those powerful spirits are trying to cope with good old trauma, with all the regular responses to trauma, including misanthropy, reliving, negation, dissociation, and even their own way of seeking therapy.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand, the Abyss was effectively a sensory deprivation chamber that the demons got tossed into.<br /> <br /> Based on real life studies, spending longer than 40 minutes inside one of those is considered to be inhumane torture, and can result in potentially life long damages. There's even an SCP focused on that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Demons have been locked in the Abyss for hundreds of thousands of years. The fact that they didn't immediately go ballistic upon their escape is a miracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T03:09:49-07:00","id":1563398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563344#post1563344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that what the game was trying to encode is not exactly intuitive to explain in its context, and frankly, they chose the words for it poorly.<br /> <br /> Humanity with a Hierarchy of Sins is a key part of the Gothic side of the game. Not as in Goth counterculture, but the original two waves of Gothic Horror literature in the 18th and 19th centuries.<br /> <br /> One central element of Gothic is a naturalistic take on morality. It's not moral in the sense we usually understand of socially accepted morals or individual beliefs, but rather the notion that the most fundamental moral principles are so basic and intuitive we can say they exist as a fact, even if we can't explain why.<br /> <br /> Killing is bad. Stealing is bad. Violence is bad. Nuance matters and circumstances change everything, but no one with a healthy mind will deny those basic ideas. The Romans were a warlike people, as by the way the modern US is, too, and many other nations. But if you asked a Roman, just as if you ask a US citizen, war is a necessary evil, not a good thing. So to Gothic the first point is this: Good and Evil are real, but not in the way we rationalize and rather in their basic principles.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't believe i missed that. It's been decades and that never clocked it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T04:41:33-07:00","id":1563404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563393#post1563393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To hear the Galliard Group describe it, the Fae are sociopathically concerned with their own personal needs and desires. They follow a <i>&quot;fuck you, got mine&quot;</i> attitude towards the rest of the world, which is only emphasized by the fact they're out here assimilating the souls of children in order to save themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From what I understand, the Abyss was effectively a sensory deprivation chamber that the demons got tossed into.<br /> <br /> Based on real life studies, spending longer than 40 minutes inside one of those is considered to be inhumane torture, and can result in potentially life long damages. There's even an SCP focused on that kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Demons have been locked in the Abyss for hundreds of thousands of years. The fact that they didn't immediately go ballistic upon their escape is a miracle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Galliard Group is full of their own shit. This description is as precise as saying Camarilla's focus is to promote philanthropy as a means to enforce Humanity and Werewolf is a game about running human slavery rings. This isn't a close enough description to even compare to the actual game.<br /> <br /> And yes, Demons are basically fucked royally in the head and that's about it. And many of them do immediately go full ballistic upon escape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563398#post1563398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe i missed that. It's been decades and that never clocked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest it took me literally study literature with two professors with extensive experience with Gothic Romance. When I say the game is obtuse about it, I mean it.<br /> <br /> Basically, from a literary standpoint I can today say VtM is serious about being Gothic Punk, it's very good at this in a very deep level. But I can also guarantee it's intellectual about it in a level that simply doesn't work for a fucking game, it overshoots when should have been accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:21:43-07:00","id":1563415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563404#post1563404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Galliard Group is full of their own shit. This description is as precise as saying Camarilla's focus is to promote philanthropy as a means to enforce Humanity and Werewolf is a game about running human slavery rings. This isn't a close enough description to even compare to the actual game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, their description does kind of fit with traditional fairy folk lore.<br /> <br /> Fey love to pull pranks that are incomprehensible to mortal minds.<br /> <br /> They have a very, very loose comprehension of how time is supposed to work, which can often destroy the lives of any mortals who find themselves crossing into their domain.<br /> <br /> When they make a promise or deal, they take the wording of such agreements in the most literal way possible. For example, a barren woman asks for a child, and they give her an infant who never ages.<br /> <br /> If you accept a gift or eat any food the Fae offer, you are contractually obligated to serve them for a year and a day.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the most minor slights against a high ranking Fae can result in your entire bloodline being cursed for generations, until one of you finally discovers a way to atone for whatever offense your ancestor committed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T09:43:43-07:00","id":1563418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563415#post1563415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, their description does kind of fit with traditional fairy folk lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avoiding garlic and running water also fits with traditional vampire lore, yet doesn't apply to VtM.<br /> <br /> I'm not talking Irish folklore. I'm talking CtD, a gameline within WoD. If you want to talk about British fairies, I think this may not be the right forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T11:26:13-07:00","id":1563422,"title":"","content":"Not for nothing but as far as what passes for canon goes, a variety of Fae in CtD have pitched in with Werewolves against BSDs and Mages against the Technocracy just fine at various points. There are entire noble houses whose dedicated/sworn purpose is monster hunting/protecting humanity besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T14:43:09-07:00","id":1563434,"title":"","content":"I so dreamed of a version 6 where the disciplines simply return on a scale of 1 to 10 like in the 20-year version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29148-elkantar","name":"Elkantar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29148_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T16:26:00-07:00","id":1563435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563422#post1563422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for nothing but as far as what passes for canon goes, a variety of Fae in CtD have pitched in with Werewolves against BSDs and Mages against the Technocracy just fine at various points. There are entire noble houses whose dedicated/sworn purpose is monster hunting/protecting humanity besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they do that because they care for humanity, or because saving the world correlates with saving themselves?<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you that the Fae were using Fianna kinfolk as vessels for their reincarnations, and when the Fianna asked them to stop so that they could produce more werewolves, they immediately broke off their alliance with them.<br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, their entire concept is anathema to everything the Fae embody. Of course they don't want them growing any more powerful, because it would be the death knell of their entire species.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, there are some noble houses who hunt monsters. But there is also a noble house that takes pride in being monsters (Balor), and a house who have to periodically destroy a mortal's capacity for creativity, just to prolong their accelerated life spans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T17:19:42-07:00","id":1563437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563422#post1563422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not for nothing but as far as what passes for canon goes, a variety of Fae in CtD have pitched in with Werewolves against BSDs and Mages against the Technocracy just fine at various points. There are entire noble houses whose dedicated/sworn purpose is monster hunting/protecting humanity besides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings literally interact with other splats and help in their problems way more frequently than any other. In their own gameline crossover is expected to be a thing at least some Fae in a city engage with regularly.<br /> <br /> You don't see them like that in other lines just because the damn WoD is not a unified setting and so the authors of other lines are not required to include in their books a splat they're not interested in writing about.<br /> <br /> Anyone saying Changelings are &quot;sociopathically concerned with their own personal needs and desires&quot; just never read the book and is talking made up shit without basic, cursory understanding of the game. That only confirms that this group isn't in any way, shape or form a minimally competent source of info about WoD. They're hallucinating more than ChatGPT in its worst days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkantar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563434#post1563434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I so dreamed of a version 6 where the disciplines simply return on a scale of 1 to 10 like in the 20-year version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't.<br /> <br /> This was a bad mechanic with badly designed sample powers in every single Legacy edition. It was horrible in 1st, remained horrible in 2nd, got slightly less horrible in Revised and in V20 it managed to be just really bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563435#post1563435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they do that because they care for humanity, or because saving the world correlates with saving themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former.<br /> <br /> Also this is not how they reincarnate, and this thing about breaking with the Fianna because of Kinfolk isn't in the books, and I know at least one confirmed occasion when the Galliard Group completely invented non existing lore, so I guess this was one of those.<br /> <br /> Regular Changelings reincarnate the same way anyone does. They get a whole new, randomly defined life after they die. It's not a change or exchange upon the human soul. The new child is a Changeling since conception.<br /> <br /> Arcadian Sidhe do the exchange thing, but not upon Kinfolk, I'm not sure they'd be able to if they tried. They send the original soul to Arcadia to live as a noble, or so they believe, and this is not something other Fae are totally ok with, there are many who want them to stop, and many Sidhe who did stop and underwent the ritual of the Changeling Way to enter the regular reincarnation cycle.<br /> <br /> Changelings have a huge variety of goals and motivations. They're living stories, they don't just require imagination to survive, they live it with their full being. A Changeling hero is just as heroic and selfish as it comes, and a villain just as despicable as it gets. You can start play with a character that literally eats children for breakfast for the lulz without any consequence, but you can also be a literal paladin that learns about the problems each splat deals with and swears an oath to protect Humanity against all the horrible servants of the Wyrm and other Big Evils, at risk to their immortal Fae souls, for no other reason than that being the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> If you want to know more, ask in good faith or go read the actual book, but stop insisting on an interpretation by vloggers that people who actually know the game are telling you to be wrong in no ambiguous terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T20:19:17-07:00","id":1563452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563437#post1563437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to know more, ask in good faith or go read the actual book, but stop insisting on an interpretation by vloggers that people who actually know the game are telling you to be wrong in no ambiguous terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't even mention the Galliard Group in that last comment, but you're right that I did get the info from them.<br /> <br /> However, telling me to read the books also sounds like it's in bad faith, when you consider these books charge upwards of 60 dollars... each, and there's about 2 decades worth of material I would need to sift through to get information that may not even be accurate, due to the unreliable narrator angle, and the fact the writers left the setting up to a 'multiple choice' interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T20:41:13-07:00","id":1563453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563435#post1563435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they do that because they care for humanity, or because saving the world correlates with saving themselves?<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you that the Fae were using Fianna kinfolk as vessels for their reincarnations, and when the Fianna asked them to stop so that they could produce more werewolves, they immediately broke off their alliance with them.<br /> <br /> As for the Technocracy, their entire concept is anathema to everything the Fae embody. Of course they don't want them growing any more powerful, because it would be the death knell of their entire species.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, there are some noble houses who hunt monsters. But there is also a noble house that takes pride in being monsters (Balor), and a house who have to periodically destroy a mortal's capacity for creativity, just to prolong their accelerated life spans.</div> </div> </div> </div>They did that because they care for humanity. That's the explicit reason in the game material. There are fae that hunt nightmare monsters that prey on humanity for no other reason than that they don't believe nightmare monsters should get to prey on humanity. And yes, some fae are decent, some fae are horrifyingly awful, some fae are some muddled in-between, as though they are a vast group with wildly varying goals, drives and identities that can't be reduced to a one note statement. I'm honestly not sure what you feel your point is thereby? Trying to define the Fae by their most explicitly malign groupings is the equivalent of saying the worst parts of whatever other gameline grouping define that grouping. Have you read any of the CtD material? <br /> <br /> Since we're talking about the Fianna, even in the revised era Fianna tribebook, the book that went hardest at &quot;whatever is said in the game Changeling the Dreaming, the Fae suck actually, you can trust my in character narration saying so&quot;, there's a Gwydion Sidhe who is being slowly metaphysically obliterated into nothing just to keep the oath they swore to guard the slumbering body of an ancient Fianna warrior. To pre empt a likely reply, you can break oaths in Changeling, as the entire existence of House Ailil demonstrates. It sucks and you'll suffer, but you can. Dude chose to be effed by the Sundering and the Shattering and is now on their way to be obliviated to stay true anyway. They never underwent the Changeling Way of any sort, Arcadian or otherwise, having locked themselves in before it even existed. They won't lose an incarnation to being undone. They'll just cease to exist. There are certainly of course fae who have a big ol laugh at garou expenses by contrast, but again, it's as though there are a variety of different types of these people, and not whatever it is that you are saying. I'm talking about the Changelings as depicted in the game Changeling the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where you or these people you are talking about are getting their material on the WoD Kithain, but it's coming off as extremely one sided and inaccurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T20:54:07-07:00","id":1563454,"title":"","content":"Just to elaborate, placing the dying sidhe lord thing in the full context of CtD, this also means the Gwydion in question managed to ignore the Dreaming backed authority of the High King demanding the Gwydion amongst others bodyguard his flight to Arcadia from the Shattering (the Gwydion later kill the High King for putting this on them in the first place, this being why there is no one high king of faerie, amongst other things. This isn't really related to anything at hand, it's just something I tend to note in &quot;What did you want the Gwydion to do?&quot; in CtD discussions). This is again in the one book that tries as hard as it can to go &quot;actually the fae are trash&quot;, and isn't even a CtD book.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, in their own actual gameline, Changelings explicitly vary wildly in motivation nature and actions on the world, from the shiny and heroic, to the unspeakably grotesque. That's not &quot;choose your own interpretation&quot;, that's &quot;in the game called Changeling the Dreaming, about Changelings, this is how they are objectively depicted&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T22:01:44-07:00","id":1563455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563453#post1563453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read any of the CtD material?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read C20.<br /> <br /> Big on mechanics, not so much on fluff.<br /> <br /> Though we're getting C6th edition now, so that might change in the future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T22:16:38-07:00","id":1563457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563452#post1563452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, telling me to read the books also sounds like it's in bad faith, when you consider these books charge upwards of 60 dollars... each, and there's about 2 decades worth of material I would need to sift through to get information that may not even be accurate, due to the unreliable narrator angle, and the fact the writers left the setting up to a 'multiple choice' interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I left the good faith question as an option rather than just go read the books and don't bother.<br /> <br /> By the way, all you need to get the basics is the core, and in this case the core C20 is, as usual, the best bang for your buck. But you do have better options if you can't buy than relying in considerably unreliable sources. I can't imagine how someone can believe that kind of stuff after actually reading this book.<br /> <br /> Asking here will give you several responses by unrelated readers, it's overall considerably more reliable. The old fandom WoD wiki is also a fairly reasonable place to look for, and it has a lot of lore. It has a few problems here and there, but is still a very good starting point, and no cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T22:26:46-07:00","id":1563458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563457#post1563457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way, all you need to get the basics is the core, and in this case the core C20 is, as usual, the best bang for your buck. But you do have better options if you can't buy than relying in considerably unreliable sources. I can't imagine how someone can believe that kind of stuff after actually reading this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very big book.<br /> <br /> Though I want to get something straight, and say that I do actually wish to learn more about Changeling. It's one of the game lines I'm most curious to delve more into.<br /> <br /> Along with Demon and Mage; so hearing that 6th edition is going to tackle Changeling and Mage first, before considering any other splats has me excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-24T23:43:02-07:00","id":1563459,"title":"","content":"<b>Please Ignore:</b> Removed the video link to Black Lodge Games' review, because he drops the R word in the video.<br /> <br /> Didn't know that at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-25-2026, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T03:03:44-07:00","id":1563460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563452#post1563452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't even mention the Galliard Group in that last comment, but you're right that I did get the info from them.<br /> <br /> However, telling me to read the books also sounds like it's in bad faith, when you consider these books charge upwards of 60 dollars... each, and there's about 2 decades worth of material I would need to sift through to get information that may not even be accurate, due to the unreliable narrator angle, and the fact the writers left the setting up to a 'multiple choice' interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>E-books. Save your budget, save your shelf space. Also, the details are accurate in that they actually came from the books as written and aren't from someone online filling in details from sources unknown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Please Ignore:</b> Removed the video link to Black Lodge Games' review, because he drops the R word in the video.<br /> <br /> Didn't know that at the time. </div> </div> </div>BLG is also pretty hypocritical in that they hate V5 and think that &quot;millennials ruined it&quot; when it was clearly written by much the same kind of Gen-X one true wayers that they are, in reference to their &quot;How you should play&quot; V:tM video wherein they state that if you're not playing it like a mafia game you're doing it wrong. This is, of course, over and above their typical &quot;I hate woke!&quot; BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T06:31:02-07:00","id":1563461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563460#post1563460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> E-books. Save your budget, save your shelf space. Also, the details are accurate in that they actually came from the books as written and aren't from someone online filling in details from sources unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've taken to buying the PDF's now, instead of physical copies off DriveThru, after two of their books started to fall apart on me. Pages coming disconnected from the spine. It's great that there's a site I can easily acquire RPG books, but their printing quality is not that great.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563460#post1563460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BLG is also pretty hypocritical in that they hate V5 and think that &quot;millennials ruined it&quot; when it was clearly written by much the same kind of Gen-X one true wayers that they are, in reference to their &quot;How you should play&quot; V:tM video wherein they state that if you're not playing it like a mafia game you're doing it wrong. This is, of course, over and above their typical &quot;I hate woke!&quot; BS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought they were a fairly popular gaming channel, alongside Critical Roll.<br /> <br /> As for the mafia simulator analogy, I've actually seen a fair bit of reviewers describe Masquerade as such.<br /> <br /> While I can see the themes present in what they are referring to, I personally like to take a different approach to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T07:29:39-07:00","id":1563462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563461#post1563461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've taken to buying the PDF's now, instead of physical copies off DriveThru, after two of their books started to fall apart on me. Pages coming disconnected from the spine. It's great that there's a site I can easily acquire RPG books, but their printing quality is not that great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only had my EX3 core POD come apart on me, but my main issue with POD is the same as its appeal - it's a book, which in the case of the phat, phat EX3 books, means it's going to take a lot of space up, when even the new-ish bookshelf I have is rather full.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I thought they were a fairly popular gaming channel, alongside Critical Roll. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that anyone is &quot;alongside&quot; CR. It's really in a league of its own, thanks to its perfect storm of popular voice actors, when they started, and memetic &quot;goofing off&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the mafia simulator analogy, I've actually seen a fair bit of reviewers describe Masquerade as such.<br /> <br /> While I can see the themes present in what they are referring to, I personally like to take a different approach to the game. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's the Catch 22 - they wag their fingers at people who do take different approaches. Again, just like the first group that PDX had in charge of V:tM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T10:31:47-07:00","id":1563466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563458#post1563458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a very big book.<br /> <br /> Though I want to get something straight, and say that I do actually wish to learn more about Changeling. It's one of the game lines I'm most curious to delve more into.<br /> <br /> Along with Demon and Mage; so hearing that 6th edition is going to tackle Changeling and Mage first, before considering any other splats has me excited.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very good setting, despite low popularity among fans of other lines. I'm also cautiously excited with 6th Ed doing it.<br /> <br /> Demon is my favorite, only line that dethroned VtM in my preference. But it has kinks to work, as should be expected from anything in WoD that only got one edition, and a rushed one at that.<br /> <br /> What I'd say is key to get Changeling is that the Fae are more focused on being themselves than with survival. Their main, maybe only law, is to be larger than life, in a world that punishes this in several ways as it is still the WoD.<br /> <br /> You also have very little in the form of social bans. It's the only gameline where you're not punished in any way for immoral behavior. The vampires need Humanity or Paths, Demons are under Torment, Werewolves must follow the Litany and Mages have a whole war over ideals going on, etc. Changelings face no pressure from rules of social norms to behave within a given moral parameter, only Banality saying that whatever you do, do with fanfare.<br /> <br /> But that cuts in all directions, so what puts evil Fae in check is that no one will stop good ones from messing with their schemes and possibly their faces. Be a jerk and someone will take on themselves to make you miserable, and their society will just watch while eating popcorn.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation doesn't protect your memories and personality, either, so while they treat it as true immortality and so death isn't a big deal, they actually for all purposes die like a normal person and what comes later is only the same character in a very lose sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T10:38:15-07:00","id":1563467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563466#post1563466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reincarnation doesn't protect your memories and personality, either, so while they treat it as true immortality and so death isn't a big deal, they actually for all purposes die like a normal person and what comes later is only the same character in a very lose sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially true, according to C20.<br /> <br /> The deeper your venture into the Dreaming, the more memories of your past lives begin to resurface. It's not that death causes a full memory wipe, so much as the memories you had become dormant.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Dauntain, who are explicitly stated to be incurable. Even if you slay them, they will reincarnate as another Dauntain, so the only way to deal with them is cold iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T10:40:55-07:00","id":1563468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563466#post1563466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reincarnation doesn't protect your memories and personality, either, so while they treat it as true immortality and so death isn't a big deal, they actually for all purposes die like a normal person and what comes later is only the same character in a very lose sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, hey, some of us like to put a lot of points in Remembrance ;p<br /> <br /> Me, I'm some of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T10:45:24-07:00","id":1563469,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Greatewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkneere a fairly popular gaming channel, alongside Critical Roll.<br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> CR apart, popular channels usually are so due to a presentation that moves people in some way rather than information quality.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately choosing quality sources really is a hard skill to learn, and the best starting point is usually to take suggestions on sources from people you think to know their stuff.<br /> <br /> For WoD in general, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness\" target=\"_blank\">the old White Wolf Wiki</a> is overall a solid start for lore.<br /> <br /> With Changeling the only bad part is that the bulk of it are gigantic copy paste book sections rather than explanations, it's a horrible way to write in a wiki, but beggars can't be choosers. It gets the work done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T10:55:34-07:00","id":1563471,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that having memories from a past life isn't the same as being a perfect continuation of it.<br /> <br /> Even with topped Remembrance and in the Fae Dreaming you're still short from being literally a resurrection, rather than a life that remembers having been many others before.<br /> <br /> Put another way, it's like regular IRL experience with the concept. The important part isn't how much you can recover your memories, but that for the most part they're, well, a past life.<br /> <br /> It's in contrast to some descriptions that seem to think Changelings are just possessing spirits or something like that, jumping bodies but still retaining full consciousness and memory through the process, like how Demons actually do because <i><b>they</b></i> are, in fact, possessor spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T11:08:57-07:00","id":1563472,"title":"","content":"I mean to dive into the metaphysics of it more seriously for a moment, your original faerie life, as it were, is still &quot;you&quot; in a lot of ways, it just gets filtered through an ongoing cycle of other experiences. Your fae soul is still in there somewhere, but it's perspectives get shifted around and even transformed by new lifetimes. It doesn't mean you're a possessing spirit (barring the Arcadian way, and even there some Arcadians opted to be born into the world as babies and grow up naturally, as it were), it just means there is a certain quality of you carrying through lifetimes.<br /> <br /> I see it less as Michael Moorcock's Eternal Champion, who very much are vastly different people expressing the same incarnation in ways that can have little to do with each other, and more in some cases like the Doctor, for whom there is always a certain underlying measure of &quot;Doctor&quot;-ness, if you will, that still flavours the different ways they end up engaging with and processing the world.<br /> <br /> We see in the material that the rare person who does come into their full original selves/memories (whether by actually making it back to Arcadia, or Siochain-ing, or what have you) has something of a coming into the fullness of themselves, as it were. It's not the equivalent of reading a book about someone else's life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T12:54:08-07:00","id":1563475,"title":"","content":"What are the metaphysics of reincarnation if not an essential &quot;you&quot; continuing through lives while being filtered by new experiences?<br /> <br /> This filtering, though, is still an indelible reality, and in Changeling it is extremely important due to the theme of balancing mundane needs with living fantasy. To ignore your current life in its particular expression, relationships, obligations and roles is to neglect a part of you and court with Bedlam.<br /> <br /> Here I have to counter your description also on grounds of diversity. Changelings come in all levels of Remembrance and relationships with this past. You're insisting in a reading that exist in the game, but is far from a rule. I don't think either the Eternal Champion or the Doctor are good representations of reincarnation as they are quite particular takes for quite particular stories, and both use premises uncommon for stories or beliefs about reincarnation.<br /> <br /> Changeling is open ended about this. No one is wrong in playing their character very differently from what you're describing, just as you're not wrong in playing like that. A Changeling that is very different each life is valid, as is one that even upon remembering rejects the person they were previously. One is almost exactly the same each life even without memories, other is reinventing themselves every time based more on the person they grew to become rather than the fairy they were hundreds of years ago.<br /> <br /> For every Time Lord Changeling there is also an Eternal Champion, yet the vast majority is anything in between and beyond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T12:57:58-07:00","id":1563476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563475#post1563475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here I have to counter your description also on grounds of diversity. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd note I said &quot;in some cases&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-25T14:01:31-07:00","id":1563479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563475#post1563475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the metaphysics of reincarnation if not an essential &quot;you&quot; continuing through lives while being filtered by new experiences?<br /> <br /> This filtering, though, is still an indelible reality, and in Changeling it is extremely important due to the theme of balancing mundane needs with living fantasy. To ignore your current life in its particular expression, relationships, obligations and roles is to neglect a part of you and court with Bedlam.<br /> <br /> Here I have to counter your description also on grounds of diversity. Changelings come in all levels of Remembrance and relationships with this past. You're insisting in a reading that exist in the game, but is far from a rule. I don't think either the Eternal Champion or the Doctor are good representations of reincarnation as they are quite particular takes for quite particular stories, and both use premises uncommon for stories or beliefs about reincarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>While memory wipes are common theme among reincarnations, it's not necessarily an automatic process.<br /> <br /> The Greeks, for example, believed you had to drink water from one of the Underworld's rivers (forgot its name) in order to erase the memories before a soul was reborn.<br /> <br /> And while I know very little about Hindu / Buddhist beliefs outside from basic pop culture, I believe there was a plot hook somewhere in 1st edition of Scion, where the antagonist was trying to seize control of the cosmic wheel, so that the Titans would be free to reincarnate their followers into key positions of influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T12:41:57-07:00","id":1563504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563466#post1563466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a very good setting, despite low popularity among fans of other lines. I'm also cautiously excited with 6th Ed doing it.<br /> <br /> Demon is my favorite, only line that dethroned VtM in my preference. But it has kinks to work, as should be expected from anything in WoD that only got one edition, and a rushed one at that.<br /> <br /> What I'd say is key to get Changeling is that the Fae are more focused on being themselves than with survival. Their main, maybe only law, is to be larger than life, in a world that punishes this in several ways as it is still the WoD.<br /> <br /> You also have very little in the form of social bans. It's the only gameline where you're not punished in any way for immoral behavior. The vampires need Humanity or Paths, Demons are under Torment, Werewolves must follow the Litany and Mages have a whole war over ideals going on, etc. Changelings face no pressure from rules of social norms to behave within a given moral parameter, only Banality saying that whatever you do, do with fanfare.<br /> <br /> But that cuts in all directions, so what puts evil Fae in check is that no one will stop good ones from messing with their schemes and possibly their faces. Be a jerk and someone will take on themselves to make you miserable, and their society will just watch while eating popcorn.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation doesn't protect your memories and personality, either, so while they treat it as true immortality and so death isn't a big deal, they actually for all purposes die like a normal person and what comes later is only the same character in a very lose sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>DtF my beloved. I'd change the fluff a bunch these days before applying them to any campaign I run granted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T15:24:11-07:00","id":1563511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563504#post1563504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DtF my beloved. I'd change the fluff a bunch these days before applying them to any campaign I run granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make a single change, but that would be the assumption that they are from the reality they inhabit now.<br /> <br /> They come from a world they created, and this world is analogous to the one the game goes in, but Hell is linked to infinite possible realities and knowing which is which is both impossible and, from their perspective, irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-26T17:15:15-07:00","id":1563516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563511#post1563511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd make a single change, but that would be the assumption that they are from the reality they inhabit now.<br /> <br /> They come from a world they created, and this world is analogous to the one the game goes in, but Hell is linked to infinite possible realities and knowing which is which is both impossible and, from their perspective, irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how I'd do it, but valid and fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T04:07:41-07:00","id":1563561,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in some ways, the fae soul is recycled like an Avatar. It carries memories and maybe even personality, but it's only ever a component in the final being (except in the case of Arcadian sidhe). It merges with a human soul, but the imbalance of Glamour and Banality means the human soul tends to win out more often (and wins for good in the end, if the changeling survives long enough to finally be Undone).<br /> <br /> As for demons, I like the idea that the world(s) they built might no longer exist, or have evolved in their absence, and so they're emerging into a world that often seems vastly different (but with just enough details that they are convinced it's the same world). Re-reading <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i> recently, this seems even more likely, given that the book seems to seed ideas picked up on in later books.<br /> <br /> E.g., Yahweh and Lucifer are both described as Elohim/Shining Ones, and as &quot;brothers&quot;. This implies the different Godheads are all manifestations of the One (also called the Ancient One or the greater YHVH in the book). The seraphim, cherubim and &quot;daemoni&quot; are said to be some of Yahweh's servants, although it's also fair to assume his siblings have similar servants of their own. As Yahweh's brother, Lucifer is his peer, so stands above such angels (though he's still below Yahweh, who is the &quot;Firstborn&quot;).<br /> <br /> Each Shining One (and we're given the names of various deities here) creates their own garden, and after Lilith gives the fruit to Eve (who gives it to Adam), they all have a terrible argument (maybe a war?) that rains down stones from the sky (fallen angels?). When the Shining Ones finally leave to retire to their own worlds, they leave three angels behind to protect humans on Earth (possibly the Ministers/Aralu/surviving trio of angels from DTF).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T08:22:25-07:00","id":1563567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563461#post1563461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought they were a fairly popular gaming channel, alongside Critical Roll.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Current year argument, we should know that popularity does not equal reliable source. With people getting their news from Facebook and Twitter, Rogan being one of the biggest podcasters and most popular political streamers being Asmongold and Hasan Piker we know better than to equate popularity with reliability. <br /> <br /> Also happy to see that Demon gets some love. VtM will be always special as the game that introduced me to WoD but Demon is da bomb. Granted, it has limited official material out there and since it never had a revision or even Anniversary treatment it lacks certain depth and has plethora of creases that needs smoothing but the core concept is powerful. Shame that OP will never have a chance to do D20. Even more because of the memes ;P <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T11:48:41-07:00","id":1563576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563561#post1563561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for demons, I like the idea that the world(s) they built might no longer exist, or have evolved in their absence, and so they're emerging into a world that often seems vastly different (but with just enough details that they are convinced it's the same world). Re-reading <i>Revelations of the Dark Mother</i> recently, this seems even more likely, given that the book seems to seed ideas picked up on in later books.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem isn't just them being right about the world, but their existence confirming the origin of the world to some extent.<br /> <br /> Whether you place other gods as lies or Elohim doesn't change the cosmological statement on which religious narrative is closer to the truth. I despise this, and it has always been my bigger problem with the line.<br /> <br /> I don't want a game that says one mythology to be closer to the truth than other, especially one whose doctrine requires cultural and philosophical erasure.<br /> <br /> So it annoying other game lines to me is minor. It doesn't have to cater to them and vice versa. It establishing a world where some significant aspects of Christianity are objectively true and other world creation myths are objectively wrong is major.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T16:21:52-07:00","id":1563580,"title":"","content":"<b>God damn it, the site ate my post again:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563567#post1563567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Current year argument, we should know that popularity does not equal reliable source. With people getting their news from Facebook and Twitter, Rogan being one of the biggest podcasters and most popular political streamers being Asmongold and Hasan Piker we know better than to equate popularity with reliability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hasan obliterated his reputation the moment he got caught shocking his dog on live stream, and then did everything he could think of to try and publicly deny it. Even other streamers have openly made jokes at his expense while he was making guest appearances on their shows.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> That problem comes down to the concept of the <i>&quot;one true faith.&quot;</i> You've got who knows how many religions scattered all throughout the world who have their own creation myths and genesis stories about how the world was created.<br /> <br /> If these stories end up contradicting each other, then it is only rational to assume that some of them must be false. Only one of these explanations can be genuinely true; or perhaps none of them are, and all religions are just flailing around in a desperate bid to come up with an explanation.<br /> <br /> <b>We do not know the truth, one way or the other</b>, but unless the WoD introduces the concept of a metaphysical multiverse (like Scion did), they had to pick a narrative to go with, and the Abrahamic faiths is what we got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T17:11:25-07:00","id":1563581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563580#post1563580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If these stories end up contradicting each other, then it is only rational to assume that some of them must be false. Only one of these explanations can be genuinely true; or perhaps none of them are, and all religions are just flailing around in a desperate bid to come up with an explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only accurate if you assume we're dealing with a single universe. If we're dealing with a multiverse then all of them can be true without any issues because the Void is infinite in the truest sense of the word. It'd just mean our particular universe was made much later through some form of cooperation between pantheons.<br /> <br /> And we do know that the Void exists in oWoD since it's what lies beyond the prison the fallen got chucked into.<br /> <br /> The Void in this case being the primordial true nothingness everything came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T17:19:55-07:00","id":1563582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563581#post1563581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only accurate if you assume we're dealing with a single universe. If we're dealing with a multiverse then all of them can be true without any issues because the Void is infinite in the truest sense of the word. It'd just mean our particular universe was made much later through some form of cooperation between pantheons.<br /> <br /> And we do know that the Void exists in oWoD since it's what lies beyond the prison the fallen got chucked into.<br /> <br /> The Void in this case being the primordial true nothingness everything came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and that's why I edited my post to suggest a metaphysical multiverse, like what we got with Scion, in which the mortal world is a cosmic singularity where all the different cosmologies fuse into one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, that's not how World of Darkness has presented itself. I know very, very little about Wraith; but what I do know, is that the &quot;shining realms&quot; that were supposed to be the heavenly afterlives for a bunch of different faiths were corrupted and turned into prisons by tyrannical ghost kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-28T20:46:31-07:00","id":1563585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563580#post1563580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>God damn it, the site ate my post again:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hasan obliterated his reputation the moment he got caught shocking his dog on live stream, and then did everything he could think of to try and publicly deny it. Even other streamers have openly made jokes at his expense while he was making guest appearances on their shows.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> That problem comes down to the concept of the <i>&quot;one true faith.&quot;</i> You've got who knows how many religions scattered all throughout the world who have their own creation myths and genesis stories about how the world was created.<br /> <br /> If these stories end up contradicting each other, then it is only rational to assume that some of them must be false. Only one of these explanations can be genuinely true; or perhaps none of them are, and all religions are just flailing around in a desperate bid to come up with an explanation.<br /> <br /> <b>We do not know the truth, one way or the other</b>, but unless the WoD introduces the concept of a metaphysical multiverse (like Scion did), they had to pick a narrative to go with, and the Abrahamic faiths is what we got.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been copying to avoid this problem. Took me some time to her used to and not forget, but I'm managing to make it into a habit.<br /> <br /> You misunderstood the problem completely. It is obvious that religions have distinct creation myths, that should go without saying. I don't even think calling them collectively as genesis stories is the best approach as only one uses this name, with a reason for such.<br /> <br /> Also avoid talking about &quot;Abrahamic Faiths&quot;. As related as they are, most of the time this term is erroneously used to imply a universality that don't really exist among them, often attributing to all of them and aspect that isn't common, it's just being regular eurocentrism.<br /> <br /> But on the setting: the problem is it deciding on how the origin of the world happened. This was unnecessary and tasteless. As much as some fans have a hard time wrapping their minds around the concept of &quot;Noddism is a myth, not setting lore&quot;, VtM has no defined lore on origin of the world or vampires, and other lines follow suit. Some facts are laid or have evidence, but overall it's in the air what actually happened.<br /> <br /> Only Demon makes one version objectively true or close to it, and state several religions to be objectively false and demonic in nature at their origins. This being a problem should have been a no brainer even at the time, it's both shallow and offensive to several degrees.<br /> <br /> They didn't had to take a narrative if they had put the effort to make it undefined, which the idea of a metaphysical multiverse is precisely the first thing everyone and their dog said ever since that would have been a simple solution.<br /> <br /> From all possible narratives, the Catholic origin myth (because that's not, by any stretch of the word, generic &quot;Abrahamic&quot;) isn't just a casual choice, it's a socially relevant one that exists within a long history of conflict and erasure in which a certain majority regularly uses neutral language or victimization discourse to deflect guilt from how they've consistently committed abuses and persecution. Their victims do not see this choice lightly, nor should they.<br /> <br /> My proposal was precisely in line with the multiverse approach, anyway. I think being Christian-adjacent without being confirmation is part of what makes Demon interesting, it just needs to stop confirming things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T01:22:38-07:00","id":1563591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563585#post1563585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also avoid talking about &quot;Abrahamic Faiths&quot;. As related as they are, most of the time this term is erroneously used to imply a universality that don't really exist among them, often attributing to all of them and aspect that isn't common, it's just being regular eurocentrism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't mean anything by it. I was under the impression that it was the official term for the collective Christianity / Judiasm / Islam.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know they clash even within themselves. There's about 20,000 different sects of Christianity alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563585#post1563585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But on the setting: the problem is it deciding on how the origin of the world happened. This was unnecessary and tasteless. As much as some fans have a hard time wrapping their minds around the concept of &quot;Noddism is a myth, not setting lore&quot;, VtM has no defined lore on origin of the world or vampires, and other lines follow suit. Some facts are laid or have evidence, but overall it's in the air what actually happened.<br /> <br /> Only Demon makes one version objectively true or close to it, and state several religions to be objectively false and demonic in nature at their origins. This being a problem should have been a no brainer even at the time, it's both shallow and offensive to several degrees.<br /> <br /> They didn't had to take a narrative if they had put the effort to make it undefined, which the idea of a metaphysical multiverse is precisely the first thing everyone and their dog said ever since that would have been a simple solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could also have worked, if they went with the angle of presenting each of the different splats as being their own self contained universes, like what Chronicles did.<br /> <br /> But instead, they decided to mash them all together into one shared setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T04:33:07-07:00","id":1563592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563591#post1563591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't mean anything by it. I was under the impression that it was the official term for the collective Christianity / Judiasm / Islam.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know they clash even within themselves. There's about 20,000 different sects of Christianity alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It could also have worked, if they went with the angle of presenting each of the different splats as being their own self contained universes, like what Chronicles did.<br /> <br /> But instead, they decided to mash them all together into one shared setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>O didn't said you meant, just that it was better not to use it.<br /> <br /> The term do refers to all religions derived from Judaism, but it's frequently misused even if not on purpose, and you did just that: the genesis narrative assumed in DtF isn't Abrahamic in general, it's specifically Catholic in origin.<br /> <br /> Abrahamic refers to what is common about those religions. When you use it, it's implied that the thing being talked about is mostly alike across them. You shouldn't use for things you are not sure to be that common, but most of the time people use it it's a person of Christian upbringing talking about stuff that only applies to the little they know about as if it were basic theology across all those religions.<br /> <br /> Lucifer is not Abrahamic. The narrative of the Fall is not Abrahamic. Demons on general are not Abrahamic. Those and several other parts of the narrative commonly know in countries of Catholic or post Reformation majority are not Abrahamic, but Catholic developments post Nicea, some even only taking form by the end of the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> Presenting the settings as independent would not have solved shit, and it is precisely what WoD did, have you even read what I wrote? The people who think the WoD is a unified setting and CoD isn't either didn't read the books or are delusional, because it's the opposite.<br /> <br /> 1. Demon's problem is elevating one religion to be closer to the truth in its setting. The rest of the WoD has no bearing on this, most players I know of DtF find it the most distasteful part of the game regardless.<br /> <br /> 2. WoD always said gamelines are independent despite the similar system and references. The books sometimes lean more or less in the idea of One WoD and it was tried sometimes, but in the end didn't work and the official stance still is that each line is an independent setting. The fans sometimes have a hard time accepting this, that's their problem, though.<br /> <br /> 3. CoD is exactly the opposite. It avoids making many hard statements about the setting in general, but since the first book it's ostensibly a shared setting. That's written in the books and it goes to great lengths to ensure everyone is compatible and avoid contradictions, so no line harms the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T09:36:24-07:00","id":1563598,"title":"","content":"Circling back to the new rules regarding Diablerie for a moment.<br /> <br /> While I agree that being able to lower your generation regardless of who your victim was is extremely broken and should be changed, I would say that they should keep the part about being able to reduce your generation by multiple steps, if your victim is further removed from you.<br /> <br /> I know that this was technically already an option in previous editions, based on the ST's discretion, but diablerie is supposed to be a tempting shortcut to power for younger, more impatient vampires. Being able to jump from 10th to 7th generation in a single act of cannibalism would further emphasize this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T11:45:30-07:00","id":1563602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563582#post1563582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, and that's why I edited my post to suggest a metaphysical multiverse, like what we got with Scion, in which the mortal world is a cosmic singularity where all the different cosmologies fuse into one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly, that's not how World of Darkness has presented itself. I know very, very little about Wraith; but what I do know, is that the &quot;shining realms&quot; that were supposed to be the heavenly afterlives for a bunch of different faiths were corrupted and turned into prisons by tyrannical ghost kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't comment much on Wraith since I've not played it and wasn't really a fan of the fluff I read. What I can say though is that I go with the mindset that all polytheistic religions are true and that our universe is just one amongst countless others. It makes for a much better grounding. I'll stop here though before I start to rant about the crimes of christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T17:05:00-07:00","id":1563607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563598#post1563598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circling back to the new rules regarding Diablerie for a moment.<br /> <br /> While I agree that being able to lower your generation regardless of who your victim was is extremely broken and should be changed, I would say that they should keep the part about being able to reduce your generation by multiple steps, if your victim is further removed from you.<br /> <br /> I know that this was technically already an option in previous editions, based on the ST's discretion, but diablerie is supposed to be a tempting shortcut to power for younger, more impatient vampires. Being able to jump from 10th to 7th generation in a single act of cannibalism would further emphasize this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it was even intentional, probably they just overlooked the text. It's surprisingly easy to do this with pieces you're so used to that you take for granted.<br /> <br /> On the jumps, I think they could do even better than that. I always found them too small even when given as an option. What I would change, though, is that I'd make the Generation Jump be linked to age rather than just Generation. It's an old lore element that Blood Potency didn't capture well, but should still be there.<br /> <br /> Divide the age of the victim by the age of the diablerist, round down always. The result is how many steps the act can reduce Generation at once. The a chart of minimum difference: 100 years for -2, 200 for -3, 400 for -4, 800 for -5, 1.600 for -6, 3.200 for -7, 6.400 for -8. That way a Neonate can drop from 13th Gen to 5th if they somehow Diablerize one of the oldest Methuselah around, while Elders doing it on each other get more moderate benefits even if they have a big difference. A 300 years vampire would have to Diablerize a victim at least 600 years old to improve more than one step.<br /> <br /> But I would remove any XP gain or other more permanent benefit or penalty from Diablerie. I came to greatly appreciate in previous editions the idea that this is about closeness to Caine and potential, but not realization. I'm a staunch defender of the idea that a starting vampire is made with the same dots regardless of their Generation, and only age and actual experience will let them realize their potential.<br /> <br /> So, Caine himself embraced you 5 years ago? Congratulations, you're 2nd Generation and has 3 dots in Clan Disciplines to choose. Maybe 4 or 5 if you really go all in for it. You may have a greater Blood Pool or something, and Surging Blood will give you more temporary dots, but that's about it, don't feel too cocky, you're just a Neonate like any other. Likewise, Diablerie isn't a path to power, just to Generation. You may get to treat one of your victim's Disciplines as in-clan, but that's the most I'd allow.<br /> <br /> What I'd reintroduce with clearer rules is some temporary benefits. Maybe a bonus to use the Disciplines and skills of the victim for a couple days. You could get from drinking Elder Blood, but have a slightly greater benefit and duration with Diablerie. Even then, without paying XP to keep the benefits, they're lost after a while.<br /> <br /> Those temporary benefits could exist in some level to Diablerie of weaker Vampires. We do have a problem in which the game has a theme of diablerist elders and Diablerie causing quite a strong addiction without any effect. I think that giving something for it would deliver this theme better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T17:32:48-07:00","id":1563609,"title":"","content":"You know it would be really funny if partly the reason why the SI might be less prominent in v6, where during the intrem between editions they saw the Elders gathered in the middle east by the beckoning as a great opportunity to lunch a decapitation strike and it goes catastrophically badly. <br /> To the piont that many of they experienced personnel was killed off or worse turned which constitute a massive loss of material for all the orgs that made up the SI. To the piont the piont that most mundane government that backed the decided its not worth it anymore and subsequently cut funding forcing massive downscaling of operations and some orgs decided to outright leaving the SI.<br /> <br /> If thats actually the case then I suspect H6 would have an influx of bitter ex-SI veterans who survived the middle east as a major plot line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T21:43:56-07:00","id":1563612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563609#post1563609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know it would be really funny if partly the reason why the SI might be less prominent in v6, where during the intrem between editions they saw the Elders gathered in the middle east by the beckoning as a great opportunity to lunch a decapitation strike and it goes catastrophically badly.<br /> To the piont that many of they experienced personnel was killed off or worse turned which constitute a massive loss of material for all the orgs that made up the SI. To the piont the piont that most mundane government that backed the decided its not worth it anymore and subsequently cut funding forcing massive downscaling of operations and some orgs decided to outright leaving the SI.<br /> <br /> If thats actually the case then I suspect H6 would have an influx of bitter ex-SI veterans who survived the middle east as a major plot line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> First, &quot;the Middle East&quot; has a total area at least similar to Europe in conservative definitions, or way larger if you use the &quot;Middle East = Muslim Majority&quot; definition that's sadly common today.<br /> <br /> So &quot;gathered at the Middle East&quot; is a measure of how geographically illiterate the authors of V5 were, be better than that instead of talking about it as if it were really a concentration of any sort.<br /> <br /> Nations from the area are also not likely to greenlight such stupidity, and that's important. Contrary to popular ignorance, the US doesn't simply invades anywhere they want in the area, places like Afghanistan and Iraq saw military intervention in no small part because US allies in the region baked it. A blank &quot;Middle East&quot; operation is politically and strategically a bad joke.<br /> <br /> They're also professional hunters, not brainless morons, they only work by engaging vampires in direct infantry style confrontation when the author is too eager to give players easy fights to think through how big of a plot hole this kind of idiocy is.<br /> <br /> As much as I dislike most SI plots in V5, trying to get &quot;revenge&quot; by making them incompetent morons will only worsen the setting for cheap instant satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Like how they didn't it or not, there's a reason why the SI's greatest victories involved literally obscene amounts of heavy ordnance. Anyone who engages supernatural creatures directly in a battlefield is either a Werewolf or a soon to be dead lunatic. As a mortal, I wouldn't call this moron a hunter.<br /> <br /> It's also already the case that the SI is loosing its funding as time goes on, anyway. Attrition is way worse for a government than a single bad decision, the SI is a constant drain of resources with little to no return to the people in power. It is less likely to fall because of a single failure than because it is the first thing to suffer cuts in budget every quarter to make room for more politically beneficial projects.<br /> <br /> Overall such a plot relies too much on ignoring the actual reality of a densely populated area and its societies, which is certainly in line with Paradox previous works but nothing I'd find fun in any way. I'd much prefer something including actual research on how the world works rather than stupid Europe/US exceptionalism failing because of supernatural powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T22:38:01-07:00","id":1563613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563607#post1563607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would remove any XP gain or other more permanent benefit or penalty from Diablerie. I came to greatly appreciate in previous editions the idea that this is about closeness to Caine and potential, but not realization. I'm a staunch defender of the idea that a starting vampire is made with the same dots regardless of their Generation, and only age and actual experience will let them realize their potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>From an RPG power gaming stand point, I get where you're coming from. But from a story driven narrative, I have to disagree.<br /> <br /> If the only benefit to diablerie was that you reduce your generation, I doubt it would be nearly as taboo as it currently is.<br /> <br /> The elders don't fear diablerists because they consider it a reprehensible act. They fear diablerists, because they have spent centuries, even millennia cultivating their power, only for some bright eyed, young upstart to swoop in out of nowhere and topple everything they've built within a week.<br /> <br /> Diablerie has been describe as absorbing the victim's knowledge / memories, along with their abilities. So it makes sense that they would get some free EXP to spend on improving their abilities, as they assimilate the victim's skill into their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> I approve of this take. The SI got too over confident hunting down Neonates and Ancilla. It's about time somebody knocked some sense into them with a hard reality check!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T22:58:04-07:00","id":1563615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563612#post1563612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're also professional hunters, not brainless morons, they only work by engaging vampires in direct infantry style confrontation when the author is too eager to give players easy fights to think through how big of a plot hole this kind of idiocy is.<br /> <br /> As much as I dislike most SI plots in V5, trying to get &quot;revenge&quot; by making them incompetent morons will only worsen the setting for cheap instant satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Like how they didn't it or not, there's a reason why the SI's greatest victories involved literally obscene amounts of heavy ordnance. Anyone who engages supernatural creatures directly in a battlefield is either a Werewolf or a soon to be dead lunatic. As a mortal, I wouldn't call this moron a hunter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> According to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jtfNuDObCxM\" target=\"_blank\">Alfabusa's explanation</a> of the setting: <i>&quot;most Hunters are staggeringly ignorant about what they're up against.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> An opinion which Beckett himself seems to share, when you question him about the Society of Leopold.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;They for the most part know very little about us. But they know how to stalk and kill us.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T23:31:19-07:00","id":1563619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563613#post1563613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an RPG power gaming stand point, I get where you're coming from. But from a story driven narrative, I have to disagree.<br /> <br /> If the only benefit to diablerie was that you reduce your generation, I doubt it would be nearly as taboo as it currently is.<br /> <br /> The elders don't fear diablerists because they consider it a reprehensible act. They fear diablerists, because they have spent centuries, even millennia cultivating their power, only for some bright eyed, young upstart to swoop in out of nowhere and topple everything they've built within a week.<br /> <br /> Diablerie has been describe as absorbing the victim's knowledge / memories, along with their abilities. So it makes sense that they would get some free EXP to spend on improving their abilities, as they assimilate the victim's skill into their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diablerie only included absorbing memories very recently. Originally it was only Generation, with hints of something else being there more as a reason to believe it's absorbing the soul.<br /> <br /> All Legacy core books are clear that Generation is the only consistent and permanent benefit. It can give further benefits temporarily at the ST's discretion, but they're inconsistent and no one knows for sure what they mean.<br /> <br /> For a long time the only book to propose more benefits and even give rules was Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, and while many liked the idea it was only hinted as a possibility later, not as the standard setting.<br /> <br /> Elders fearing diablerists because of how long they cultivated power is utter bullshit. They fear diablerists because they're targets and kind of don't want to die, much less with the risk of the soul getting some horrible fate in the process. Other than that they already try to topple each other regularly.<br /> <br /> For every single edition Diablerie was a taboo because it causes Final Death and absorbs the soul. The benefits weren't the reason for it to be taboo, but for it to be a risk.<br /> <br /> Generation in VtM is otherwise fixed. You can't reduce it any other way (well, there's Marduk's Throat, but that's another story), so its benefits can only be attained with Diablerie. That's all you need and the game worked with this for 27 years. Diablerie won't give you XP or dots, but will increase Blood Pool, Blood/Turn and traits caps, which immediately raises what you can get with Blood Surge.<br /> <br /> You also don't get where I'm coming from because my point is not about power gaming. A story driven narrative can involve different themes and goals, the ones I find interesting are incompatible with Diablerie giving more permanent benefits. You're free to prefer other takes, but don't assume I'm ignoring story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-29T23:40:05-07:00","id":1563620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563615#post1563615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;They for the most part know very little about us. But they know how to stalk and kill us.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Who's this random YouTuber and why should I care about his opinion?<br /> <br /> More importantly, my point relies completely on the part about knowing how to stalk and kill vampires, I don't know why's that such a hard concept to grasp.<br /> <br /> If someone thinks they can face vampires in a direct confrontation, by definition they don't know the most basic of how to stalk and kill a vampire, or how to stalk and kill anything by the way, since even against other humans you avoid that until you have a ton of intel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T00:20:32-07:00","id":1563622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563620#post1563620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's this random YouTuber and why should I care about his opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a random youtuber... it's a quote from Beckett... the iconic, canon character from Bloodlines 1?<br /> <br /> The guy who (in character) wrote Beckett's Jyhad Diary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T03:14:54-07:00","id":1563628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563622#post1563622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a random youtuber... it's a quote from Beckett... the iconic, canon character from Bloodlines 1?<br /> <br /> The guy who (in character) wrote Beckett's Jyhad Diary?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about Alfabusa, Becket I know, as I know the quote. I just find it grating people insisting on interpreting ignorance as imbecility when doing exactly the one thing the quote say hunters are good at doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T05:06:47-07:00","id":1563631,"title":"","content":"Brief aside about the SI, but them losing funding becomes a lot more likely given Current Events.<br /> <br /> The US is currently undergoing a Fascist takeover. And part of that was bringing in a dipshit billionaire South African emerald mine heir to &quot;reduce government waste&quot;. Musk's &quot;DOGE&quot; proceeded to basically dismantle large parts of government infrastructure, cutting funding and getting rid of programs that, fun fact, actually SAVE citizens money. Because Fascists are stupid, and so is the &quot;Small Government&quot; fixation.<br /> <br /> All that to say, if any part of the US government was liable to be hit by funding cuts, it would be the Second Inquisition. It's probable the twenty-somethings hired for DOGE weren't even aware of what the SI parts of the government DOES, only that it's a lot of funding going something. Those same chuds took a shotgun approach to everything else, so it's no stretch they downsized SI funding Just Because.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it's highly possible the Camarilla dominated DOGE personnel to specifically target that cashflow, to hobble their enemies. Whatever supernatural force protects the President from supernatural attack probably isn't protecting DOGE guys who arguably had no official position within the government. But I'm also not terribly committed to going as far as to say anyone rigged it from the outside. Fascists ARE just that incompetent, and they ARE that pointlessly indiscriminate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T07:05:25-07:00","id":1563633,"title":"","content":"I partially disagree. Fascists wouldn't be half the problem they are if everything they did was just incompetence.<br /> <br /> Musk is a longtime student of US federal flow of money. Most of his fortune was built on the understanding of subsidies, how to make the government give you money for nothing, plus how to evade taxes and inspections so abuses of the system aren't formally identified.<br /> <br /> Less than half of DOGE's cuts were to random programs. Most of them were calculated to give his companies even more room to rig the system unimpeded.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T07:31:05-07:00","id":1563634,"title":"","content":"That said:<br /> <br /> 1. The SI itself is a fascist structure. A secret intelligence and military coalition to watch and execute people without oversight isn't a good and democratic institution just because their targets happen to be &quot;evil monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2. It's also a senseless waste of money in the way it works. It dedicates inordinate amounts of resources to operations whose targets are ill defined and benefits not calculated.<br /> <br /> 3. What actually motivates the investment in the SI by governments isn't common good, but removing challenges to authority. Vampires are a parallel power running independently and that is a problem for them.<br /> <br /> 4. Effective ways of depowering this kind of clandestine institutions circle around finding out the administrative vacuums they occupy, which usually means identifying where regular state failed its actual functions, and correcting this absence. Not just putting lethal force in the streets. The SI is just lethal force in the streets. As far as &quot;solutions&quot; go, it's a bigger threat to the safety of the population than the monsters they're trying to fight.<br /> <br /> 5. None of this is new. Since <i>Hunters Hunted</i> in the setting the groups that now comprise the SI and haven't been thoroughly modified by the authors at Paradox were clearly either corrupt or fanatics who would frequently become more of a threat to the Kine than the Kindred. PCs facing the Society of Leopold aren't monsters being hunted by virtuous heroes. They're just victims of the ire of self-righteous fascists that happen to include the undead in the list of social groups they hate indiscriminately.<br /> <br /> 6. Also the SI is an international phenomenon. The US alone going bananas isn't the SI losing anything. Your country may be the richest in the world, it's still only one and the SI would be able to survive without much issue if the problem was only in the US. At least in this the V5 authors had the basic competence to know that most of the participants of the SI wouldn't be part of the US machine or trust it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T11:53:43-07:00","id":1563639,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the SI shouldn't even need government support, when they were originally a religious organization. Meaning they were spread all over the globe.<br /> <br /> The Catholics alone rake in billions of dollars.<br /> <br /> The idea that they were struggling with the supernatural because politicians weren't on board is just absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 08-30-2026, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T13:41:40-07:00","id":1563641,"title":"","content":"My big issue with the SI was weakly written. Even the whole &quot;but they're facist&quot; hit the hero issue of beast the primordial.<br /> <br /> I tended to do a rewrite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T13:52:02-07:00","id":1563643,"title":"","content":"You know I won't be surprised if white wolf caves and allows the SI to be playable in H6 like how the Sabbat are slated to be playable for v6.,Or being a ex member is a lifeparth at the very least.<br /> <br /> If si is playable then I guess they take a cue from how the playable technocracy Is portrayed and have it's dysfunctional internal politics be as big a threat to the players as the monsters they hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-30-2026, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:09:09-07:00","id":1563644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563643#post1563643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I won't be surprised if white wolf caves and allows the SI to be playable in H6 like how the Sabbat are slated to be playable for v6.,Or being a ex member is a lifeparth at the very least.<br /> <br /> If si is playable then I guess they take a cue from how the playable technocracy Is portrayed and have it's dysfunctional internal politics be as big a threat to the players as the monsters they hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Technocracy was originally presented as being a monolithic entity that were strictly antagonistic? But people really liked the hyper science aesthetic they had going on, so they introduced more nuance possibilities to them in later editions of the game.<br /> <br /> Still, though, the New World Order is just another alias for the Illuminati, and they are canonically part of the reason why Hitler became a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:36:26-07:00","id":1563646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563644#post1563644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Technocracy was originally presented as being a monolithic entity that were strictly antagonistic? But people really liked the hyper science aesthetic they had going on, so they introduced more nuance possibilities to them in later editions of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know pretty much. Kinda like how the SI was portrayed in 5e funny enough...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:49:46-07:00","id":1563647,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a little upset that Werewolf and Hunter are being discontinued, according to the FAQ, but I\u2019m really excited by the possibility of getting 6th edition versions of Mage, Changeling and Vampire the Dark Ages. Especially the Dark Ages: I was really impressed that the D&amp;D crossover Bound by Blood was set in Scotland circa 700 CE, a time period which I don\u2019t think has ever been explored before in Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:50:22-07:00","id":1563648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563646#post1563646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know pretty much. Kinda like how the SI was portrayed in 5e funny enough...</div> </div> </div> </div>IF they are going to introduce the SI as playable, doing so when they are on the decline in relevancy would be the optimal time to do so.<br /> <br /> V5 pretty much gave them the run of the show, making it difficult to come up with ideas on how they would struggle to resolve any conflicts. The SI moving into the city was pretty much treated like a <i>&quot;we are so fucked&quot;</i> event in every live play session of the game I've witnessed.<br /> <br /> But if the setting has changed so that their funding is cut, and their influence is diminished, that's a different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T14:54:02-07:00","id":1563649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563647#post1563647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a little upset that Werewolf and Hunter are being discontinued, according to the FAQ, but I\u2019m really excited by the possibility of getting 6th edition versions of Mage, Changeling and Vampire the Dark Ages. Especially the Dark Ages: I was really impressed that the D&amp;D crossover Bound by Blood was set in Scotland circa 700 CE, a time period which I don\u2019t think has ever been explored before in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sad Fera Noises*<br /> <br /> Gaia is truly dead, it seems.<br /> <br /> But yes, new edition of Mage and Changeling are welcomed news!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T15:05:39-07:00","id":1563650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563647#post1563647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a little upset that Werewolf and Hunter are being discontinued, according to the FAQ, but I\u2019m really excited by the possibility of getting 6th edition versions of Mage, Changeling and Vampire the Dark Ages. Especially the Dark Ages: I was really impressed that the D&amp;D crossover Bound by Blood was set in Scotland circa 700 CE, a time period which I don\u2019t think has ever been explored before in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the faq said whitewolf is focusing on mage and changing while hunter and werewolf still going to contune publishing the 5e lines in the short term while the possibility of both of the lines getting a 6e is left open ended.<br /> <br /> Edit: granted werewolf and hunter being discontinued won't surprise me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-30-2026, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T19:21:07-07:00","id":1563661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563639#post1563639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the SI shouldn't even need government support, when they were originally a religious organization. Meaning they were spread all over the globe.<br /> <br /> The Catholics alone rake in billions of dollars.<br /> <br /> The idea that they were struggling with the supernatural because politicians weren't on board is just absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't understood what the SI is, at all.<br /> <br /> Hunter organizations have been a part of the game since 1st edition, as Hunters Hunted is one of the few sourcebooks from before 2nd edition, and one still immensely influential.<br /> <br /> The Society of Leopold, the Arcanum, the many government agencies that have some inkling on the existence of the supernatural, those are all old lore and yes, have existed no problem for a long time. They are not what the Second Inquisition is.<br /> <br /> What defines the Second Inquisition is their coordination and collective official resources from the mid 2000s onward.<br /> <br /> It's a movement where disparate organizations from around the world started to work together and with formal approval, authority and access to government databases et vigilance systems. It isn't any of those independent organizations.<br /> <br /> So government support is one of the things that literally define the Second Inquisition. To stay they don't need it is like saying the UN doesn't need the participation of countries.<br /> <br /> All the fucking SI plot is about how this change in support made those hunters severely more dangerous. Without it they keep existing as they always had, just in an extremely limited capacity that is exactly how they existed in the game in every other edition.<br /> <br /> On a side note, the Society of Leopold is only a small semiofficial part of the Catholic Church. They don't have unrestricted access to church resources or even complete church approval. That Church is an immense and diverse institution full of internal conflicts and politics, and plenty of members will be severely against the SoL if they learn about their existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563641#post1563641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My big issue with the SI was weakly written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, undoubtedly.<br /> <br /> But the fascism angle was a given. They're a reference to post-2001 'War on Terror' increase in government vigilance especially in the US, but also Europe, which was from the beginning very fascist adjacent and a big influence in the current fascist rise across the globe.<br /> <br /> And again, it's old. Most of the organizations that form the SI were fascist adjacent since the debut in Hunters Hunted, the exception being the orgs that didn't had shit to do with SI style hunting but get changed and lumped with them because Paradox can't understand the concept of diversity in a setting, as happened to the Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563647#post1563647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a little upset that Werewolf and Hunter are being discontinued,</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not.<br /> <br /> Nothing close to this was said.<br /> <br /> What was said was &quot;we're doing Mage and Changeling next&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563650#post1563650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure the faq said whitewolf is focusing on mage and changing while hunter and werewolf still going to contune publishing the 5e lines in the short term while the possibility of both of the lines getting a 6e is left open ended.<br /> <br /> Edit: granted werewolf and hunter being discontinued won't surprise me</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't said they're going to continue as 5e lines, but I do think this is a fair assumption, it seems like they're not slowing down the slight momentum they got with W5 and H5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T20:37:19-07:00","id":1563665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563661#post1563661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't understood what the SI is, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood it based on the information I observed by watching people actually play the game. Both in live play sessions (including the ones hosted by Jason), and the assortment of interactive novel games that have been released lately.<br /> <br /> The only game I've come across in the entirety of V5 that allowed you to actually fight back against the SI was Nightroad.<br /> <br /> Every other game in the franchise has presented me with the image that the Second Inquisition is some kind of bogeyman for the supernatural community, one that spells certain doom for anybody who comes within their crosshairs.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> Yes, Hunters have existed for a long time, I am aware of this. But those Hunters were The Imbued; men and women endowed with divine powers, like the ability to shoot holy fire from their eye. They weren't on the same level as a proper supernatural, but they at least had something to balance out the playing field.<br /> <br /> Then V5 chose to get rid of the Imbued entirely, leaving us with ordinary men and women, who have little more to go on than tons of guns, and True Faith.<br /> <br /> True Faith, which was supposed to have become increasingly RARE in the modern nights, as the Technocratic paradigm continued to expand its influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T21:23:38-07:00","id":1563669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563665#post1563665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Hunters have existed for a long time, I am aware of this. But those Hunters were The Imbued;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Imbued were introduced to the game in 1999 as a recent phenomenon those aware of were struggling to comprehend. The groups that form the SI were introduced in 1992 as diverse organizations that existed sometimes for hundreds, even thousands of years, some of them being present in Dark Ages.<br /> <br /> Literally the books presented the Society of Leopold, the Arcanum and three US federal agencies as hunter groups still in 1st edition, and would expand the list several times in the following years. At no point they were the SI.<br /> <br /> Also literally V5 defines the Second Inquisition as the government backed coalition between those groups, which is what made them more dangerous than ever before. It is, again, what defines the SI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-30T22:17:40-07:00","id":1563671,"title":"","content":"Well on the subject of fascists is that there's nothing preventing them from actually turning against each other at the slightest provocation, especially when things turns against them l like the nazis during the end of the war and the current bout of MAGA infighting. So I suspect that the American SI being hit by the (NOT) DOGE act like <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\">Bluecho</a></b> suggested is plausible.<br /> <br /> Hell I think W6 should also put a focause on infighting between factions the cult, either to give them more character (and maybe have the more more moderate factions as player charcters) or at least an easy excuse to exclude as the main threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-31-2026, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T01:42:03-07:00","id":1563675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563641#post1563641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the whole &quot;but they're facist&quot; hit the hero issue of beast the primordial.<br /> <br /> I tended to do a rewrite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they kind of are. With the exception of Vampires, none of the other splats are objectively malicious towards humanity's existence.<br /> <br /> Vampires need humans as a food source, but the other splats use them more like an energy battery at worst. Even the Werewolves created a law that forbids the consumption of human flesh.<br /> <br /> That means it is theoretically possible to strike an accord with these creatures, and achieve some level of coexistence, if both sides were willing to come to the negotiating table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T04:04:21-07:00","id":1563677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563665#post1563665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understood it based on the information I observed by watching people actually play the game. Both in live play sessions (including the ones hosted by Jason), and the assortment of interactive novel games that have been released lately.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was already discussed around this forums but you do not base your knowledge about the game world on watching a game. The only thing that you can understand this way is HOW A GIVEN STORYTELLER interprets the game world. It might be very close or very far from the descriptions but it's not them. <br /> <br /> Also, for the nth time - games, novels or whatever adaptations of WoD on are just interpretations the same way actual plays are. They are interpreting the setting canon and are not it.<br /> <br /> As for supernaturals being or not &quot;objectively malicious&quot; I think we misunderstand words here. <br /> <br /> First, vampires are not &quot;objectively&quot; malicious. Often they are even not malicious at all. When a Nosferatu kills a homeless person while frenzying he did not do it out of malice. Vampires prey on humanity for survival. <br /> <br /> Second, other splats are not &quot;intentionally malicious&quot; towards humanity? What the fuck was Impregium then? Did werewolves just one day said: Oops, we wanted the best for humanity and somehow the genocide happened. Is Technocracy controlling the masses out of the goodness of their hearts? <br /> <br /> The gist what I am saying is this: vampires are not malicious by definition and the other splats are not &quot;using (Humanity) as battery at worst&quot;. Every game has examples of their splat individuals doing most heinous shit and some examples of individuals doing bad shit by accident or good thing on purpose. <br /> <br /> Stop watching YT and start reading books if you want to argue about the TTRPG setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T04:34:32-07:00","id":1563680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563661#post1563661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, undoubtedly.<br /> <br /> But the fascism angle was a given. They're a reference to post-2001 'War on Terror' increase in government vigilance especially in the US, but also Europe, which was from the beginning very fascist adjacent and a big influence in the current fascist rise across the globe.<br /> <br /> And again, it's old. Most of the organizations that form the SI were fascist adjacent since the debut in Hunters Hunted, the exception being the orgs that didn't had shit to do with SI style hunting but get changed and lumped with them because Paradox can't understand the concept of diversity in a setting, as happened to the Arcanum.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's more authoritarianism than fascism, but that's probably quibbling given that I broadly agree with the comparison.<br /> <br /> For me, part of the problem is that the moral ambiguity of the War on Terror doesn't translate especially well into VtM when the &quot;terrorists&quot; are vampires. A lot of the real-world critique depends on innocent people being subjected to surveillance, detention and violence by institutions vastly more powerful than they are. That becomes considerably muddier when the target is a population of supernatural predators who routinely murder, enslave and manipulate human beings. This is worse in 5th were the more sympathetic traits were filled off.<br /> <br /> I also think making practically every organisation involved in hunting vampires ultimately fascist- or authoritarian-adjacent is reductive, questionable and, frankly, not very interesting. Different institutions should arrive at vampire hunting for different reasons and behave differently once they're involved. Paradox's tendency to flatten disparate organisations into the Second Inquisition compounds that problem rather than solving it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T05:00:48-07:00","id":1563681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563680#post1563680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, part of the problem is that the moral ambiguity of the War on Terror doesn't translate especially well into VtM when the &quot;terrorists&quot; are vampires. A lot of the real-world critique depends on innocent people being subjected to surveillance, detention and violence by institutions vastly more powerful than they are. That becomes considerably muddier when the target is a population of supernatural predators who routinely murder, enslave and manipulate human beings. This is worse in 5th were the more sympathetic traits were filled off.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I suspect that the writers would adopt something along the lines of Ranbow 6 with focus on tacticool gears to make it slightly distinct from the technocracy for the SI for H6 if it comes out.<br /> <br /> Also I still suspect that they're weakened due to botching a major operation in the middle east if only to parallel amercia retreat in 2016.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-31-2026, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T05:20:02-07:00","id":1563682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563680#post1563680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it's more authoritarianism than fascism, but that's probably quibbling given that I broadly agree with the comparison.<br /> <br /> For me, part of the problem is that the moral ambiguity of the War on Terror doesn't translate especially well into VtM when the &quot;terrorists&quot; are vampires. A lot of the real-world critique depends on innocent people being subjected to surveillance, detention and violence by institutions vastly more powerful than they are. That becomes considerably muddier when the target is a population of supernatural predators who routinely murder, enslave and manipulate human beings. This is worse in 5th were the more sympathetic traits were filled off.<br /> <br /> I also think making practically every organisation involved in hunting vampires ultimately fascist- or authoritarian-adjacent is reductive, questionable and, frankly, not very interesting. Different institutions should arrive at vampire hunting for different reasons and behave differently once they're involved. Paradox's tendency to flatten disparate organisations into the Second Inquisition compounds that problem rather than solving it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like to run mass surveillance as its own quiet conflict. Mass surveillance and digital infrastructure is pursued by many, SI, the Technocratic Union, the Camarilla, World Governments, the Virtual Adepts, and some Pentex subsidiaries, for many reasons (Camarilla needs to control it so they can subvert it). Usually they end up fighting over it. It's a neat source of potential plot lines.<br /> <br /> Like to run the SI as it's own flavor of vampire hunters.<br /> <br /> Independents: Experienced ones work in small teams with makeshift equipment. Hits you on the street, fights you for a round, then runs. Pretty hardcore. May sneak up on you. Inexperienced ones are just normal people who has breached the masquerade.<br /> Society of Leopold: Classic militant catholic fanatics. Though in a recent thread I made a more moderate version of them as well. But it's a strong archetype.<br /> SI: I like to have them use kindred against kindred. Have them recruit kindred and ghouls as defectors. Agents get to have vitae syringes. A kindred plants people in a local institution, oh there's the SI. It's fun because they can just troll kindred by acting like kindred. Also stalking, the SI is good for just stalking. It's not just that they spy on you, it's that they start map the city. It's a different kind of threat. You need to explain why they don't just torrent their info across the entire faction though, but the explanation doesn't actually need to be that good. <br /> <br /> It's a rewrite though, it's not superdeep hasn't done much with them in game.<br /> <br /> They could really have used an entrance into the setting with a little less brute force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T05:48:25-07:00","id":1563683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563677#post1563677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was already discussed around this forums but you do not base your knowledge about the game world on watching a game. The only thing that you can understand this way is HOW A GIVEN STORYTELLER interprets the game world. It might be very close or very far from the descriptions but it's not them.<br /> <br /> Also, for the nth time - games, novels or whatever adaptations of WoD on are just interpretations the same way actual plays are. They are interpreting the setting canon and are not it.<br /> <br /> As for supernaturals being or not &quot;objectively malicious&quot; I think we misunderstand words here.<br /> <br /> First, vampires are not &quot;objectively&quot; malicious. Often they are even not malicious at all. When a Nosferatu kills a homeless person while frenzying he did not do it out of malice. Vampires prey on humanity for survival.<br /> <br /> Second, other splats are not &quot;intentionally malicious&quot; towards humanity? What the fuck was Impregium then? Did werewolves just one day said: Oops, we wanted the best for humanity and somehow the genocide happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only people who don't think of the Impergium as ancient history are the Mokole. And that's because they spent tens of millions of years culling apes into anatomically modern humans on account of how they missed their old Drachid kin. There are probably modern, non-stone age killings to cite as evidence of malice, especially on account of how the Red Talons don't really try to convince others that they don't hate humans. They absolutely do and declare it proudly; they carry a grudge from the first extinctions caused by human hands to the present. It's their thing.<br /> <br /> But then, they don't live near human habitations, and accordingly, don't manipulate the laws so that lots of missing persons reports get ignored, or that John or Jane Does don't get looked into when they show up dead. That's all the vampires, trying to get easy access to blood. Between the two, the malice can be more relatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T07:58:50-07:00","id":1563688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563677#post1563677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was already discussed around this forums but you do not base your knowledge about the game world on watching a game. The only thing that you can understand this way is HOW A GIVEN STORYTELLER interprets the game world. It might be very close or very far from the descriptions but it's not them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an argument I've seen consistently used on these very forums, and I've got to say that it's irritating me when I see people use it.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Actions speak louder than words&quot;</i> as the saying goes; and in terms of actions, the impression I have from the game is the one that everybody who plays or makes the game seem to be in agreement with. Because that is the impression that is constantly being presented in World of Darkness products.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what the books have to say on the matter, that does not change the fact everybody who showcases the game is presenting me with contradictory information.<br /> <br /> So if I'm wrong about a subject, then everybody else is wrong too, because they're the ones I'm getting my information from.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> When I say objectively malicious, I mean there is no rational reason for why they should be allowed to continue to exist. Vampires are parasites, and not even the symbiotic kind either. All they do is take, without giving anything back to the community.<br /> <br /> <br /> The werewolves of today largely agree that the Impergium was a mistake, and have passed a series of laws to help them maintain at least some degree of connection to humanity, instead of writing it off as an existential threat. They are forbidden to eat humans, and are even expected to take humans as their mates. They have tried to reform themselves into something that can coexist alongside us, while simultaneously trying to prevent the end of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for not watching youtube, I think you and everybody else on the forums seem to have a serious misunderstanding about my sources:<br /> <br /> The people I get them from are reading directly from the books themselves. They not only use direct quotes, but also upload screenshots and discuss how the lore has existed across multiple generations.<br /> <br /> I do not comprehend why not personally having the book in front of me somehow invalidates their critic of the game, when the people I'm watching have already purchased the book and are reading through it for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:09:47-07:00","id":1563690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563671#post1563671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well on the subject of fascists is that there's nothing preventing them from actually turning against each other at the slightest provocation, especially when things turns against them l like the nazis during the end of the war and the current bout of MAGA infighting. So I suspect that the American SI being hit by the (NOT) DOGE act like <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\">Bluecho</a></b> suggested is plausible.<br /> <br /> Hell I think W6 should also put a focause on infighting between factions the cult, either to give them more character (and maybe have the more more moderate factions as player charcters) or at least an easy excuse to exclude as the main threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is plausible, it's even probable.<br /> <br /> My point was to address the surrounding argument, and to stress that the US is not what defines the SI, so DOGE alone doesn't mean much to it globally.<br /> <br /> But definitely, if the SI was having issues with its federal backing in the US, DOGE probably helped making it worse. And given how it was run, in my own tables I wouldn't even make it just have vampiric influence, I'd made it include Vampires directly.<br /> <br /> Elon Musk had those assholes literally mount camp in the offices they were defunding. This is basically saying to a vampire you'll give them a job, influence, haven and feeding grounds in one go, paid and protected by the White House.<br /> <br /> The only reason this won't happen in the books is that they won't reference current US politics so directly.<br /> <br /> W6 shouldn't do that with the Cult because it should drop the Cult entirely by the time it gets to do Werewolf. W5 should do that to the Cult in the still coming books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563675#post1563675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they kind of are. With the exception of Vampires, none of the other splats are objectively malicious towards humanity's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not exactly true.<br /> <br /> On one hand, vampires need human blood, not human suffering. There's no reason to exempt them from this reasoning and they're actually the splat most invested in society's wellbeing.<br /> <br /> But more importantly, all splats have plenty of reasons to harm humans on a regular basis. Not a requirement to, but still enough that a lot of them will do so even more than vampires.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are protectors of wild places and spirit realms, humanity is at best a secondary concern, frequently an acceptable sacrifice and sometimes seen as objectively deserving to be severely culled. A huge fucking lot of Gaian Garou are way more malicious toward humans than any Sabbat vampire.<br /> <br /> Mages are incapable of giving a fuck to regular law because of how strongly they feel about their personal beliefs and the power to bend reality itself. For this reason the Traditions still allow slavery, human sacrifices and all sorts of abuse against Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Changelings have no law against it, either, and kidnapping humans to toy with them is in fact a tradition. In the most benevolent Freeholds a human will only be asked to enjoy the party, but while those Fae don't mean harm it's important to be clear that they don't have the concept of consent well developed. And enough of them are not benevolent and will terrorize, torture, maim and even eat humans for fun.<br /> <br /> Demons can be very kind and truly value your wellbeing, possibly being among the splats I listed until now the one more probable to act with common sense and legitimately help the people around them if that's what they want. If that's not what they want, they can bargain for your faith in ways you won't recognize to know the danger, and once they get it you're in their pocket for the rest of your life as they can take their toll regardless of distance, dimensions or anything.<br /> <br /> Mummies and Wraiths are the ones I know the less about, still ghosts aren't usually a healthy company for the living. Mummies can be, so it is arguably the only splat without any reason to be regarded as a monster. IIRC from 1st and 2nd Ed Mummy, they have nothing to gain from harming humans, and that is actually unique.<br /> <br /> None of those change that most hunters are fascist adjacent, because that's not the point. The problem is the mindset needed for you to take up arms against a whole class of beings on the assumption that their nature makes them deserving of violent destruction without parole. Here their ignorance is relevant: those hunters don't know the splats are monstrous, they assume with enough certainty to seek genocide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563680#post1563680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's more authoritarianism than fascism, but that's probably quibbling given that I broadly agree with the comparison.<br /> <br /> For me, part of the problem is that the moral ambiguity of the War on Terror doesn't translate especially well into VtM when the &quot;terrorists&quot; are vampires. A lot of the real-world critique depends on innocent people being subjected to surveillance, detention and violence by institutions vastly more powerful than they are. That becomes considerably muddier when the target is a population of supernatural predators who routinely murder, enslave and manipulate human beings. This is worse in 5th were the more sympathetic traits were filled off.<br /> <br /> I also think making practically every organisation involved in hunting vampires ultimately fascist- or authoritarian-adjacent is reductive, questionable and, frankly, not very interesting. Different institutions should arrive at vampire hunting for different reasons and behave differently once they're involved. Paradox's tendency to flatten disparate organisations into the Second Inquisition compounds that problem rather than solving it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call the War on Terror thing fascist-adjacent because holistically it has way more to do with ultranationalistic protection of oligarchs and a demeaning narrative generalized against whole groups than &quot;mere&quot; authoritarianism entails. It is not fascism, but it is very close.<br /> <br /> And the ambiguity itself actually does translate well, it's the books that frequently fail showing how, especially V5. For one, you can't subject a hidden group to surveillance without subjecting everyone, the SI is not just watching vampires. And they've been described several times as willing to target the mortals around a vampire. It's easy to extrapolate from there that they are regularly targeting and harming innocents.<br /> <br /> You have then a group that surveil people all the time, will target anyone they want to get to their quarry, has been given free rein to do their shit without consequences and more often than not had already previous history of abuse against minorities. The books just neglect to talk about how much the SI presence probably makes life hell to the local population, but it is actually baked in their design that they do so.<br /> <br /> Now, the last part goes without saying. Some of the groups in it make total sense to be like fascists or even to be actual fascists, and the Society of Leopold is a prime example since their debut. But overall the V5 take of &quot;all Orgs are evil&quot; is pure, uninspired bullshit and quite frequently goes against the actual lore. Even in the governmental agencies, giving the same type of stance to the FBI and the CDC is depressingly idiotic.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563683#post1563683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only people who don't think of the Impergium as ancient history are the Mokole.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of Garou that voice support to going back to Impergium isn't small, and while it isn't happening now, mortals are still killed by Gaian werewolves regularly. Not always on purpose, but sometimes on purpose and never with much thought given to it.<br /> <br /> It's not the only kind of harm they cause, and if they don't manipulate things to get away with murder, that's be cause they have talens that vanish with corpses and other means to magic away with murder.<br /> <br /> You know more Garou lore than maybe anyone else in the forum, stop ignoring it just to make werewolves look better than vampires in every discussion. As far as malice against humans go, no splat is meaningfully more innocent with the possible exception of Mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:29:38-07:00","id":1563692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563688#post1563688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say objectively malicious, I mean there is no rational reason for why they should be allowed to continue to exist. Vampires are parasites, and not even the symbiotic kind either. All they do is take, without giving anything back to the community.<br /> <br /> <br /> The werewolves of today largely agree that the Impergium was a mistake, and have passed a series of laws to help them maintain at least some degree of connection to humanity, instead of writing it off as an existential threat. They are forbidden to eat humans, and are even expected to take humans as their mates. They have tried to reform themselves into something that can coexist alongside us, while simultaneously trying to prevent the end of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for not watching youtube, I think you and everybody else on the forums seem to have a serious misunderstanding about my sources:<br /> <br /> The people I get them from are reading directly from the books themselves. They not only use direct quotes, but also upload screenshots and discuss how the lore has existed across multiple generations.<br /> <br /> I do not comprehend why not personally having the book in front of me somehow invalidates their critic of the game, when the people I'm watching have already purchased the book and are reading through it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. That's not what malice means.<br /> <br /> 2. Thinking that a group should not be allowed to exist is one of the defining traits of Fascism.<br /> <br /> 3. We don't write off lions, mosquitoes and other animals that naturally harm humans as deserving obliteration. If you do, that's a you problem, and a very serious one.<br /> <br /> 4. Vampires are not parasites. They're micropredators. Biologically there's a big difference, and it's an important one because it means they actually can minimize harm.<br /> <br /> 5. They do minimize harm, and many do give back to the community. The reason it doesn't work better is because this is the World of Darkness and all societies in it are shittier than they have to.<br /> <br /> 6. The reason why you get so much of this criticism here is not, contrary to your belief, that you have terrible sources. It's that when a person who actually knows the setting better says something isn't quite like you think, you double down instead of reevaluating what you think you know.<br /> <br /> This has actually zero to do with your sources, they're just the obvious problem, but not the actual one. The actual problem is that you act with absolute certainty about your conclusions in situations where you're not just wrong, but wrong in a way that's so obvious to everyone else it hurts.<br /> <br /> We all get things wrong sometimes, and we all disagree on setting interpretation frequently. But you do with undeserved confidence while blurting some of the most obnoxious argument possible.<br /> <br /> Also you're far from the only one getting criticism around here, we all do as we are all passionate assholes to some degree and so we do say stupid bullshit sometimes, and we do distill undeserved vitriol other times against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:32:00-07:00","id":1563693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563690#post1563690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not exactly true.<br /> <br /> On one hand, vampires need human blood, not human suffering. There's no reason to exempt them from this reasoning and they're actually the splat most invested in society's wellbeing.<br /> <br /> But more importantly, all splats have plenty of reasons to harm humans on a regular basis. Not a requirement to, but still enough that a lot of them will do so even more than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant 'malicious' as in a universal application.<br /> <br /> It's true, there are some bad apples among each of the different splats, but there are also good ones too. I don't see Boggans, Trolls or the Akashic Brotherhood being the types of people who just randomly fuck with humanity for their amusement.<br /> <br /> I would also politely argue that vampires care about society. At best, they want society to remain stabilized, because that makes things easier on them. But in terms of active development, I suspect most vampires would prefer if we all went back to the dark ages, where they didn't need to try so hard to maintain their secrecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:39:43-07:00","id":1563696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563692#post1563692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Thinking that a group should not be allowed to exist is one of the defining traits of Fascism.<br /> <br /> 3. We don't write off lions, mosquitoes and other animals that naturally harm humans as deserving obliteration. If you do, that's a you problem, and a very serious one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the SI believe that every group other than humans should not be allowed to exist.<br /> <br /> Lions, no, but I'm certain that our species would breathe a collective sigh of relief if all the mosquitos, fleas and ticks of the world spontaneously teleported into the core of the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T08:55:42-07:00","id":1563697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563693#post1563693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I meant 'malicious' as in a universal application.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a wrong application, not a universal one, and even then would still be wrong.<br /> <br /> Vampires are individuals. They're perfectly capable of having the wellbeing of others at heart and that has been part of the point of the game since 1st edition. Their society isn't rotten because that's their nature, they're pressed into becoming assholes because their society is rotten.<br /> <br /> And the others are not different. This has nothing to do with bad apples, they're literally societies that accept harming humans as legitimate behavior.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can't eat human flesh because that's a source of taint. They couldn't during the Impergium, either. Still their laws allow killing humans with exquisite violence. Same for all the others. Garou, Mages, Fae, Demons, Wraith, they all accept killing, maiming, torturing and enslaving humans. Being against it is personal, not standard.<br /> <br /> Malice means the desire or intention to cause harm without need. By definition a predator is not malicious just for being a predator. If you do harm because you think you have to, that's precisely what malice isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T09:00:03-07:00","id":1563698,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> thanks! That\u2019s a relief. I like both Hunter and Werewolf, and I\u2019m glad to know they aren\u2019t being canceled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T09:27:16-07:00","id":1563699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563697#post1563697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a wrong application, not a universal one, and even then would still be wrong.<br /> <br /> Vampires are individuals. They're perfectly capable of having the wellbeing of others at heart and that has been part of the point of the game since 1st edition. Their society isn't rotten because that's their nature, they're pressed into becoming assholes because their society is rotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the constant backstabbing and vying for power was an intrinsic part of their curse?<br /> <br /> Just as Caine slew his brother, Abel, in a fit of jealousy, now he is damned to watch as all his descendants repeat the same crime over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T09:55:22-07:00","id":1563701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563699#post1563699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the constant backstabbing and vying for power was an intrinsic part of their curse?<br /> <br /> Just as Caine slew his brother, Abel, in a fit of jealousy, now he is damned to watch as all his descendants repeat the same crime over and over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of in Book of Nod:<br /> And then, through dread Uriel, cursed me, saying<br /> &quot;<b>Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness<br /> You will drink only blood<br /> You will eat only ashes<br /> You will be always as you were at death,<br /> Never dying, living on,<br /> You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> When Caine with some demonic help figured out how to Embrace? (interesting to point out when Uriel first cursed Caine, he not yet knew how to Embrace - that curse was technically means his <i>mortal</i> children will bear his curse too, Uriel's 2nd curse fine tuned the first to apply to the Vampires. The Book of Nod literally says: &quot;By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot; after detailing how Lilith helped him, implying Caine was not only a Ravenant but an infernalist, a proto-baali so to speak... but he never technically died. His curse is not vampirism, but immortality &quot;never dying, living on&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Caine, though powerful you are, and marked by God know you this: that any Childe you make will bear your curse, that any of your Progeny will forever walk in the Land of Nod, andfear flame and sun, drinking blood only and eating ashes only.<br /> And since they will carry their father's jealous seed, they will forever plot and fight amongst themselves.<br /> Doom not those of Adam's grandchildren who seek to walk in righteousness, Caine!<br /> Stay your dread Embrace!&quot;</b><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> The he give his own twist with the Generation, trying to &quot;solve it&quot; - spolier: it dodn't work<br /> <br /> It's in Erciyes Fragments, page 91:<br /> <br /> <b>Let our proud blood weaken with each generation,<br /> So that no childe can match its sire's strength<br /> Or rise up against those who came before.<br /> So shall you be bound to peace,<br /> Enslaved by weakness where force has failed.</b>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T10:58:12-07:00","id":1563702,"title":"","content":"Caine ensured that his progeny would further doom themselves by making them weaker with each embraced generation and that diablerie would be a powerful tool to improve themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T15:16:59-07:00","id":1563710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563697#post1563697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a wrong application, not a universal one, and even then would still be wrong.<br /> <br /> Vampires are individuals. They're perfectly capable of having the wellbeing of others at heart and that has been part of the point of the game since 1st edition. Their society isn't rotten because that's their nature, they're pressed into becoming assholes because their society is rotten.<br /> <br /> And the others are not different. This has nothing to do with bad apples, they're literally societies that accept harming humans as legitimate behavior.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can't eat human flesh because that's a source of taint. They couldn't during the Impergium, either. Still their laws allow killing humans with exquisite violence. Same for all the others. Garou, Mages, Fae, Demons, Wraith, they all accept killing, maiming, torturing and enslaving humans. Being against it is personal, not standard.<br /> <br /> Malice means the desire or intention to cause harm without need. By definition a predator is not malicious just for being a predator. If you do harm because you think you have to, that's precisely what malice isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to both agree with this take yet also want to very quickly note that the one universal death crime across the seelie, unseelie, and all kith in Changeling society is Rhapsody. Back when the Leanhaun used to have to Rhapsody to live/not be doomed to a slow agonizing death (I kind of find it a bummer that 20th got rid of that as far as the messed up tragedy of the underlying story there, along with the Leanhaun being one of the most terrifying secret apocalypse conspiracies in the WoD, though technically that second part could still be there, nothing actually notes it being junked) they created an intricate conspiracy just to hide that so that they didn't get gang murdered by everyone else. It's not even in a &quot;wink wink&quot; where you can loophole and scheme your way around diablerie every so often even outside of the Sabbat despite what a purported social horror it's supposed to be (the Camarilla in fact sometimes legally allows diablerie, and the Ventrue for instance have a 'reclaiming the blood' cultural thing they do sometimes to failure children).<br /> <br /> I honestly really like that as a thematic touch. For people looking for that somewhat off human perspective within the game &quot;oh, you ate that guy? Sure, that's fine, I'm sad you didn't save some for me. Oh, you <i>Rhapsodied</i> that guy? Dying time friendo.&quot; It's interesting to noodle philosophically about Fae for that being the great big unforgivable crime across their social and racial divides, even for the ones that otherwise love, you know, crime.<br /> <br /> Nothing really stops you from Rhapsodizing other than Fae society having just collectively decided that is the one thing even some of the worst of them will not tolerate being done to a human. It's not even a pragmatic thing, if it were, people wouldn't ravage due to its potential to create Autumn People and Dauntain. It's just, even the monsters looked at it and went &quot;this is the worst crime imaginable.&quot;<br /> <br /> edit: Before it gets noted for pedantry purposes, I'm comparing it to diablerie in a &quot;this is supposedly an almost universally condemned social horror that in fact can be worked into society at a semi frequent clip, you can even do it openly consequence free in the right conditions&quot;, I know diablerie is a vampire on vampire thing y'all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","user":"MarkK","date":". 08-31-2026, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T15:43:14-07:00","id":1563712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563710#post1563710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to both agree with this take yet also want to very quickly note that the one universal death crime across the seelie, unseelie, and all kith in Changeling society is Rhapsody. Back when the Leanhaun used to have to Rhapsody to live/not be doomed to a slow agonizing death (I kind of find it a bummer that 20th got rid of that as far as the messed up tragedy of the underlying story</div> </div> </div> </div>I just double checked my C20 to make sure about that, because I thought differently.<br /> <br /> Leanhaun still age by 1 year for every week they don't receive Glamour from humans, but the method in which they obtain that glamour affects how much the aging is reversed.<br /> <br /> Rhapsody reverses the aging by 5 years for each point of Glamour obtained.<br /> <br /> Ravaging does 1 year for each point.<br /> <br /> Reverie and Rapture does 1 year for every 5 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T15:43:56-07:00","id":1563713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563690#post1563690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The number of Garou that voice support to going back to Impergium isn't small</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bone Gnawers, CoGs, and Glass Walkers represent most Gaian Garou. None of them are angling for that; it is, in fact, pretty much antithetical to their patrons' vibes. The Shadow Lords may or may not be depending on what they think they can use it to motivate other Garou. The Fianna don't like a lot of modern tech, but they stick by their human kinfolk far too much to consider it, aside from the Mother's Fundamendalists. The Get of Fenris are obsessed with getting their Renown scoreboard higher and don't pay much attention to humans that aren't their kinfolk, though like the Fianna, they have That One Camp that tries to be fake Red Talons and pretty obviously doesn't reflect the overall tribe vibes. Both Elder Brother and Younger Brother largely abstained from it in the first place and don't really have agendas with a place for it. The Silver Fangs do double-think and view it as their glory days while also denouncing it rather hypocritically or at least with a great deal of cognitive dissonance. The Red Talons themselves only really have the Lodge of the Predator Kings and Winter Packs (covertly, in the latter case) to advocate for that sort of thing; the Dying Cubs kind of do but are also deeper freaks than the rest who hide from non-Dying cub tribemates.<br /> <br /> So, I'm going to say that it is, in fact, small, but will concede that they probably make an outsized problem for the Garou Nation relative to their numbers. It's a bunch of isolated septs, so they're probably very well dug in where they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and while it isn't happening now, mortals are still killed by Gaian werewolves regularly. </div> </div> </div>I did mention as much in the second sentence of my post. There are plenty of rampages more modern than the Neolithic to draw from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not the only kind of harm they cause, and if they don't manipulate things to get away with murder, that's be cause they have talens that vanish with corpses and other means to magic away with murder. </div> </div> </div>They can cover up the occasional rampage, but it has the potential to strain their relationship with a non-Talon sept's spirits. Vampires can spearhead wide-scale social oppression by grabbing hold of the minds of the rich and powerful, or even just having orthogonal aims like a scheme to ruin residential or public use areas that will make those rich and powerful folks even richer and more powerful while setting up prime hunting grounds for the vampire. This is a point that gets brought up constantly across both Vampire and Werewolf, where Garou can't steer human society worth a damn but Kindred find it pretty easy to club them with it. They'd almost have to, given that they're also walking drug factories that can turn blood into addictive substances used to control humans even if they don't have Dominate or Presence. Which they can easily sneak into food and drink, so that people end up addicted and/or mind controlled via a Blood Bond without even realizing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know more Garou lore than maybe anyone else in the forum, stop ignoring it just to make werewolves look better than vampires in every discussion. </div> </div> </div>It'd help if people brought up Wyrmcomers and European Garou going along with colonization, stone cold glory hounds trying to climb a sept's pecking order at any cost, or the modern context that frames them as terrorists. Or the Red Talons, specifically, in any time period where tribes exist.<br /> <br /> But for some reason, Impergium. Always, Impergium. An event that no contemporary player character Garou, their elders, or any but the most ancient ancestor-spirits is going to have participated in, ever, and which the contemporary Garou (so, the characters, their elders, and most ancestor-spirits) have likely been taught was a terrible betrayal of trust, reason, and nature.<br /> <br /> (Also, vampire lore is super extra and competes with werewolf lore for who's the worst, so it's really just playing to the writing of V:tM to let it wallow in mud and track it everywhere.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:00:03-07:00","id":1563714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563712#post1563712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just double checked my C20 to make sure about that, because I thought differently.<br /> <br /> Leanhaun still age by 1 year for every week they don't receive Glamour from humans, but the method in which they obtain that glamour affects how much the aging is reversed.<br /> <br /> Rhapsody reverses the aging by 5 years for each point of Glamour obtained.<br /> <br /> Ravaging does 1 year for each point.<br /> <br /> Reverie and Rapture does 1 year for every 5 points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can get by on other things besides Rhapsody as a Leanhaun as of 20th. I get why the change? It makes them a loooot more playable from a player perspective. I just found the previous Leanhaun far more evocative of a horror story, even if their mechanics were jank (they needed to do it far too frequently in previous. It's enough of a big deal to have to do it at all or face agonizing slow death)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T16:57:17-07:00","id":1563721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563699#post1563699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the constant backstabbing and vying for power was an intrinsic part of their curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't, and the books before V5 are all very clear about it.<br /> <br /> It's core to the game that vampiric society work like that's the case, but at the same time it is relevant because individual vampires are not. Humanity in particular represents this: you are facing consequences from behaving like a monster precisely because you're human, and if you lose this human side what remains isn't more vampire, but just ego-death.<br /> <br /> There may be something at a lather scale, but it is less about any given vampire and more about the context they live in making another lifestyle hard to pursue. Still, it's a point of the game that it is doable.<br /> <br /> How much this large scale tendency for being a society of monsters is fate is ambiguous, and the Book of Nod hints to that being the case, but the Book of Nod itself is dubious at best. Contrary to popular belief it is not meant to be fact, and has never been, its whole point is that vampires are willing to go to extremes for their beliefs about Nod without evidence of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563702#post1563702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine ensured that his progeny would further doom themselves by making them weaker with each embraced generation and that diablerie would be a powerful tool to improve themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, if you take the Book of Nod for granted, but here's the catch: this is indirect. It is not Vampires being cursed to be backstabbers, but rather being placed in a situation that makes the backstabbing more tempting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563713#post1563713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for some reason, Impergium. Always, Impergium. An event that no contemporary player character Garou, their elders, or any but the most ancient ancestor-spirits is going to have participated in, ever, and which the contemporary Garou (so, the characters, their elders, and most ancestor-spirits) have likely been taught was a terrible betrayal of trust, reason, and nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a valid point.<br /> <br /> Garou are overall monsters for humans, just like every other splat (Mages definitely included, every single faction of them), but the narratively low hanging fruit is always how tens of thousands of years ago their ancestors were genocidal assholes.<br /> <br /> It's like arguing Vampires based on the First City and Changelings on the Fomorians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563714#post1563714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you can get by on other things besides Rhapsody as a Leanhaun as of 20th. I get why the change? It makes them a loooot more playable from a player perspective. I just found the previous Leanhaun far more evocative of a horror story, even if their mechanics were jank (they needed to do it far too frequently in previous. It's enough of a big deal to have to do it at all or face agonizing slow death)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I get your point but the playability really changes a lot. As they were before it meant you wouldn't actually see it in play because no one would play a Leanhaun. Or, if they did, they were likely to quickly become the sole focus of the chronicle until killed.<br /> <br /> As it is now, IME it actually does give you the Rhapsody moments because it's sitting there, so tempting, and most PCs won't worry about the aging regularly enough to really avoid this temptation.<br /> <br /> When one does... Well, that's either a lot of work or an unhealthy amount of Ravaging, which isn't going to look that good on you. Not a capital crime, but Ravaging once or twice a month is definitely going to get you weird glances even from the Unseelie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:24:35-07:00","id":1563723,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563690#post1563690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W6 shouldn't do that with the Cult because it should drop the Cult entirely by the time it gets to do Werewolf. W5 should do that to the Cult in the still coming books.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree W6 shouldn't keep the cult. But that's for White Wolf to decide and if they do keep the I think adding factional infighting would add some much needed characterization to the cult. Especially if W6 makes an evil player option like Sabatt are slated to be in V6. Unless White wolf does a stupid and make the BSD the playable antagonist.<br /> <br /> On the subject of V6 I like to state again that clan frenzies should be carried over to W6 as tribe hauglosk.<br /> <br /> Again the hunter entertainment version of W5 expremented with this JF Sambrano's <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/jfsambrano/posts/glass-walkers-97379727?utm_medium=clipboard_copy&amp;utm_source=copyLink&amp;utm_campaign=postshare_fan&amp;utm_content=web_share\" target=\"_blank\">parton </a>has shown:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ghreena* of the Glass Walkers is the sterilization of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers flip the usual narrative of the Triat represented by Garou on its head, suggesting that the Wyld is at fault for driving the Weaver mad, which resulted in its machinations on the Wyrm. They will turn the tools of the Weaver on the Wyld with intent, building dams that provide &quot;clean energy&quot; while destroying ecosystems, genetically modifying crops to make them more durable against weather and pests, or creating low carbon footprint technologies which require mining operations that poison animals, people, and waterways. Many Glass Walkers favor terraforming the &quot;undesirable&quot; aspects of Gaia, such as deserts, by diverting waterways and creating solar panel fields which make these spaces more hospitable for humanity. They might claim that these actions are made out of a need for progress, but they seek out the sterilization of unstable qualities in the environment.\u200b<br /> <br /> *the cancelled edition term for hauglosk. </div> </div> </div>It would add depth to the condtion if W6 keeps it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:51:34-07:00","id":1563729,"title":"","content":"While Hauglosk as it is in W5 is horrible, I think a V6 style Tribal Hauglosk would be interesting even for the Legacy setting.<br /> <br /> As long as it is enough of a hard path as to mostly be just justification for NPCs being as they are, it's an interesting addition to Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The only point I'd make is this: Harano and Hauglosk can get rules, but they shouldn't be a constant threat or even remotely regular. What they should be is something a player will fall to only if they want in practice, and STs can use to justify dysfunctional characters with too much political power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T17:56:20-07:00","id":1563731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563729#post1563729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only point I'd make is this: Harano and Hauglosk can get rules, but they shouldn't be a constant threat or even remotely regular. What they should be is something a player will fall to only if they want in practice, and STs can use to justify dysfunctional characters with too much political power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed again V6 already did this with they revised humanity bar would fit Harano and Hauglosk in my opion. Even if it's a ripoff of Forsaken 2E harmony bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T18:15:43-07:00","id":1563733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563721#post1563721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I get your point but the playability really changes a lot. As they were before it meant you wouldn't actually see it in play because no one would play a Leanhaun. Or, if they did, they were likely to quickly become the sole focus of the chronicle until killed.<br /> <br /> As it is now, IME it actually does give you the Rhapsody moments because it's sitting there, so tempting, and most PCs won't worry about the aging regularly enough to really avoid this temptation.<br /> <br /> When one does... Well, that's either a lot of work or an unhealthy amount of Ravaging, which isn't going to look that good on you. Not a capital crime, but Ravaging once or twice a month is definitely going to get you weird glances even from the Unseelie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I think that in exchange they lost a lot of distinctiveness. The need to Rhapsody could have been toned down some while still keeping their backstory, as it were. I get that it was an attempt to solve a real problem, I'm just unsatisfied with the solution. I enjoyed that the Leanhaun weren't a terrifying secret apocalypse cult because they were edgelords, or had soul their souls or whatever, or were the secret servants of some thing, or were cosmic nihilists or what have you (not that there isn't mileage to be had out of that kind of thing, it was just compelling that they came at this from a completely different path). You could see every awful terrifying step, one after another, that lead them to become what they are and pursuing the course that they do, you could understand it in a sense, and that made it even more frightening and bleakly tragic. There was a feeling that there was no other way this could have ended up for them. And that their plan was essentially long term avoided the playable Baali trap of &quot;you have to be actively doing awful corrupting infernal shit either because you are straight up horrible or because you're doing some extreme, almost parodic hard man making hard choices to kinda sorta preserve the world junk, in which case you're the most important person in the group I guess anyway and the plot bends around you.&quot; They could be doing plenty of other things in the meantime, but the hidden truth of them was always there, looming over their lives, filtering how they experienced them. If you could decouple that from &quot;you have to Rhapsodize wayyy too frequently to be a manageable pc&quot; I think something compelling could have been preserved.<br /> <br /> I always found the Balor more of an overall problem in that unless everyone are playing Balor, or Thallain I guess (ugh) you are everyone else's antagonist by almost default. Unless you are, I don't know, some kind of special Drizz't style Balor? (which I don't think was even possible with their pre 20th setup) you are actively working to ruin everyone else's day. You're palling around with both WtA Fomorians and CtD Fomorians. I get why that kinda had to go if you want playable Balor.<br /> <br /> Anyway! Vampire!<br /> <br /> I did otherwise want to note on &quot;aren't vampires intrinsically shitty?&quot; that even a bit into Revised, there was an explicitly in game material notion for some that &quot;A beast I am lest a beast I become&quot; was a false paradox, was an answerable riddle. And the answer was &quot;no&quot;. That's in game material. NPCs in Golconda existed, for example, to demonstrate that, while incredibly difficult, and probably you might die or fail, other ways were possible. You might find an end as tragic as the Grail Knights did, but you might all the same not (and hey, maybe one or two of them survived and stayed true to their blessing maybe). Neither the thirst nor the beast always had to win. There was a suggestion that part of why vampire society, be it that of the Sabbat, Anarchs, Camarilla, or Indep Clans, was so ugly, was that the vampires reinforcing the worst parts of those societies *needed* it to be ugly. They couldn't face their own spiritual/ethical ugliness, it was too hard, so, consciously or more often subconsciously and rationalized, they enforced social orders that would make everyone ugly and complicit in that ugliness, accepting it as just the way things are. That's not really even that far off from the world we live in where &quot;trying for better things is impossible and stupid, the world is too complex and awful by default&quot; is a fairly commonly passed around message. I tend to think that's intentional. Even the game material used to quote the Crow (the first one, the good one) in noting that as grim and horrible as things might be and are in the WoD, &quot;it can't rain all the time&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T18:53:39-07:00","id":1563734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563723#post1563723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree W6 shouldn't keep the cult. But that's for White Wolf to decide and if they do keep the I think adding factional infighting would add some much needed characterization to the cult. Especially if W6 makes an evil player option like Sabatt are slated to be in V6. Unless White wolf does a stupid and make the BSD the playable antagonist.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would be more interested in trying a BSD as a playable villain option, but Nurgle is my least favorite of the Chaos Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T18:55:55-07:00","id":1563735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"