ewolves, I'll petition Tzeentch and Slaanesh.<br /> <br /> Not the mountain sized pustule, who thinks projectile defecation is a sacred blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T19:11:58-07:00","id":1563737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563736#post1563736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I want to play around with tentacled werewolves, I'll petition Tzeentch and Slaanesh.<br /> <br /> Not the mountain sized pustule, who thinks projectile defecation is a sacred blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not knowing who Malal is made me feel even older!<br /> <br /> *crumbles into dust*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T20:51:58-07:00","id":1563740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563737#post1563737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not knowing who Malal is made me feel even older!<br /> <br /> *crumbles into dust*</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't worry, I know.<br /> <br /> Chaos God of Nihilism, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-31T21:24:28-07:00","id":1563741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563740#post1563740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, don't worry, I know.<br /> <br /> Chaos God of Nihilism, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a close enough short version, yerp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T03:28:46-07:00","id":1563749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563733#post1563733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but I think that in exchange they lost a lot of distinctiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't, because that's not what I understand to have happened.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the change has that much of an impact on their original description. Everything the Leanhaun believed and did works just fine with the less severe weakness, and so does their reason for wanting Endless Winter, as the problem is the aging, not the Rhapsody itself.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, the only thing that really relied on the need for Rhapsody specifically was their overly romantic approach to it, but while it was a very interesting pathos, especially for an Unseelie House, it was greatly overdone because of the requirement. You loose a lot of the punch of a heartbreaking love tragedy when you have to get one every month. The new take allows to explore greater variety, while still remaining within their ethos towards Glamour taking, and in fact you can extrapolate the romantic approach to all forms of Epiphany that would then make for a greater variety of takes on Leanhaun excess, rather than focus only in the archetype of Leanan Sidhe.<br /> <br /> What removed the Doomsday Cult aspect was not the Rhapsody thing, but that C20 removed the metaplot of the Shadow Court. Leanhaun were an Apocalyptic Cult because they were written almost exclusively in the context of &quot;this House is for use with the Shadow Court&quot;, so a version of the game where that Court is not that important won't work this aspect.<br /> <br /> And honestly? Good riddance. I personally see the Shadow Court as one of the worse things they added to Changeling. It was there to force the game into the apocalyptic tone of other lines while ignoring how much it had nightmare fuel and space for such plots without it. What the Shadow Court did was not to add this kind of plot to the game, was to make it mandatory when it shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> C20 overall has a hard time to condense every aspect of the Leanhaun in the core book, but that's actually the standard corebook treatment being applied to factions who originally had a dedicated book. It's standard fare for WoD20 and it's still compatible with old lore. And if you play a Shadow Court member or Shadow Court style Leanhaun, everything they were before will apply to the letter. But I personally think the Apocalyptic Cult part isn't required, isn't the most interesting aspect of playing Leanhaun, and even in itself works best as an occasional plot that can then get your full attention rather than a standard metaplot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563733#post1563733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always found the Balor more of an overall problem in that unless everyone are playing Balor, or Thallain I guess (ugh) you are everyone else's antagonist by almost default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take what I said above about Leanhaun and increase a hundredfold, I despise the old take on House Balor. They're seriously way better in C20 with the sheer antagonism toned down in favor of a performative antagonism that may of may not be hiding actual malice in plain sight while they act as competent politicians for a change.<br /> <br /> Overall previous Changeling sourcebooks had the &quot;50 Shades of Nightmare&quot; problem: authors who didn't understood that the game's whimsy was not a denial of evil kept adding villains and trying to build an equivalent to the BSD and the Nefandi that Changeling didn't really need, and would naturally subsume in itself because it is made for utterly despicable evil to not be a problem or antithetical to whimsy. So the next author would feel the same &quot;gap&quot; and repeat, and we ended up with what, four or more types of &quot;Uber Villains&quot; sitting mostly useless there?<br /> <br /> Adhene, Thallain, the Shadow Court, agents of the Fomorians, all were attempts to make for a play style that were actually so basic that being made only for that just made them generic and uninspired rather than dreadful. Sure, Thallain are the worse offenders by a mile, but still.<br /> <br /> C20 was doing an excellent job overall toning down the Evil Villains of Villanic Evilness take to instead emphasize the previously secondary aspects that were actually way more interesting. So we have Balor as an ambiguous player working with obviously performative edginess that may either be just style or may be a double deception strategy and you'll never be sure, the Adhene got lovecraftian weirdness amped, the Shadow Court is optional and if does work better as an option you can apply surgically rather than assuming as metaplot true antagonists... And the Thallain don't really have much where to go, I guess, we kind of have to suffer them for completionism's sake.<br /> <br /> Sure, corebook treatment and lack of books for the line in C20 does have a cost as we see with more complex concepts like Leanhaun, but I do think it was overall well done and heck, Balor was an exceedingly welcome and refreshing change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563733#post1563733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did otherwise want to note on &quot;aren't vampires intrinsically shitty?&quot; that even a bit into Revised, there was an explicitly in game material notion for some that &quot;A beast I am lest a beast I become&quot; was a false paradox, was an answerable riddle. And the answer was &quot;no&quot;. That's in game material.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said elsewhere, the actual rules even made being an ok vampire relatively easy. Between managing feeding to avoid harming people too much, burning Willpower to not risk Frenzy and many other little things scattered through the game, you don't have any real impediment to be a good person while still being a vampire.<br /> <br /> Players who enjoy the grimdark take complain about this, but those are not failures in design. They are what the game intended all along. The Kindred society repeating endlessly that you have no choice when you actually have was the point all along.<br /> <br /> The description of the condition as one that entails inevitable degradation isn't given by an unreliable narrator just for style: the narrator is wrong. He was wrong all along.<br /> <br /> What staying at high Humanity actually require is just that you put in the basic effort. Evil isn't unavoidable, it's just convenient, and Elders want to convince themselves and others that they didn't fell so low just because it was more convenient. They want to believe it was greater than them when, in fact, it was their choice all along, their human, mundane choice.<br /> <br /> So much so that you'll see a number of NPCs who are better than this without any kind of surreal effort. They got toned down as editions went on to keep things ambiguous and give space for groups that like to play the edgy dark style, but there was a reason why you had non negligible amounts of vampires that were good simply and genuinely. And I find it way more compelling than just &quot;Vampires are all cursed to be horrible&quot;, which is just childish and monotone to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T04:19:01-07:00","id":1563752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What removed the Doomsday Cult aspect was not the Rhapsody thing, but that C20 removed the metaplot of the Shadow Court. </div> </div> </div>It didn't, though. The C20 &quot;mostly commoner and otherwise unseelie protest movement&quot; Shadow Court is now an unwitting patsy of the Fomorian courts, as opposed to previously an organization with varying, even feuding, opinions on the Fomorian courts (compare the Cold Watch for instance to the Balor, or the various feuding political impulses that wanted wildly different, even opposing things for fae society). Which is an easy thing to miss honestly because one of the problems of the C20 hardcover, reflecting a difficult development process, is that it's contradictory on itself in various places. The Thallain in C20 usurped the leaders of the Court and are a secret controlling presence within it, and are using it as a pawn to fracture fae society. It's like the sections talking about how the nobility have become near murderous glamour hoarders juxtaposed with the various kingdom descriptions that talk like everything's going great actually, and all of it as third person statements. C20 is in various ways as janky as any other edition of Changeling, just in different ways (in some ways I find it thus a lateral move overall, where they fixed some of my problems, then gave me new problems, but at this point. Favourite of my WoD games alongside pre 5th VtM though it is, I'm used to that you can't really run a Changeling game without picking what you're actually going to take from it, and also not, and making that super clear to your players, to avoid massive headaches)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And honestly? Good riddance. I personally see the Shadow Court as one of the worse things they added to Changeling. It was there to force the game into the apocalyptic tone of other lines while ignoring how much it had nightmare fuel and space for such plots without it. What the Shadow Court did was not to add this kind of plot to the game, was to make it mandatory when it shouldn't be. </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Shadow Court was a fairly early game add on, book wise. It came out a year and a half after the 1e corebook and the court itself had mentions and plot relevance beforehand as a thing. It's been some while now, but before going ArtHaus, CtD's release schedule was actually pretty compressed.<br /> <br /> It's also easy to miss that there was material in CtD had a big sweeping tone from pretty much the jump, as the Immortal Eyes books and adventures were.. erhm... not great? And not as widely focused on after they came out as a lot of other stuff in the line. (To people who love those books and adventures. Look. I actually do like the bits about what Ailil himself has been doing for the past long while, but Changeling Ireland was.. oof. Ooof. Oi. Ooof. Yikes. Not Isles of the Mighty unfortunate- which I do have a sad fondness for some pieces of as well- but oof.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Adhene, Thallain, the Shadow Court, agents of the Fomorians, all were attempts to make for a play style that were actually so basic that being made only for that just made them generic and uninspired rather than dreadful. Sure, Thallain are the worse offenders by a mile, but still. </div> </div> </div>Other than the Adhene, those things all had a fairly early presence in the gameline. I'm not saying I'm particularly fond of the Thallain (though mostly it's that I'm not fond of playable Thallain), I'm just saying, CtD was doing that stuff not long into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, corebook treatment and lack of books for the line in C20 does have a cost as we see with more complex concepts like Leanhaun, but I do think it was overall well done and heck, Balor was an exceedingly welcome and refreshing change. </div> </div> </div>C20 for me suffers mostly from trying to do too many things at once, as if they knew they were maybe going to get three books tops, and feeling rushed and creaking at the seams as a result. It's crowded and not everything fits with itself. It doesn't help that there have been writer comments floating around that described what seemed like a stressed, rushed process. There's a bunch of things in C20 I'm entirely partial to and I'm glad to see them, but there are any number of things that I otherwise throw my hands up in the air about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T05:31:48-07:00","id":1563759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563752#post1563752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn't, though. The C20 &quot;mostly commoner and otherwise unseelie protest movement&quot; Shadow Court is now an unwitting patsy of the Fomorian courts, as opposed to previously an organization with varying, even feuding, opinions on the Fomorian courts (compare the Cold Watch for instance to the Balor, or the various feuding political impulses that wanted wildly different, even opposing things for fae society). Which is an easy thing to miss honestly because one of the problems of the C20 hardcover, reflecting a difficult development process, is that it's contradictory on itself in various places. The Thallain in C20 usurped the leaders of the Court and are a secret controlling presence within it, and are using it as a pawn to fracture fae society. It's like the sections talking about how the nobility have become near murderous glamour hoarders juxtaposed with the various kingdom descriptions that talk like everything's going great actually, and all of it as third person statements. C20 is in various ways as janky as any other edition of Changeling, just in different ways (in some ways I find it thus a lateral move overall, where they fixed some of my problems, then gave me new problems, but at this point. Favourite of my WoD games alongside pre 5th VtM though it is, I'm used to that you can't really run a Changeling game without picking what you're actually going to take from it, and also not, and making that super clear to your players, to avoid massive headaches)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm misremembering, but I thought C20 described one of the Shadow Courts' motivations as trying to restore the shared power system, where the Seelie and Unseelie courts exchange rulership throughout the year?<br /> <br /> Or was that the case before they got taken over by Thallain?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T05:42:19-07:00","id":1563760,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying those problems weren't early, but it's more that they appear in books that are rather dissonant from the core.<br /> <br /> Truth be told, there are very few Changeling sourcebooks I liked in any edition, and that impetus to give it BSD/Baali/Nefandus analogues is one of the reasons.<br /> <br /> C20 is better in my opinion, but I get what you mean and can't say I actually gave a lot of attention to the Shadow Court anyway. As I said, I find it a bad piece of lore to begin with.<br /> <br /> Simply put, the regular court system of Kithain has plenty of space for all sorts of factions. What exactly does the Shadow Court adds that can't be done within the regular courts?<br /> <br /> You have all those terrible nightmare Fae like the Thallain and stuff and... you can have core book Kithain that include Infernalist Eiluned, Unseelie Fionna partying with Black Spiral Dancers, and whatever you wanna do with Red Caps. You can literally and easily homebrew an Oath to have a regular Changeling being the frigging demonic force behind some of the Super Evil Factions in the other game lines.<br /> <br /> With everything the core Changeling offers in every edition, I always had the impression that most sourcebooks were both contradictory with the base game to an uncomfortable level and for no gain. Their plots feel a lot more a try hard than adding much value, with excessively poetic text making up for very bland ideas.<br /> <br /> Exceptions exist, but that's what they are. The Leanhaun are a good example and I find most of their writeup very interesting, but Thallain and Balor are more representative of the usual fare with those books.<br /> <br /> And yeah, my praise on C20 is mainly for the core book and what it did with the basics. The sourcebooks are better than average for the line, but that's a low bar IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T05:51:55-07:00","id":1563761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563759#post1563759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm misremembering, but I thought C20 described one of the Shadow Courts' motivations as trying to restore the shared power system, where the Seelie and Unseelie courts exchange rulership throughout the year?<br /> <br /> Or was that the case before they got taken over by Thallain?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's right, it's just that their idea of how to achieve it is crazy as fuck.<br /> <br /> Bottom line, they think the only way to restore balance is to bring about the apocalyptic start of the Endless Winter to cause an electroshock style seizure in the Dreaming itself that'll reboot the Kithain out of the Changeling Way and undo the Sundering.<br /> <br /> You know, a simple plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T06:00:50-07:00","id":1563763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563759#post1563759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I'm misremembering, but I thought C20 described one of the Shadow Courts' motivations as trying to restore the shared power system, where the Seelie and Unseelie courts exchange rulership throughout the year?<br /> <br /> Or was that the case before they got taken over by Thallain?</div> </div> </div> </div>In C20 in the corebook, the Shadow Court is mostly, on a superficial level, a protest movement by commoners and landless nobles against both seelie and unseelie nobility behaviour and leadership in the Evanescence, having largely ditched its previous focus. It's compared to Occupy Wall Street, the Arab Spring and BLM. Secretly it's controlled by the Thallain of the Black Court to mess with and fracture fae society on behalf of their terrifying masters.<br /> <br /> Honestly I *reaalllly* don't like that as it is basically &quot;your protest movements for social change are actually just useful idiot pawns of the boogeyman!&quot;, it's such a terrible image/message/metaphor.<br /> <br /> Now, this itself doesn't fit well with the way House Ailil is still portrayed as being heavily tied into the Shadow Court from its leadership on down, which would make more sense with the Shadow Court's previous version, but that's something else that needed some extra editing passes. It sometimes feels like some sections were written without any awareness of other sections.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you're thinking of the pre Thallain takeover court.<br /> <br /> (I don't use the Shadow Court when I run C20)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> C20 is better in my opinion, but I get what you mean and can't say I actually gave a lot of attention to the Shadow Court anyway. As I said, I find it a bad piece of lore to begin with. </div> </div> </div>I honestly find the C20 version of the court worse because, weelll, see above!<br /> <br /> Again, there's a lot of good things in C20, it's just, like every edition of Changeling, there's also a bunch of &quot;oh buddy, ooof.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T06:02:53-07:00","id":1563764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563761#post1563761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's right, it's just that their idea of how to achieve it is crazy as fuck.<br /> <br /> Bottom line, they think the only way to restore balance is to bring about the apocalyptic start of the Endless Winter to cause an electroshock style seizure in the Dreaming itself that'll reboot the Kithain out of the Changeling Way and undo the Sundering.<br /> <br /> You know, a simple plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there are something like four or five different plans in the original Shadow Court for what restoring balance means, how it should be done, if it should be done at all, and everyone is keeping them the mostly private matter of their own faction while stabbing the other faction when there's a stabby opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T06:23:15-07:00","id":1563768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563764#post1563764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair there are something like four or five different plans in the original Shadow Court for what restoring balance means, how it should be done, if it should be done at all, and everyone is keeping them the mostly private matter of their own faction while stabbing the other faction when there's a stabby opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think the one interesting thing about the Shadow Court is how some of the views, like this one, fully embrace a Changeling ethos of making things as unnecessarily hard and over the top as possible.<br /> <br /> This particular take is something like being upset that a particular political party has been in power too long, so your proposal to solve it is to secretly provoke a nuclear war that'll make the Earth uninhabitable, forcing everyone to build a spaceship and the wealthy to finance the Terraforming of Mars, leaving them without money to pay for lobbying when the new Mars Governments call for elections.<br /> <br /> All else apart, those are legitimately creative motivations for an Apocalyptic Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T06:41:30-07:00","id":1563770,"title":"","content":"I mean for the original Shadow Court, essentially the plans are:<br /> <br /> House Balor: &quot;Unseelie/Seelie will not matter once our dark masters are free and we conquer the world or at the very least the Dreaming in their service and also we kill you all, not that we're telling the rest of you that.&quot;<br /> <br /> House Ailil: &quot;We will methodically, ruthlessly and carefully scheme our way into enough military and political power to present the restoration of seasonal rule as a fait accompli to the Seelie. We are telling you all this. This is a sensible plan that we should be doing. Yes, totally coincidentally House Ailil will be the actual rulers of the Winter Court, but you all get something. Compromise damn you!&quot;<br /> <br /> House Leanhaun: &quot;Armageddon. Not that we're telling the rest of you that.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then you have factions like the Cold Watch who are just there to kill Thallain and Fomorians whenever the chance arises while giving the Balor a hairy suspect eyeball in-between leaping backwards out of skyscraper windows and firing bullets up at the monster on the other side of it (there is artwork of that. Look, sometimes I am a simple person of simple pleasures ;p)<br /> <br /> And then there's a huge grab bag of various commoner kiths and unseelie members of seelie noble houses who have plans ranging from &quot;Restore heavy ritual practice so that the kithain resume seasonal rule out of, I don't know, religiosity&quot; to &quot;Permanent unseelie takeover!&quot; to &quot;Chaos! Chaos, chaos, CHAOS!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T11:06:06-07:00","id":1563775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563763#post1563763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In C20 in the corebook, the Shadow Court is mostly, on a superficial level, a protest movement by commoners and landless nobles against both seelie and unseelie nobility behaviour and leadership in the Evanescence, having largely ditched its previous focus. It's compared to Occupy Wall Street, the Arab Spring and BLM. Secretly it's controlled by the Thallain of the Black Court to mess with and fracture fae society on behalf of their terrifying masters.<br /> <br /> Honestly I *reaalllly* don't like that as it is basically &quot;your protest movements for social change are actually just useful idiot pawns of the boogeyman!&quot;, it's such a terrible image/message/metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not entirely unrealistic, though. A lot of coups have resulted in the revolutionaries becoming the very thing they swore to destroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T19:54:26-07:00","id":1563794,"title":"","content":"You know I find really sad and funny that the fact that the Sabbat is slated to be playable in the base game is the least talked about aspect of this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T20:43:22-07:00","id":1563795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563794#post1563794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I find really sad and funny that the fact that the Sabbat is slated to be playable in the base game is the least talked about aspect of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because we haven't heard much about it from the live play tests yet.<br /> <br /> All we know at the moment is they're coming back in as a playable option, but nothing about how they've changed up their operations during their absence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T21:16:54-07:00","id":1563796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563794#post1563794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I find really sad and funny that the fact that the Sabbat is slated to be playable in the base game is the least talked about aspect of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just me, but the whole idea of a 6th edition, coming out of Paradox, is exhausting.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Yeah? Okay? Would have been nice if they'd done that in V5 in the first place.&quot;<br /> <br /> We had a good thing going with V20, and now the better part of a decade later we're scrambling for word that ANYTHING we used to have is coming back. I'm so numb right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T21:18:34-07:00","id":1563797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563796#post1563796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's just me, but the whole idea of a 6th edition, coming out of Paradox, is exhausting.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Yeah? Okay? Would have been nice if they'd done that in V5 in the first place.&quot;<br /> <br /> We had a good thing going with V20, and now the better part of a decade later we're scrambling for word that ANYTHING we used to have is coming back. I'm so numb right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I'm looking forward to how they Stumble with W6... IF W6 even sees the light of day...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T07:13:06-07:00","id":1563801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563794#post1563794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I find really sad and funny that the fact that the Sabbat is slated to be playable in the base game is the least talked about aspect of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not.<br /> <br /> But all we have is a Playtest testing rules. What is there to talk about the setting itself when we have almost nothing in what it will be like?<br /> <br /> As far as I could see this was actually the most commented revelation about their plans by far, but there's not much to say given the revelation really is just a 5 words sentence: &quot;the Sabbat will be playable&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563796#post1563796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's just me, but the whole idea of a 6th edition, coming out of Paradox, is exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's just you, but for now is just a pointless fixation.<br /> <br /> Paradox is the owner of the IP and that's not going to change. They have zero reason to sell and if they did no one we would actually want to see buying it would have the money to do so.<br /> <br /> V5 is a fact and has been for years. Judging V6 by the lens of &quot;this should have been done at V5&quot; is refusing to disengage from past frustration rather than any new frustration being added.<br /> <br /> For now V6 is an unknown quantity with very little hinted about how it will actually be, but this little does indicate a departure of V5's problems, which is what most people wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T07:35:36-07:00","id":1563802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563794#post1563794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I find really sad and funny that the fact that the Sabbat is slated to be playable in the base game is the least talked about aspect of this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing you say that when there is a recent thread with people arguing that it's great and then other people arguing that you could already play them in V5. <br /> <br /> But I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a>, we know little of how it will work in practice so while the idea is admirable the proof is in the pudding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T09:34:01-07:00","id":1563803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563802#post1563802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing you say that when there is a recent thread with people arguing that it's great and then other people arguing that you could already play them in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, it just required you to ignore almost everything V5 said and use unofficial rules, because the actual official Sabbat material is unplayable in every sense.<br /> <br /> I find it disingenuous to argue you can do it in an edition just because you can house rule it. V5 did what it could to actively deny this option in any game following the official setting and rules.<br /> <br /> Being able to ignore their efforts isn't playable Sabbat being incidental, it's people ignoring actual constraints placed to disallow it and homebrewing around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T10:10:04-07:00","id":1563806,"title":"","content":"Let's hope they don't tone down the Sabbat to a more family friendly version.<br /> <br /> I still want the crazy fanatics, who take turns leaping over bonfires to prove their mastery over their Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T14:07:20-07:00","id":1563807,"title":"","content":"We're all kind of in a holding pattern at the moment really, there's not much more to go on than has already been talked about.<br /> <br /> I mean look at how much of this thread alone went off on tangents about Demon and Changeling *coughs, shuffles guiltily*<br /> <br /> (Sidebar: I remain sad Demon never got the 20th treatment. Demon with an actual cleaned up ruleset, or at least an attempted one, would have been fun)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T02:12:54-07:00","id":1563818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563803#post1563803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could, it just required you to ignore almost everything V5 said and use unofficial rules, because the actual official Sabbat material is unplayable in every sense.<br /> <br /> I find it disingenuous to argue you can do it in an edition just because you can house rule it. V5 did what it could to actively deny this option in any game following the official setting and rules.<br /> <br /> Being able to ignore their efforts isn't playable Sabbat being incidental, it's people ignoring actual constraints placed to disallow it and homebrewing around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a common issue in 5th edition discussions in general, were the defences against feedback relied on a concept of the game which didnt really exist.<br /> <br /> Theoretically yes you can home-brew Sabbat, with sufficient time I can homebrew mage mechanics or playing as a space marine.<br /> <br /> Imo not making sabbat playable was probably one of the editions major errors as it cultivated ill will among a lot of players and early sabbat is about as personal horror as it gets as your humanity is fed into a wood chipper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T02:42:49-07:00","id":1563821,"title":"","content":"At most I can say WoD has a history with this attitude. In the 90s it was hard to complaint about rules you thought were bad because out of every shadow would jump a defender saying the game didn't have bad rules because you could ignore them or punish players that used rules you don't like.<br /> <br /> The same assholes used to say there were no suboptimal options because bad option were actually superior roleplay opportunities and a player that avoided them was moraly bankrupt and should be humiliated for it.<br /> <br /> Criticism deflection of this kind must be met with complete, unapologetic exposure of their bullshit. If someone is willing to talk bullshit on others to protect a piece of media, then they forfeited their own right for respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T04:07:17-07:00","id":1563824,"title":"","content":"Honestly I wonder if each splat's Sabbat equivalent being playable is going to be a trend in the 6th edition? Like I guess we would get the Technocracy and Shadow court for M6 and C6. The SI would be playable for H6 possibly with vastly reduced resources due to random meta-plot reasons and I guess the Cult is playable for W6 unless they're randomly redeemed for that edition or are still unplayable in lieu of the BSD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-04-2026, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T04:47:09-07:00","id":1563826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563821#post1563821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At most I can say WoD has a history with this attitude. In the 90s it was hard to complaint about rules you thought were bad because out of every shadow would jump a defender saying the game didn't have bad rules because you could ignore them or punish players that used rules you don't like.<br /> <br /> The same assholes used to say there were no suboptimal options because bad option were actually superior roleplay opportunities and a player that avoided them was moraly bankrupt and should be humiliated for it.<br /> <br /> Criticism deflection of this kind must be met with complete, unapologetic exposure of their bullshit. If someone is willing to talk bullshit on others to protect a piece of media, then they forfeited their own right for respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall the suboptimal options was deployed in 5th &quot;the sabbat's total lack of personality is the opportunity to create one.&quot; Not to mention the anarchs chronic underwritting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-04-2026, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T11:16:01-07:00","id":1563831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563821#post1563821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same assholes used to say there were no suboptimal options because bad option were actually superior roleplay opportunities and <b>a player that avoided them was moraly bankrupt</b> and should be humiliated for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>... how?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> Sabbat Sire snatches a college student by the throat and holds them in front of you.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Right now, I want you to eat this.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Newly embraced shovelhead desperately tries to stammer out an excuse for why they can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T11:20:42-07:00","id":1563832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563826#post1563826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recall the suboptimal options was deployed in 5th &quot;the sabbat's total lack of personality is the opportunity to create one.&quot; Not to mention the anarchs chronic underwritting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;LACK OF PERSONALITY!?&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> They're the vampiric equivalent to the catholic church.<br /> <br /> Come on, the very concept alone sounds metal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T13:39:17-07:00","id":1563836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563806#post1563806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's hope they don't tone down the Sabbat to a more family friendly version.<br /> <br /> I still want the crazy fanatics, who take turns leaping over bonfires to prove their mastery over their Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of one of my favorite stock scenes when STing a Sabbat game: having the player roleplay trying to jump over the fire not by resisting their fear, but instead by convincing their beast that getting to the other side of the fire is an enemy they must defeat. Channel the beast into rage when it wants to be afraid, instead of simply repressing the beast. <br /> <br /> I always liked it. It's not a dice scene. Purely a roleplay scene, but it's a fun little roleplay moment that helps the players get into the mindset of playing Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T13:47:18-07:00","id":1563837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563832#post1563832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>&quot;LACK OF PERSONALITY!?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> They're the vampiric equivalent to the catholic church.<br /> <br /> Come on, the very concept alone sounds metal!</div> </div> </div> </div>In 5th they're not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T15:42:23-07:00","id":1563840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563803#post1563803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could, it just required you to ignore almost everything V5 said and use unofficial rules, because the actual official Sabbat material is unplayable in every sense.<br /> <br /> I find it disingenuous to argue you can do it in an edition just because you can house rule it. V5 did what it could to actively deny this option in any game following the official setting and rules.<br /> <br /> Being able to ignore their efforts isn't playable Sabbat being incidental, it's people ignoring actual constraints placed to disallow it and homebrewing around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know and one redittor was bending him/herseflf into a pretzel trying to reason that actually you can because s/he been doing that for ages so &quot;why can't you you lazy bum&quot; (I am exaggerating but s/he really called people terrified and lazy for claiming that V5 does everything to make playing Sabbat unappealing and hard). Of course one can play Sabbat with homebrewing rules, people did stranger things, but it's hard to argue with someone who can't acknowledge the facts.<br /> <br /> And as for playable Technocracy, Shadow Court or BSD? Who knows? We know very little about the vision the current creative team has for WoD6 so I would loath to gamble on that. Probably after we get more lore for V6 we can start to piece the puzzle together. Sabbat being playable in V6 is a good move but will the sect be given proper treatment? Only time will tell. Anarchs were put as the centrepiece in V5 and yet they were as undercooked as in Legacy. So let's hope for some good Sabbat writing in V6. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T18:08:25-07:00","id":1563845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563831#post1563831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... how?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Rein-Hagen in a nutshell for you.<br /> <br /> He did, effectively, believe his work should be taken seriously as artistic exercise, all players should strive to achieve high end performance, and anyone daring to face it as a mere game was indeed akin to a criminal and should for real be made to suffer in the game until they either learn their lesson or accept social ostracism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563840#post1563840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know and one redittor was bending him/herseflf into a pretzel trying to reason that actually you can because s/he been doing that for ages so &quot;why can't you you lazy bum&quot; (I am exaggerating but s/he really called people terrified and lazy for claiming that V5 does everything to make playing Sabbat unappealing and hard). Of course one can play Sabbat with homebrewing rules, people did stranger things, but it's hard to argue with someone who can't acknowledge the facts.<br /> <br /> And as for playable Technocracy, Shadow Court or BSD? Who knows? We know very little about the vision the current creative team has for WoD6 so I would loath to gamble on that. Probably after we get more lore for V6 we can start to piece the puzzle together. Sabbat being playable in V6 is a good move but will the sect be given proper treatment? Only time will tell. Anarchs were put as the centrepiece in V5 and yet they were as undercooked as in Legacy. So let's hope for some good Sabbat writing in V6.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I've literally house-ruled the Sabbat for D&amp;D 3.5 once, but I'm not arguing that it proves WotC made the game to be compatible with it.<br /> <br /> Anarchs weren't undercooked in Legacy. 1st and 2nd Edition Anarchs are perfectly done: it's not a Sect. For their purpose there they fit very well and they were the focus of the game, even more so in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> Revised and V20 dropped the ball precisely because instead of explaining why they should not be compared to a sect, they decided to let players run with the idea without giving it actual support. That was gross negligence.<br /> <br /> V5 is a case study of design imbecility, making them a formal Sect based on the central idea of having no idea of what they're about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T20:04:12-07:00","id":1563848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563845#post1563845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's Rein-Hagen in a nutshell for you.<br /> <br /> He did, effectively, believe his work should be taken seriously as artistic exercise, all players should strive to achieve high end performance, and anyone daring to face it as a mere game was indeed akin to a criminal and should for real be made to suffer in the game until they either learn their lesson or accept social ostracism.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Joke's on you - I'm already socially ostracized!&quot; [/Skeletor]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, I've literally house-ruled the Sabbat for D&amp;D 3.5 once, but I'm not arguing that it proves WotC made the game to be compatible with it.<br /> <br /> Anarchs weren't undercooked in Legacy. 1st and 2nd Edition Anarchs are perfectly done: it's not a Sect. For their purpose there they fit very well and they were the focus of the game, even more so in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> Revised and V20 dropped the ball precisely because instead of explaining why they should not be compared to a sect, they decided to let players run with the idea without giving it actual support. That was gross negligence.<br /> <br /> V5 is a case study of design imbecility, making them a formal Sect based on the central idea of having no idea of what they're about. </div> </div> </div>Spinal Tap V:tM design. &quot;A long time ago there was a sect of vampires known as... The Sabbat! And no one knew where they came from or what they were doing!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T21:28:48-07:00","id":1563849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563845#post1563845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's Rein-Hagen in a nutshell for you.<br /> <br /> He did, effectively, believe his work should be taken seriously as artistic exercise, all players should strive to achieve high end performance, and anyone daring to face it as a mere game was indeed akin to a criminal and should for real be made to suffer in the game until they either learn their lesson or accept social ostracism.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they're a whack job? Okay!<br /> <br /> I mean, I understand and agree with the assessment that playing suboptimal characters can make for fun and engaging role play opportunities. But actively punishing the player for not utilizing them is ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T01:00:27-07:00","id":1563850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563848#post1563848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Spinal Tap V:tM design. &quot;A long time ago there was a sect of vampires known as... The Sabbat! And no one knew where they came from or what they were doing!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That was funnily enough the problem, they were chasing a aesthetic rather than game design, the Anarchs had the same problem in 5th. It's why people stated it felt like what the Sabbat was back to what it was supposed to be but when pressed their elaborations were often non-sensical. (they're like the mongol horde, the Sabbat shouldnt hold territory, it's like playing orcs in d&amp;d etc)<br /> <br /> The funny part is if you're a in game Anarch or Camarilla vampire the Sabbat actually behaves pretty much the same in all editions (although it's actually more predictable in 5th due to reduction in variation) when you're facing one and the re-writes only mattered to the irl reader or if you wanted to play them.<br /> One of the ironies of 5th was it wanted to be a sandbox but then reduced the sects to around 1.5, it wanted to focus on personal horror then got rid of the personal horror sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-05-2026, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T08:14:21-07:00","id":1563854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563849#post1563849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they're a whack job? Okay!<br /> <br /> I mean, I understand and agree with the assessment that playing suboptimal characters can make for fun and engaging role play opportunities. But actively punishing the player for not utilizing them is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is - TTRPGs are still entertainment, and unlike something like movies or books, people playing TTRPGs are deciding what to include in their interactions with this form of media. So I can understand that the developers might want VtM to be angst filled drama but they cannot stop people from portraying a coterie of losers who gather each night to make pranks on government officials or celebrities. VtM doesn't need to be personal horror, it can be comedy, action, science fiction or romance. Hell, often it can be all of those things in one Chronicle. And TTRPG developers should realize that people like different things and they do not have to put dozens of books about comedy in VtM but also they should not make STs and players feel inferior because they want to run VtM for laughs. <br /> <br /> I was not engaged with the game when V20 happened but from what I have seen of the books OPP understood that people want different things from the setting and their approach to the metaplot was a reflection of that. You could play pre-Gehenna, during the Gehenna, post-Gehenna or ignoring the events of the Time of Judgement altogether. And they understood that even the silliest thing from the previous editions were someone's favourite parts so when they handled them they tried to make them fleshed out and interesting to both appeal to the original fans but also make it appetising to people who never liked them. I never cared much about DSotBH but &quot;Black Hand...&quot; is one of my favourite WoD supplements. Just imagine, Baali who do not want to destroy the world but want to save it. <br /> <br /> So I am hoping that V6 can bring more tools for people wanting to play varied games of VtM and there are some rays of hope with elders and Sabbat being made playable again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T11:59:18-07:00","id":1563857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563850#post1563850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(they're like the mongol horde, the Sabbat shouldnt hold territory, it's like playing orcs in d&amp;d etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orc's whole thing is all about seizing territory. Gruumsh told them to go forth and conquer!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2357\" data-vbnamecard=\"2357\">sathriel</a> Considering that the new Humanity system presents it as being a highly personalized thing that is different for each individual, I think the chances of us getting more varied playstyle options is fairly high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T17:19:06-07:00","id":1563858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563857#post1563857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Orc's whole thing is all about seizing territory. Gruumsh told them to go forth and conquer!<br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is they're a wild horde on the attack and the idea they hold turf and do regular vampire stuff is 'wrong' but on a practical level it doesnt matter because you don't see it anyway. The average non sabbat vampire might know the sabbat holds terf but you have no idea what they do there. it's specially written for some abstract satisfaction of specific readers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-05-2026, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T20:15:51-07:00","id":1563862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563857#post1563857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Orc's whole thing is all about seizing territory. Gruumsh told them to go forth and conquer!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why their reasoning was wrong in every conceivable level, because they justified their wrong conclusions with things they also completely misunderstood.<br /> <br /> But their main point was about the faction not being playable or knowable, just a horde that comes out of nowhere unexpected. Which is also not how orcs work in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Or what the Mongol hordes were, by the way, but you can see the problem clearly in how the racist assholes are completely oblivious when talking about an actual social phenomenon in the history of ethnicities and nationalities still standing as if it not only were just a literature trope, but even then one note and simplistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-05T21:56:11-07:00","id":1563864,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> <br /> <br /> Also, the Sabbat didn't just run around burning every village they came across. Their long term goal was to avert Gehenna and then reign eternal over the mortal world as their new vampire overlords.<br /> <br /> Where did they get the idea that the Sabbat were just a bunch of mindless savages who attacked anything that moved?<br /> <br /> Did they think Shovelheads were the norm or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T00:47:15-07:00","id":1563866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563576#post1563576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem isn't just them being right about the world, but their existence confirming the origin of the world to some extent.<br /> <br /> Whether you place other gods as lies or Elohim doesn't change the cosmological statement on which religious narrative is closer to the truth. I despise this, and it has always been my bigger problem with the line.<br /> <br /> I don't want a game that says one mythology to be closer to the truth than other, especially one whose doctrine requires cultural and philosophical erasure.<br /> <br /> So it annoying other game lines to me is minor. It doesn't have to cater to them and vice versa. It establishing a world where some significant aspects of Christianity are objectively true and other world creation myths are objectively wrong is major.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I definitely agree here. That's my major gripe with DTF. That, and the fact it &quot;retcons&quot; everything else into its pantheon (or seems to), and DTF fans take that as gospel (pun intended).<br /> <br /> E.g., any article about non-DTF demons on the WWWiki carried a big template saying they were non-canon because of DTF. Naturally, I edited the wording of that, so that it now only says something like &quot;these demons don't match those demons&quot;, which is far more defensible.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, we'd have to tag all the pages with vampires with a tag to say CTD proves they're non-canon, or all WTA pages to say MTAs proves they're wrong, etc. The way I see it, DTF can say Malfeans are actually just demons all it wants, but it doesn't make it true (especially outside of that line itself).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T07:16:04-07:00","id":1563868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563866#post1563866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, I definitely agree here. That's my major gripe with DTF. That, and the fact it &quot;retcons&quot; everything else into its pantheon (or seems to), and DTF fans take that as gospel (pun intended).<br /> <br /> E.g., any article about non-DTF demons on the WWWiki carried a big template saying they were non-canon because of DTF. Naturally, I edited the wording of that, so that it now only says something like &quot;these demons don't match those demons&quot;, which is far more defensible.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, we'd have to tag all the pages with vampires with a tag to say CTD proves they're non-canon, or all WTA pages to say MTAs proves they're wrong, etc. The way I see it, DTF can say Malfeans are actually just demons all it wants, but it doesn't make it true (especially outside of that line itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. I don\u2019t think Demon the Fallen should control the whole World of Darkness or be empowered to make sweeping changes outside of its line. I also believe that there are numerous different creatures which are all referred to as demons by different game lines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T08:32:30-07:00","id":1563870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563866#post1563866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I definitely agree here. That's my major gripe with DTF. That, and the fact it &quot;retcons&quot; everything else into its pantheon (or seems to), and DTF fans take that as gospel (pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>My only correction here is that the people taking it as gospel weren't every DtF fans, and in fact some weren't DtF fans at all.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda tired of diatribes about how &quot;DtF kidnapped the whole setting&quot; because it didn't actually did anything new.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, Mage and Changeling all had done the exact same thing: establish cosmologies that include and retcon everything else. And it includes their later editions catching up to cover things that came after initial release.<br /> <br /> The people saying something wasn't canon anymore because of DtF were talking bullshit, but this bullshit had been around for a long time without the same vitriolic reaction.reaction.<br /> <br /> Seriously, why Demon has to be sensible to the cosmologies of others? This was not what the WoD was about. Why Demon has to hold to a standard developed in CoD while Werewolf say that Vampires are fomors, Mage say Garou are mindbogglingly ignorant of the spiritual worlds, and Changeling is adamant that all splats are just mutated Kithain?<br /> <br /> And all those have the same problem of fans who want to force this interpretation into other games. Even because they all have some way to claim objective knowledge of what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Demon is being blamed for doing something it was in no way wrong at doing, because it was held to a standard all other lines had already rejected. I don't accept this accusation as valid or legitimate. It was an independent line with full legitimacy to make independent claims for its version of the setting. If someone takes that and extrapolate to say DtF is objectively right outside its own books, this is a problem of this person, not of the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T09:13:17-07:00","id":1563872,"title":"","content":"I would agree that Demon does not have any particular sole ownership of the &quot;here's how the entire setting <i>actually</i> works&quot; thing, nor, especially, having chunks of fandoms that fervently insist their gameline defines the entire WoD and get hopped up at anything/one that suggests otherwise. That's an old, ollllld fan arguement problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T18:23:08-07:00","id":1563876,"title":"","content":"If we're getting Changeling and Mage first (after vampire), then it stands to reason we'll probably be getting back to super powerful abilities we all know and love. Instead of confining us to this street level crap we have in V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-06T19:19:40-07:00","id":1563877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563876#post1563876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're getting Changeling and Mage first (after vampire), then it stands to reason we'll probably be getting back to super powerful abilities we all know and love. Instead of confining us to this street level crap we have in V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Werewolf didn't stop them before, so I'd say if they want to focus on street level they'll just butcher things again.<br /> <br /> But given the Playtest has rules for Methuselah I think we can hope they'll be more sensible in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""}