</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which I don't think it has, and it would have been useful if you could link your source, as sometimes analyzing the source is informative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the post is a single sentence do yeah it's probably nothing. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563892#post1563892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is there any reason you're thinking about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply it's a complete opposite of W5<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T14:04:10-07:00","id":1563900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563896#post1563896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would depend heavily on the direction you want to go in, of which there are so many! So it comes down to your table really.<br /> <br /> For the Lolz: A brand new 4th gen of any clan. Now everyone will collectively shit their pants.<br /> For the Ultimate Lolz: A brand new 4th gen... That's a caitiff. Now the kindred will collectively shit their pants even harder because suddenly they're dealing with a complete unknown. Cue the spooky music! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>New Fourth Gen Nosferatu:</b> <i>&quot;How do you do, fellow sewer rats?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>The Entire Warren:</b> <i>&quot;AAAAAAAHHHHHHHH!!!!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T16:54:22-07:00","id":1563903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563897#post1563897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure. Ur-Shulgi's return wasn't exactly popular, and The Stoneman was already there as a low gen Caitiff. I'm guessing V5 didn't develop either any further?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ur-Shulgi is in the Gehenna War book but otherwise you are right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-07T21:42:22-07:00","id":1563906,"title":"","content":"Even then Ur-Shugi isn't really fleshed out in Gehenna War and we replaced him with Issim Ur Baal in our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T02:09:56-07:00","id":1563908,"title":"","content":"I really find the idea of equating power and Generation stupid. If everyone is shitting their pants because of a new 4th Gen knowing they are new, either something else is happening or this is not a game I recognize as VtM or am interested in playing.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why Generation is the greater source of temptation but fear comes from age. And part of the fun of a game involving new low Gen Embraces, which I've played and run a number, is how they deal with the fact of their weakness.<br /> <br /> A new Embrace and an ancient vampire waking up are very distinct concepts. A Methuselah waking up or an ancient Caitiff are completely unrelated story proposals from a new 4th Gen popping up, as Caitiff or not. It's a nonsensical comparison.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi, it must be added, is a badly written character that is unpopular because of how his plot unfolds with no stakes or anything that warrants the reader's emotional investment, not because he is a bad concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T03:28:16-07:00","id":1563911,"title":"","content":"IMO pants would be shat, but mainly because a newly Embraced 4th Gen means their Ante is active. In the most likely scenario that would also mean the new arrival is a proxy or herald, and whatever shake-up they bring is a result of that - the Ur-Shulgi plot got that part right, although I agree that the main problem was that the specific execution and character wasn't up to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T13:50:18-07:00","id":1563922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563908#post1563908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really find the idea of equating power and Generation stupid. If everyone is shitting their pants because of a new 4th Gen knowing they are new, either something else is happening or this is not a game I recognize as VtM or am interested in playing.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why Generation is the greater source of temptation but fear comes from age. And part of the fun of a game involving new low Gen Embraces, which I've played and run a number, is how they deal with the fact of their weakness.<br /> <br /> A new Embrace and an ancient vampire waking up are very distinct concepts. A Methuselah waking up or an ancient Caitiff are completely unrelated story proposals from a new 4th Gen popping up, as Caitiff or not. It's a nonsensical comparison.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi, it must be added, is a badly written character that is unpopular because of how his plot unfolds with no stakes or anything that warrants the reader's emotional investment, not because he is a bad concept.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hyperbole of my previous post aside, the reason any new 4th gen would be a cause for concern would be because of what it means. A third gen moving about with unknown motives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563908#post1563908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or this is not a game I recognize as VtM or am interested in playing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've no idea what you mean by this though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T16:25:38-07:00","id":1563925,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> There's quite an awful lot of fantasy settings, which present us with the idea that magic became weaker or more difficult to use over time. While the ancient times were a golden age of power and prosperity.<br /> <br /> With that as a reference, the idea of the vampires growing weaker with each subsequent generation isn't too far fetched.<br /> <br /> Sure, when you're first embraced, you may not have access to the god level abilities that your fellow 5th gens can use. But you do have the ability to pump a hell of a lot more BP into using your low tier powers than a higher gen vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-08T21:55:24-07:00","id":1563928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563922#post1563922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hyperbole of my previous post aside, the reason any new 4th gen would be a cause for concern would be because of what it means. A third gen moving about with unknown motives.<br /> <br /> I've no idea what you mean by this though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm annoyed with Char Gen rules that equate the benefits of age and Generation, something V5 did and V6 is toying with too. I'm against giving a single extra dot at anything to a low Gen character.<br /> <br /> And yes, the third Gen is a worrisome matter, if people find out. Because part of the fun with a plot like that is how hard it really is to measure someone's Generation without very specific magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563925#post1563925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> There's quite an awful lot of fantasy settings, which present us with the idea that magic became weaker or more difficult to use over time. While the ancient times were a golden age of power and prosperity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, so what?<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about any fantasy setting, I'm talking about VtM. There's an awful lot of tropes to do anything, my interest is in tropes that improve the specific themes of this specific setting.<br /> <br /> And you described exactly what I said I find the setting in question benefits from and use, so I don't get what you're trying to argue? A 5th Gen Neonate should have clear advantages that age can't cover, and lo and behold, it is what happens. Yet they are a Neonate, their powers are meaningful, but not decisive.<br /> <br /> Or, put in simpler terms, a 5yo 4th Gen has a lot of innate command over their blood. And about 3, maybe 4 Discipline dots. Those are not mutually exclusive, and both being true and relevant is the point.<br /> <br /> V5 did one thing I find abhorrent in how they mixed Generation and Age aspects in the Blood Potency rules. Some effects, like needing to feed on &quot;stronger&quot; targets, have always been a sign of age. Others, like more potent Mending, are derived from Generation for a reason.<br /> <br /> Stuffing everything in a single trait was a stupid way of going about it. You can't have a low Gen Kindred without the effects of being old, you can't give the strangeness of age to a high Gen Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T00:49:07-07:00","id":1563930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563928#post1563928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 did one thing I find abhorrent in how they mixed Generation and Age aspects in the Blood Potency rules. Some effects, like needing to feed on &quot;stronger&quot; targets, have always been a sign of age. Others, like more potent Mending, are derived from Generation for a reason.<br /> <br /> Stuffing everything in a single trait was a stupid way of going about it. You can't have a low Gen Kindred without the effects of being old, you can't give the strangeness of age to a high Gen Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry, I misunderstood the mechanics of what you were talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T04:38:02-07:00","id":1563931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563928#post1563928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm annoyed with Char Gen rules that equate the benefits of age and Generation, something V5 did and V6 is toying with too. I'm against giving a single extra dot at anything to a low Gen character.<br /> <br /> And yes, the third Gen is a worrisome matter, if people find out. Because part of the fun with a plot like that is how hard it really is to measure someone's Generation without very specific magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah that! Yeah I'm not a fan of that either. I can't speak for others, but I'm quite harsh on what benefits age gives for vampires. If they just sit around brooding, they get nothing. If they actually DO stuff, I stat them out accordingly. In other words... I separate age, activity and generation completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T11:08:06-07:00","id":1563935,"title":"","content":"That's a reasonable take on stating elders and methsulaths Amalasuintha and I try to have a vision of what and who they are. My homebrewed 4th generation Malkavian is suffers from memory gaps and his skill set and discipline stats are geared towards trying to figure who he used to be. Not to mention he feels a certain degree of responsibility towards his kindred branch and uses some of his ability to watch over and guide when needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T14:37:45-07:00","id":1563941,"title":"","content":"That's pretty nice of him. Also a bit unusual given how kindred society is so backstabby it makes the roman empire look like toddlers in the art by comparison. So its always nice to see characters who aren't like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-09T18:24:07-07:00","id":1563942,"title":"","content":"I would hardly call him a saint as he has done terrible things in the past that he regrets and interestingly enough I had him born and embraced during height of the Roman Empire. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T01:44:37-07:00","id":1563951,"title":"","content":"To be fair to him, by default VtM kindred canon standards, he kinda is! xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-10T08:29:10-07:00","id":1563953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563906#post1563906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then Ur-Shugi isn't really fleshed out in Gehenna War and we replaced him with Issim Ur Baal in our games.</div> </div> </div> </div>But to be fair, even Gehenna War is not fleshed out in &quot;Gehenna War&quot; so yeah. <br /> <br /> And Blood Potency seems to be just one more example of making changes to the setting/systems without considering the repercussions of that on the setting/systems. One cannot just transplant part of his/hers favourite system and call it a day. They need to think on the ramification such a move has on existing themes and mechanics present in the game. And worryingly V6 playtest seems to have that in spades, this time not only from CofD but also from random other games the developers like. <br /> <br /> We can only hope that those foreign transplants that do not fit the body of VtM will be rejected in the development process. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T03:32:11-07:00","id":1564007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563953#post1563953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But to be fair, even Gehenna War is not fleshed out in &quot;Gehenna War&quot; so yeah.<br /> <br /> And Blood Potency seems to be just one more example of making changes to the setting/systems without considering the repercussions of that on the setting/systems. One cannot just transplant part of his/hers favourite system and call it a day. They need to think on the ramification such a move has on existing themes and mechanics present in the game. And worryingly V6 playtest seems to have that in spades, this time not only from CofD but also from random other games the developers like.<br /> <br /> We can only hope that those foreign transplants that do not fit the body of VtM will be rejected in the development process.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>6th edition has introduced some interesting ideas, but they still need to be tweaked a bit before they're ready to be implemented. For the most part, I like the new Diablerie system, but lowing your generation regardless of who you consume needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> Clan Traits are also a cool introduction, which I think can be used to emphasize the thematic stereotypes of how the clan presents itself, while still giving players the freedom to play a different role. Sure, this means that a Toreador will probably never reach the heights of martial mastery as a Brujah will, but issues like that don't matter to anyone who isn't a min-maxer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T04:29:44-07:00","id":1564011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563953#post1563953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And worryingly V6 playtest seems to have that in spades, this time not only from CofD but also from random other games the developers like.<br /> <br /> We can only hope that those foreign transplants that do not fit the body of VtM will be rejected in the development process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think this is a fair assessment of the playtest, as it fundamentally ignores what a playtest is and that this &quot;that in spades&quot; is simply trying ideas in a safe environment to see what sticks before even starting to flesh or polish anything.<br /> <br /> A playtest that just gave old rules back would mean a dev team that doesn't take seriously what a playtest is about. One with only a few changes would be the wrong approach to new edition, small changes are for experiments during an edition, not at transition.<br /> <br /> For all the real risk we indeed have of things taking bad turns later in development, taking the pre-alpha playtest as evidence of the final game is like taking a movie like Independence Day as evidence of how the Pentagon run crisis scenarios or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T08:19:08-07:00","id":1564013,"title":"","content":"In response to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> we disagree on Clan Traits. I much prefer clans to be bloodlines made of varied individuals instead of class (in fantasy sense, not in ideologic sense) archetypes. There is no reason that an individual Toreador could not be as good, or better, warrior as Brujah. I hate people treating clans as jobs and I think that Clan Traits might be encouraging that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564011#post1564011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all the real risk we indeed have of things taking bad turns later in development, taking the pre-alpha playtest as evidence of the final game is like taking a movie like Independence Day as evidence of how the Pentagon run crisis scenarios or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a great refutation of the argument I have not made. I even expressed hope that further development will improve the rules that were presented in the playtest. Just because a playtest is &quot;throwing shit at the wall and see what sticks&quot; it's not unfair to remark on how some of that shit stinks. Otherwise what would be the point of the surveys or this discussion.<br /> <br /> And change is neutral. I am evaluating it on the basis on how it fits the setting and it's themes and, of course, how fun they make the game. Hence I like maturing Disciplines even if they are a new mechanic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T18:11:46-07:00","id":1564027,"title":"","content":"<br /> Too many edits so post is trapped waiting for moderation so a quick repost:<br /> <br /> In response to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> we disagree on Clan Traits. I much prefer clans to be bloodlines made of varied individuals instead of class (in fantasy sense, not in ideologic sense) archetypes. There is no reason that an individual Toreador could not be as good, or better, warrior as Brujah. I hate people treating clans as jobs and I think that Clan Traits might be encouraging that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564011#post1564011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all the real risk we indeed have of things taking bad turns later in development, taking the pre-alpha playtest as evidence of the final game is like taking a movie like Independence Day as evidence of how the Pentagon run crisis scenarios or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a great refutation of the argument I have not made. I even expressed hope that further development will improve the rules that were presented in the playtest. Just because a playtest is &quot;throwing shit at the wall and see what sticks&quot; it's not unfair to remark on how some of that shit stinks. Otherwise what would be the point of the surveys or this discussion.<br /> <br /> And change is neutral. I am evaluating it on the basis on how it fits the setting and it's themes and, of course, how fun it makes the game. Hence I like maturing Disciplines even if they are a new mechanic.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T23:28:32-07:00","id":1564036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564027#post1564027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many edits so post is trapped waiting for moderation so a quick repost:<br /> <br /> In response to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> we disagree on Clan Traits. I much prefer clans to be bloodlines made of varied individuals instead of class (in fantasy sense, not in ideologic sense) archetypes. There is no reason that an individual Toreador could not be as good, or better, warrior as Brujah. I hate people treating clans as jobs and I think that Clan Traits might be encouraging that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole concept of the different clans / bloodlines, is that their founders passed on some of their more iconic characteristics down through the blood. Brujah being fiery and passionate, Toreador being artistic and seductive, Ventrue being proud and authoritative, est. In that respect, clan affiliated traits serves to highlight those characteristics and provide a stronger connection with whoever / whatever is responsible for their creation.<br /> <br /> It's not telling you that the other clans can't explore different roles outside of their stereotype. It's just pointing out that falling into that stereotype is much easier, due to having natural advantages that come with doing so.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you present the idea that any clan is able to excel at any field they desire, then it makes the whole premise of their distinction pointless. You may as well take a page from V5 Sabbat and treat everybody as Caitiff.<br /> <br /> <i>I will not being doing that!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I believe you may have put too much stock in the idea of certain clans overtaking each other within their specific fields. While a Toreador may not be able to match a Brujah as a warrior, they are still several orders of magnitude above the capability of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-14-2026, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T23:51:51-07:00","id":1564037,"title":"","content":"Also if Toreador are interested in the art of sword fighting or forms that they find beautiful. You know that they will put there heart and soul into it.<br /> <br /> I also try not to be defined by clan stereotypes as you know that some will defy that label.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T02:43:12-07:00","id":1564039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564037#post1564037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if Toreador are interested in the art of sword fighting or forms that they find beautiful. You know that they will put there heart and soul into it.<br /> <br /> I also try not to be defined by clan stereotypes as you know that some will defy that label.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely.<br /> <br /> And thanks to the formation of MMA (Mixed Martial Arts) competitions, a lot of famous styles have been exposed as more performative pieces, that failed to hold up in a practical fight.<br /> <br /> A dedicated Toreador might find the style to be aesthetically pleasing, even if it's not as effective as its reputation suggests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T08:11:22-07:00","id":1564041,"title":"","content":"The very idea that Brujah will be better warriors is a gross misrepresentation of what Clan Traits can be. At most the Brujah would excell at once particular aspect of combat, if at all, as the point of those traits is to highlight Clan Identity, not lock up roles.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the Ministry. Their Clan Traits are basically Legacy Serpentis, one of the most reviled yet loved Disciplines in VtM's history. A power set that always felt weird, suboptimal, ripped off from Protean for the most part, with zero synergy to anything else in the Clan. But nothing was more evocative, immediately iconic of a Follower of Set, than snake traits.<br /> <br /> Now they're all there without commanding space among Discipline powers, accessible at a fair price for the relative low reward, because no one really takes them thinking they'll be a game changing addition to your supernatural arsenal.<br /> <br /> And better than V5, it's properly bound to Clan rather than translated as a fucking Amalgam.<br /> <br /> What's iconic about the Brujah? Rousing the masses of downtrodden in anger, cowering the powerful through messages and actions rather than being in same room, clandestine violence that can't be properly armed, spotting the dynamics of power in a system and being passionate about it. Maybe even a rare control of Celerity that leans more in the area of having time to think, slowing the world around you, and other feats of hyper attention and reaction that look less like being fast and more like, you know, <i>bending time</i>.<br /> <br /> I personally think the playtest did a poor job with the Brujah. But that's a ridiculous reason to judge the whole concept of Clan Traits. We don't even know if they'll really be unique, or just harder to transmit. But the concept is good and has a lot of potential to re add iconic traits and powers that never really fit the Discipline structure that much.<br /> <br /> Which includes virtually every Bloodline Discipline and some Main Clan Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T09:02:22-07:00","id":1564043,"title":"","content":"Tbh im suprised how much 6th (and to a lesser degree 5th) lock you into you your clan considering the designers always person first clan second.<br /> <br /> Then again the community often seemed ambivelant and outright didnt get some clans, i recall a guy who stated a ventrue priest was breaking steriotypes (lol no) and a game designer who thought the lasombra are a poor match for the sabbat. So maybe some scaffolding is useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-14-2026, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T09:42:23-07:00","id":1564047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564043#post1564043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh im suprised how much 6th (and to a lesser degree 5th) lock you into you your clan considering the designers always person first clan second.<br /> <br /> Then again the community often seemed ambivelant and outright didnt get some clans, i recall a guy who stated a ventrue priest was breaking steriotypes (lol no) and a game designer who thought the lasombra are a poor match for the sabbat. So maybe some scaffolding is useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think v5 did it less.<br /> <br /> Clan Traits are nice, but what really locks the clan is what the playtest calls Clan Beast, and this thing is a direct transplant of v5's Clan Compulsions. It was the whole inventor of the clan stereotype being an actual mechanic.<br /> <br /> But as you noted, the community always had a damn hard time getting some concepts like &quot;stereotypes are biased by definition, they're not reality&quot;. Playing Hats is always an easier path to reward. I've heard once a friend telling of a chronicle they opened saying the Tremere Prince was hosting a party: one of the players exploded that a Tremere wouldn't ever party, get up and walked away.<br /> <br /> With Clan Traits it's easier to materialize on the games the actual reasons why clan stereotype exist, how small quirks can add momentum to direct you towards a presentation of yourself. With luck this will give more space to let minor mechanics give the scaffolding while the text goes more adamantly on how every vampire is actually an exception to something about their Clan even if they seem overall typical.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, the Clan Beasts have to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T10:19:42-07:00","id":1564048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564041#post1564041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very idea that Brujah will be better warriors is a gross misrepresentation of what Clan Traits can be. At most the Brujah would excell at once particular aspect of combat, if at all, as the point of those traits is to highlight Clan Identity, not lock up roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree. The Brujah can hit harder than any other clan in melee combat, thanks to their amplified Potence. But any seasoned fighter will probably agree that power alone is useless if you lack the skill to use it properly.<br /> <br /> The Brujah is a thug, who comes swinging at you with a baseball bat, while the Toreador is a using precise, surgical strikes against your weak spots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T10:59:16-07:00","id":1564049,"title":"","content":"Someone thought that a Venture priest didn't fit the clan archetype? A clan that views itself as the rulers of the damned are not going to overlook avenues of influence and I seem to recall that in the dark ages that one of the most prominent Ventrue elders was heavily involved in the Catholic Church. So this is very much on brand for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T12:41:58-07:00","id":1564051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564047#post1564047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ic.<br /> <br /> But as you noted, the community always had a damn hard time getting some concepts like &quot;stereotypes are biased by definition, they're not reality&quot;. Playing Hats is always an easier path to reward. I've heard once a friend telling of a chronicle they opened saying the Tremere Prince was hosting a party: one of the players exploded that a Tremere wouldn't ever party, get up and walked away.<br /> <br /> With Clan Traits it's easier to materialize on the games the actual reasons why clan stereotype exist, how small quirks can add momentum to direct you towards a presentation of yourself. With luck this will give more space to let minor mechanics give the scaffolding while the text goes more adamantly on how every vampire is actually an exception to something about their Clan even if they seem overall typical.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, the Clan Beasts have to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is how players perceive clans as the stereotype rather than the archetype, a Tremere prince is weird but an interesting plot beat rather than a sin. A clans archetype is a framework for new players to feel comfortable with which makes them very useful as well as providing the setting with flavour, their isnt even anything wrong with player them as experienced. I recall a Ventrue (adapted from requiem) who had the monstrous flaw so set himself up as Baron and infiltrated into the local homeless support networks-which perfectly meshed with ventrue's tendency to integrate into power structure.<br /> <br /> Once you understand what they're really about it's so easy to work with rather than against. I'm unsure the mechanics are needed as much better scaffolding, especially for more unusual clans<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T12:44:36-07:00","id":1564052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564049#post1564049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone thought that a Venture priest didn't fit the clan archetype? A clan that views itself as the rulers of the damned are not going to overlook avenues of influence and I seem to recall that in the dark ages that one of the most prominent Ventrue elders was heavily involved in the Catholic Church. So this is very much on brand for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly trying to think of clans which are hard to justify as some sort of priest or another.....the sheer variety of religions means their's always going to be someone who can fit. some of the bloodline perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T12:48:59-07:00","id":1564053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564049#post1564049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone thought that a Venture priest didn't fit the clan archetype? A clan that views itself as the rulers of the damned are not going to overlook avenues of influence and I seem to recall that in the dark ages that one of the most prominent Ventrue elders was heavily involved in the Catholic Church. So this is very much on brand for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Ventrue go where the power is. In the ancient times, this included members of the clergy, as well the nobility.<br /> <br /> Embracing boardroom CEO's only became a thing in the modern nights, as the scales of power shifted away from aristocratic and theological institutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T12:58:04-07:00","id":1564054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564053#post1564053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Ventrue go where the power is. In the ancient times, this included members of the clergy, as well the nobility.<br /> <br /> Embracing boardroom CEO's only became a thing in the modern nights, as the scales of power shifted away from aristocratic and theological institutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's something a lot of people miss, the Ventrue are drawn to institutional power rather than specific stuff. It's why they were medieval barons, then aristocrats the corporate oligarchs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T13:03:20-07:00","id":1564055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564054#post1564054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it's something a lot of people miss, the Ventrue are drawn to institutional power rather than specific stuff. It's why they were medieval barons, then aristocrats the corporate oligarchs</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was also customary for many noble families to send their 'surplus' children off to join the clergy. Meaning that even within the church, there would have been a strong presence of noble blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T13:44:55-07:00","id":1564057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564055#post1564055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe it was also customary for many noble families to send their 'surplus' children off to join the clergy. Meaning that even within the church, there would have been a strong presence of noble blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>which in turn links to the institutional power of the church, allowing nobles to get a cut of that pie.<br /> <br /> The political clans (which is all clanskinda) all pursue power in subtly different ways, the Toreador lean the most into soft power through social elites, the Brujah also lean into soft power a lot but through populism and mass mobilisation, the lasombra are individualistic and more exploitive of institutions, they also have a tendacy to look for power in odd places (abyss mysticism, pirates) were they'll find it easier to build a personal monopoly.<br /> The Ventrue are probably the most effective since their internal organisation, policy to other kindred and acquirement of power over humans all follows the same model so synergises really really well. so the idea the Ventrue wouldnt ever take interest in priesthoods is absurd, they may shit away from the Catholic due to the 2nd inq and the lasombra but theirs so many more out their. I can easily imagine ventrue inams or Purohita's. Once you understand why they're drawn to corporations and old boy networks then it becomes easy to apply that logic elsewhere while remaining consistant with what the clan is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T14:38:12-07:00","id":1564059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564057#post1564057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> which in turn links to the institutional power of the church, allowing nobles to get a cut of that pie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lastly, we can't ignore the fact that a coronation ceremony often required the endorsement of the church in order to officially legitimize it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T00:34:39-07:00","id":1564068,"title":"","content":"The reason I'm interested in a smart use of Traits is that I actually think this leaning into Clan archetype is excessive. I actively dislike it.<br /> <br /> I lean heavily on the idea the individual Vampire is first a person with zero reason to follow the culture of the abomination who turned them. Your society not having a place for you doesn't change it is the framework you have for reality and that goes deep.<br /> <br /> So the whole Toreador are artists, Brujah are thugs and Ventrue are power players for me is a huge ball of bullshit. And that IS the fun, to be thrown in a reality that empowers and curses you into a path that's not your nature.<br /> <br /> But the archetypes exist for a reason. What so happens is that this reason usually isn't culture because there's little real common culture in a Clan to begin with. My take is that this is the result of details of the Curse that nudge things and then create the space for a stereotype to appear.<br /> <br /> Exceptions exist, there's nuance, but that's the baseline. Most vampires aren't an expression of the archetype: they're in friction with it, but in different ways. The Ventrue Neonate pay lip service to a cult of &quot;lineage&quot; of a curse, but they are in real danger to life if they don't learn the spiel. A Toreador can't help but be stuck in the spot admiring things they legitimately find boring, and reach others who share in this type of experience to learn coping strategies.<br /> <br /> My preferred take is that. To ask how does a mundane mind react in response to the curse and its alien &quot;physiology&quot;. It so happens that to me a direct change in personality \u2013 be it explained as a Beast or as Clan culture \u2013 is the least interesting exploration, a blunt tool to turn the vampire into a Planet of the Hats kinda thing that's shallow and asinine.<br /> <br /> Clan Traits have a chance of doing that since as powers/mutations they're less prescriptive of who you are and more of what you've been empowered to do.<br /> <br /> What most players do with VtM, in my sincere opinion, is if anything more appropriate to the Japanese take on Vampires: a blood sucking Youkai that has never been something else. A race proper, from crib to final destruction. And I don't think this is a bad take, it's just not what VtM describes and the transition breaks my immersion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T06:27:29-07:00","id":1564079,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> While I understand where you're coming from, and agree with you in a strictly technical sense that vampires don't necessarily need to adhere to stereotypes, I think that the chances of a vampire being chosen for the embrace are quite low, if they did not at least exhibit some of their qualities. The low clans might be less selective about who they bring into the fold, but those high clans have more distinguished criteria.<br /> <br /> Both the <b>Ventrue</b> and the <b>Assamites</b> put their childer through a grueling training period before they are ever allowed to meet the public. I don't know the duration of such for Ventrue, but in the case of the Assamites, it lasts for 7 years.<br /> <br /> <b>Giovanni</b> embrace exclusively from their own mortal family, and only the most successful among them are granted that honor.<br /> <br /> <b>Followers of Set</b> are a full blown cult, who don't grant the embrace until they are certain you've been fully indoctrinated.<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra</b> will cast you aside like trash, if you lack the strength and tenacity to rebuild your life after they systematically destroy it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b> have spells in place that allow your superiors to monitor your thoughts and behavior from long distance, and would certainly be aware if any new apprentices aren't living up to their expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T09:31:42-07:00","id":1564083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29027_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29027\" data-vbnamecard=\"29027\">GreatHornedRatkin</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564068#post1564068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptions exist, there's nuance, but that's the baseline. Most vampires aren't an expression of the archetype: they're in friction with it, but in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's break down my take on the matter:<br /> <br /> 1. The core books state repeatedly that kindred are not consistent in Embraces. It's true that as far as they can, the Ventrue will chose the best. But it's also plainly clear that their actual ability to enforce this or make the best choices is limited at best. That goes for most.<br /> <br /> 2. A lot of clans don't do that at the same level, or at all. Those who do either have a limit or go through a excruciating process that still gives us clear friction points and costs. It's not about Clan culture being real or not, but how deep it goes, which isn't a binary.<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Some of their qualities&quot; and close to their stereotypes are two different things. I lean a lot more in the former than most.<br /> <br /> 4. Low vs High Clans is the single stupidest thing in VDA. Full stop. And this is also false: Toreador, Malkavian and Gangrel royally don't care, Nosferatu are very selective and involve a whole Warren. Tzimisce followed family lines but stopped at that, and the Cappadocians are literally the clan that most Embraced whatever and only barely changed ways after the Feast.<br /> <br /> 5. Friction is the key concept: what you were is in conflict with what other factors press you to be. My interest is in exploring this conflict. You are the nexus of many independent influences and will respond to each while still feeling the others. How that generates idiosyncrasies is what I like to see. In this sense, Clan influence is crucial, don't get me wrong, it just has to not be the end of it.<br /> <br /> 6. A lot of players go strictly Clan stereotype, from Fledgling to Methuselah, that's stupid. But I must add that, for me, the idea of &quot;their mortal days were so long ago they don't play a part anymore&quot; isn't just arguable at best, it is just an uninspired excuse to flatten the character.<br /> <br /> 7. As I'll show, how far a clan goes to make the members fit shouldn't be incidental, but rather a defining trait. That should show up in many more ways than simply being effective.<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Ventrue</b> are not grueling. That wouldn't allow for the infiltration they favor, as they need to be able to incorporate new elites and knowledge constantly. They're also capable at hiding their indiscretions from each other. Ventrue ideal is to become the best of the best. Ventrue reality is that most of them are at best midway to the ideal, and frequently those who best perform the archetype are the farther from its values. I take it from knowing corporate elites and how much their competence is smoke and mirrors.<br /> <br /> 9. <b>Banu Haqim</b> are gruesome. They're also zealots that live collectively in a palace, not a warren for those in the city, a single castle for the whole clan. Or at least did so until recently. They also frequently ask permission to their prospect for the Embrace, they follow dozens of strict rules, and they actively hunt those who don't fit. Not destroy if convenient, hunt. Even then there's plenty of space for differences to appear.<br /> <br /> 10. <b>Giovanni</b> is a prime example for what going through pains to ensure conformity means. It's so strict you're watched by the collective Clan since you're a child. Not Fledgling, a turns-milk-into-poop child. Your sire may even have been your babysitter for a night or two in the past, a monster you met every Sunday at family dinner and in holidays. Even if the Embrace was not a choice, it was family duty rather than external predation. And they conciliate the friction between vampire society and mortal society making both the same god you, there's zero &quot;unlearning&quot; involved.<br /> <br /> 11. <b>Followers of Set</b> were turned into Ministry precisely because they had more schisms than anything and that was not actually v5 invention, it has been in the making since 2nd Edition. And since cults are a real thing that affect real people, I can also point you to the fact that the indoctrination has limits and cult escapees are a thing. By the way, their stories are underused in VtM, and I imagine many from the clan being such people.<br /> <br /> 12. <b>Lasombra</b> Social Darwinism is philosophic trash as it has been repeatedly demonstrated with Social Darwinism in reality. The books do a poor job demonstrating that their spiel does not really correspond to their reality, with many authors believing this bullshit, so let me be clear: <i>if they were competent at doing what they claim, that itself would undermine their uniformity</i>. For them, the stereotype itself is a logical fallacy.<br /> <br /> 13. <b>Tremere</b> don't have such spells, to begin with. Otherwise wouldn't be the most infiltrated Clan in canon. They have strict vigilance, which is key to their concept, but it has serious limits, which is also important. It also doesn't ensure archetype, it ensures obedience, which is a very different thing. It should be where the struggle is the most intense, because it's the Clan that enforces conformity most directly and rigidly through imposition. <hr /><br /> Final words: I'm not saying my take is the most correct. The books allow many takes, and in fact it is impossible to be 100% true to them as all possible interpretations of canon also require you to place distinct weights in each part.<br /> <br /> My points, thus, are:<br /> 1. The books allow the above take fully within canon;<br /> 2. Many popular takes actually conflict with canon, as it is meant to be nuanced;<br /> 3. I don't avoid full archetypal integration because I find it unofficial, I avoid it because I don't like it. I like the conflict better. Everything else is accessory to my preference and you should favor yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T11:15:09-07:00","id":1564089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564083#post1564083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;29027&quot;]<br /> 5. Friction is the key concept: what you were is in conflict with what other factors press you to be. My interest is in exploring this conflict. You are the nexus of many independent influences and will respond to each while still feeling the others. How that generates idiosyncrasies is what I like to see. In this sense, Clan influence is crucial, don't get me wrong, it just has to not be the end of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I too enjoy playing characters who break the classical mold, but I usually do it more as a joke. I find such characters as the Orc Wizard, or the Gnome Barbarian amusing, because of how wildly unexpected they are.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, a Nosferatu who embraces Absimiliard's legacy as the greatest hunter would be awesome to see. Instead of hiding in the warrens, working cyber security, he's going out into the city and beating the living shit out of whoever is causing problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T12:40:49-07:00","id":1564093,"title":"","content":"my thought on playing the clans archetypes are simply they're often a good thing because well.... <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ede95ekWAng\" data-code=\"Ede95ekWAng\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ede95ekWAng/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Their's something for playing a nightmarishly evil fiend or a mega capitalist bastard blue blood to the point I'll sometimes deliberately go to 11 with them-my last Tremere was Saruman the white with boobs. My gf had a lot of fun playing a nightmarishly evil fiend for example. The other advantage is its easy scaffolding to build a more complex pc from. I also enjoy the idea of clans having ecological niches and cultural trends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T12:45:25-07:00","id":1564094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564083#post1564083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 12. <b>Lasombra</b> Social Darwinism is philosophic trash as it has been repeatedly demonstrated with Social Darwinism in reality. The books do a poor job demonstrating that their spiel does not really correspond to their reality, <b>with many authors believing this bullshit,</b> so let me be clear: <i>if they were competent at doing what they claim, that itself would undermine their uniformity</i>. For them, the stereotype itself is a logical fallacy.<br /> yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a common issue with the lasombra in the community and the writers, they believe the lasombra's own IC statements about themselves. I recall I got this banger for playing a lasombra who was superficially pleasant (key word: superficially)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going against the norm is lazy thinking. It's inability to assume the role of a real Lasombra. For some reason, the people who think they're doing something different always act and thing almost identically because they cannot adapt their thinking and separate their character from their own personality and fantasies. What is described here is not only lazy thinking, but an utter lack of creativity as well. Essentially we have the &quot;I wanna play a bad guy but I also want people to like me&quot; - approach, which has to be the most unoriginal and uninspired take on anything ever. This is less original than simply fully embracing being a cliche. You have to respect and understand the stereotype before you can give it your own spin, and not try to force your own personality onto the concept. You're not open minded, you are incapable of playing a plausible Lasombra. You want to eat your cake and have it too without having thought through the causal consequences of either option. </div> </div> </div>.....it went on like this for another 4 paragraphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T14:59:45-07:00","id":1564096,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a> We like the bad guys, because they seem to be having fun as the bad guys. The most memorable villains from my childhood were the ones who fully embraced their wickedness and owned up to the fact they weren't good people. Yes, they were evil, and yes they did some bad things that hurt people. <b>But they had charisma.</b><br /> <br /> Any villain who tried to justify themselves with some cry-baby backstory that caused them to lash out at the world have been forgotten over the years.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a likable villain, go for the performative evil, not the sympathetic kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-15T16:30:28-07:00","id":1564100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564093#post1564093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their's something for playing a nightmarishly evil fiend or a mega capitalist bastard blue blood to the point I'll sometimes deliberately go to 11 with them-my last Tremere was Saruman the white with boobs. My gf had a lot of fun playing a nightmarishly evil fiend for example. The other advantage is its easy scaffolding to build a more complex pc from. I also enjoy the idea of clans having ecological niches and cultural trends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully endorse people who play to clich\u00e9s and whatnot when that's self aware. It's not something I'm in the mood for frequently, but I find that to be indeed a flaw of mine. It's when people don't get the joke and start talking bullshit that I get pissed. I can accept different tastes, I can accept ignorance. I can't accept so easily misinformation and general stupidity, like this Lasombra ball licker boy you found.<br /> <br /> As for villains, that depends a lot, and it is too easy to look at the matter with a biased selection.<br /> <br /> But the simplest reason why most memorable villains are performative is because they were accessories to another person's story and this accessory has to stand out in the time they get in the spotlight. This convention is mostly for cinema and to a lesser extent TV, as the media favors simplifying narrative elements to convey the message within seconds.<br /> <br /> Most villains we don't even know if they have a justification, there's this tendency of assuming that not being told something in a story means it didn't happened. But when sequels and what have you come, they either avoid talking about the villain or eventually make the sympathetic part, because its lack was actually a narrative need, not a point.<br /> <br /> Genre plays another spin on this, so you'll have a pretty different experience depending on the movies and media you like, and... Gothic is all about sympathetic villains. The genre is built upon the premise that the villain could have been better, and is the ultimate cause of their own tragedy. So VtM actually comes from a tradition of sympathetic villains, and the game is very clearly built to support them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T23:54:56-07:00","id":1564137,"title":"","content":"I try to not to fall into clan stereotypes as much as I can, but I it's so easy to fall into the habit as each clan has it preferences and I still try to remember who the kindred was before when they were human and since I usually play kindred who max out around the 250 year mark as a personal choice as I can better picture what life would be like for them then someone born thousands of years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T00:37:38-07:00","id":1564138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564137#post1564137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I try to not to fall into clan stereotypes as much as I can, but I it's so easy to fall into the habit as each clan has it preferences and I still try to remember who the kindred was before when they were human and since I usually play kindred who max out around the 250 year mark as a personal choice as I can better picture what life would be like for them then someone born thousands of years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, it should be mandatory for all Elders and Methuselah characters to become Bi / Multi Lingual.<br /> <br /> Not because they are properly educated in foreign dialects, but simply by virtue of how language continues to evolve over time.<br /> <br /> Modern day English and medieval English are extremely different from each other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T07:36:58-07:00","id":1564139,"title":"","content":"That reminds me of the tumblr post that keeps floating around of old vampires having a horrendous mix of incompatible slang from over the decades and centuries. In fact you just made me look it up. The line was:<br /> <br /> &quot;Unhand me, you egg-sucking, lily-livered, jive-talking, whackadoo. Foul villain! Cur! I bite my thumb at thee, you ugly m___ f___, so hasta la bye bye, daddy-o!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T10:57:36-07:00","id":1564140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564138#post1564138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, it should be mandatory for all Elders and Methuselah characters to become Bi / Multi Lingual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Some people actively forget how they used to speak a few decades ago, it isn't unlikely that a vampire with little attention to such details would do the same.<br /> <br /> Also, VtM books are quite clear that vampires in the setting adapt to language abnormally fast. While anachronistic speech is a recurring motif among players, the actual books make it mostly non existent. Any Methuselah speaking in outdated fashion either woke very recently or are uncommon exceptions, not the norm, even possibly more affectation than real difficulty to catch on.<br /> <br /> V5 is the only corebook that doesn't talk about this directly, and even it has makes no reference to the related Flaw being common, just that it exists.<br /> <br /> Overall, though the cost of learning languages in the WoD systems is overall too high to make it a regular part of the game. Which I actually find quite boring. As hard as actually learning a new language is, making it costly in the game only results in this being done sparingly or never, what removes the whole theme from the game rather than giving it teeth.<br /> <br /> I think that deriving languages from something other than exclusive language traits would help a lot. For example, We could have Language as a specialization for Intelligence and Academics that, if chosen, let you know as many extra languages as your dots in those traits. If you don't have them, you still get an extra language at 4th dot in each. And outside it you can learn languages without XP or at a fixed 1 XP per language cost.<br /> <br /> The world has more than 20 thousand languages in use today. Giving people a dozen extras won't make anyone an universal translator, but will increase enormously the presence of languages as an element in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T11:29:22-07:00","id":1564141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564138#post1564138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Come to think of it, it should be mandatory for all Elders and Methuselah characters to become Bi / Multi Lingual.<br /> <br /> Not because they are properly educated in foreign dialects, but simply by virtue of how language continues to evolve over time.<br /> <br /> Modern day English and medieval English are extremely different from each other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Smart elders and methsulaths would need to learn to speak numerous languages over the ages, it helps them to blend in better and sells the notion of how they have endured.<br /> <br /> But my homebrewed ancient Malkavian Latin might be rusty as it's not a widely spoken dialect anymore and many like him would be speaking more contemporary and properly and not use slang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T20:43:40-07:00","id":1564156,"title":"","content":"What's even slang for someone who saw millennia of linguistic drift?<br /> <br /> Everything regarded now as proper form was at some point (and sometimes not even that long ago) slang, neologism, accent, what have you.<br /> <br /> They didn't saw people change from Old English to Modern English. They saw slang and all sorts of linguistic &quot;vices&quot; being added, build up over each other, go from reviled to widespread, until the &quot;same&quot; language was but unrecognizable from centuries before despite being perfectly understandable, just with a new fad, from one year to the other.<br /> <br /> Such a Methuselah either never paid attention and just adopted whatever people use around them, or they noticed long ago that the &quot;proper form&quot; of today frequently has little to do with the actual past, as even old people who speak like in their young days actually don't, but rather mixture their old accents with adaptations they took as time went on.<br /> <br /> Better to say they keep up with a given class or environment. Maybe they keep business lingo, or academic, or talk like octogenarian farmers from the southern frontier. But &quot;no slang&quot;, just as &quot;no accent&quot;, is not actually a thing and both most multilingual people and any Methuselah with this kind of attention, would know it too well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T11:55:10-07:00","id":1564168,"title":"","content":"The language thing is often ignored for convenience's sake. I am in a VtDA campaign atm and after a couple decades spent in Constantinople my mate, who is the ST, said that we are starting to feel disconnected from the language and so we all found ways to interact with mortals to keep up with evolving speech. But many people won't bother with highlighting that in their games or even be unconscious of it happening.<br /> <br /> And also I would not begrudge anyone ignoring this aspect because this is one of those Rockstar techniques to bring realism into their games like horses dangling penis in RDR2 or stacking the fridge in GTA VI (which they decided to remove eventually): cool thing that might help immersion for some but intrusive and pointless for the rest.<br /> <br /> Bonus meme: I roftled hard when I read about that player quitting because Tremere do not throw parties. Hilarious. Even more so considering that you do not have to be a party animal to organise one - party is a social gathering like any other and can have multiple functions other than, you know, having a blast. You can use it as a sign of status, to divert attention, to draw someone into the limelight. That guy is a perfect example why I hate people seeing clans &quot;only&quot; as stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T12:35:56-07:00","id":1564170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564168#post1564168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus meme: I roftled hard when I read about that player quitting because Tremere do not throw parties. Hilarious. Even more so considering that you do not have to be a party animal to organise one - party is a social gathering like any other and can have multiple functions other than, you know, having a blast. You can use it as a sign of status, to divert attention, to draw someone into the limelight. That guy is a perfect example why I hate people seeing clans &quot;only&quot; as stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they were hosting the party as a means of celebrating a recent promotion, or passing a particularly difficult examination!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T02:33:11-07:00","id":1564175,"title":"","content":"So apparently the V6 devs heavy implied in a Q&amp;A event that the collation/Second inquisition have collapsed or at least hampered due to hubris (and AI of all things) something along those lines.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/N2MG-4hxCRw?is=OlpTIX1M8FnWeZYf%C2%A0\" data-code=\"N2MG-4hxCRw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N2MG-4hxCRw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> relevant info at around 36:50<br /> <br /> Like the wording is very vague but I suspect that SI won't have much presence in the V6 corebook besides side bars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 09-19-2026, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:06:19-07:00","id":1564176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564175#post1564175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently the V6 devs heavy implied in a Q&amp;A event that the collation/Second inquisition have collapsed or at least hampered due to hubris (and AI of all things) something along those lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like the wording is very vague but I suspect that SI won't have much presence in the V6 corebook besides side bars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good riddance to bad rubbish.<br /> <br /> Now let's make sure a 3rd Inquisition never kicks off the ground.<br /> <br /> 1st order of business, tear down the Camarilla, because they're the ones responsible for the last two!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:19:12-07:00","id":1564177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1563870#post1563870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My only correction here is that the people taking it as gospel weren't every DtF fans, and in fact some weren't DtF fans at all.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda tired of diatribes about how &quot;DtF kidnapped the whole setting&quot; because it didn't actually did anything new.<br /> <br /> Werewolf, Mage and Changeling all had done the exact same thing: establish cosmologies that include and retcon everything else. And it includes their later editions catching up to cover things that came after initial release.<br /> <br /> The people saying something wasn't canon anymore because of DtF were talking bullshit, but this bullshit had been around for a long time without the same vitriolic reaction.reaction.<br /> <br /> Seriously, why Demon has to be sensible to the cosmologies of others? This was not what the WoD was about. Why Demon has to hold to a standard developed in CoD while Werewolf say that Vampires are fomors, Mage say Garou are mindbogglingly ignorant of the spiritual worlds, and Changeling is adamant that all splats are just mutated Kithain?<br /> <br /> And all those have the same problem of fans who want to force this interpretation into other games. Even because they all have some way to claim objective knowledge of what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Demon is being blamed for doing something it was in no way wrong at doing, because it was held to a standard all other lines had already rejected. I don't accept this accusation as valid or legitimate. It was an independent line with full legitimacy to make independent claims for its version of the setting. If someone takes that and extrapolate to say DtF is objectively right outside its own books, this is a problem of this person, not of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the late reply (I'm currently finishing my PhD), but I agree with all of this. I don't think the problem was DTF, but the way (some) DTF fans interpreted it. I actually like DTF. I just didn't like that particular attitude at the time (which seems to have died down considerably since the 2000s, but occasionally rears its head).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:31:59-07:00","id":1564178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564177#post1564177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for the late reply (I'm currently finishing my PhD), but I agree with all of this. I don't think the problem was DTF, but the way (some) DTF fans interpreted it. I actually like DTF. I just didn't like that particular attitude at the time (which seems to have died down considerably since the 2000s, but occasionally rears its head).</div> </div> </div> </div>No excuses, you cannot prioritise personal education above your duties to the internet forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Good luck with your PhD. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:37:22-07:00","id":1564179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564178#post1564178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No excuses, you cannot prioritise personal education above your duties to the internet forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Good luck with your PhD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! The deadline is 30th September, so I'm right on the cusp. It feels like it's all on track, but there's always something that crops up at the last moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T03:57:47-07:00","id":1564181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564175#post1564175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently the V6 devs heavy implied in a Q&amp;A event that the collation/Second inquisition have collapsed or at least hampered due to hubris (and AI of all things) something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>A time stamp would have been appreciated.<br /> <br /> Looks like they address it at the 36:50 mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T04:10:34-07:00","id":1564182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564175#post1564175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So apparently the V6 devs heavy implied in a Q&amp;A event that the collation/Second inquisition have collapsed or at least hampered due to hubris (and AI of all things) something along those lines.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/N2MG-4hxCRw?is=OlpTIX1M8FnWeZYf%C2%A0\" data-code=\"N2MG-4hxCRw\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/N2MG-4hxCRw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> relevant info at around 36:50<br /> <br /> Like the wording is very vague but I suspect that SI won't have much presence in the V6 corebook besides side bars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Makes sense, it isnt v5's fault but they were somewhat incorrect in their route of how they explored state survelance with big tech going forward combined with the practical issue that v5 treated the 2nd inq as a mass extinction event but didnt really engage with the ramifications. I'd probably go a little deeper than AI as it's a symptom of our state of unreality atm rather than the actual cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T04:31:34-07:00","id":1564183,"title":"","content":"Second Inquisition is one of those developments I am agnostic about. I would not be generally using it as written as I wasn't the fun of Mage Revised metaplot either. But I know some people love it and I could use it WAW for a single chronicle if I felt like it, it's a fine idea for &quot;hunter becoming hunted&quot; type of deal. <br /> <br /> As such I have no strong feelings towards this but I have seen many V5 fans being disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T04:47:14-07:00","id":1564185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564183#post1564183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Inquisition is one of those developments I am agnostic about. I would not be generally using it as written as I wasn't the fun of Mage Revised metaplot either. But I know some people love it and I could use it WAW for a single chronicle if I felt like it, it's a fine idea for &quot;hunter becoming hunted&quot; type of deal.<br /> <br /> As such I have no strong feelings towards this but I have seen many V5 fans being disappointed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like a lot of v5 it's a neat idea but with questionable execution.<br /> <br /> Me to but to be candid I find it hard to particularly sympathetic to a lot of v5 players considering their attitude to feedback, Sabbat players or issues with the edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T04:59:05-07:00","id":1564186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564182#post1564182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Makes sense, it isnt v5's fault but they were somewhat incorrect in their route of how they explored state survelance with big tech going forward combined with the practical issue that v5 treated the 2nd inq as a mass extinction event but didnt really engage with the ramifications. I'd probably go a little deeper than AI as it's a symptom of our state of unreality atm rather than the actual cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, the Technocracy shoots itself in the foot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T05:21:30-07:00","id":1564187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564185#post1564185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like a lot of v5 it's a neat idea but with questionable execution.<br /> <br /> Me to but to be candid I find it hard to particularly sympathetic to a lot of v5 players considering their attitude to feedback, Sabbat players or issues with the edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well personally I would like to have them survive into H6 in some form to open the possibility that they're might be playable for H6. Like V6 are taking steps to make the Sabbat playable again for caines shake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T06:47:20-07:00","id":1564189,"title":"","content":"I have a Tremere NPC that was chosen <i><b>because</b></i> she's a party animal, and sometimes the clan needs one. She may not be going far in the regular hierarchy, but she is the clan's face in her area, deals with other clans, host events and manage a nightclub that gives the clan both a feeding ground and revenue.<br /> <br /> The SI could not have happened and still have the whole surveillance thing, because the crux of it isn't actually the surveillance, but a notion of disparate groups and nations working together in the shadows. Remove it and hunters with access to surveillance apparel remain extremely dangerous without pretending something like vampires will make almost 200 countries and about 10 to 12 active wars at any given time suddenly become best buddies.<br /> <br /> And there's no need for the Second Inquisition to make its constituent groups playable. I am really getting tired of the SI being treated as a discreet thing and not a novelty fad involving far older threats to vampires.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> rooting for you, good luck with your presentation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T09:03:12-07:00","id":1564192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564187#post1564187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well personally I would like to have them survive into H6 in some form to open the possibility that they're might be playable for H6. Like V6 are taking steps to make the Sabbat playable again for caines shake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what both of those things have in common but ok. <br /> <br /> So far there was nary a peep about H6 so I would not worry too much about it. Also I doubt that SI will be gone, I am sure it will survive in SOME form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T09:51:23-07:00","id":1564193,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that they are keeping Hunter and Werewolf actively published in 5e and advancing Vampire to 6e. There has also been some mention of possibly publishing Mage, Changeling and Vampire the Dark Ages in 6e at some point in the future, but right now the design team is focusing exclusively on 6e Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T10:25:52-07:00","id":1564194,"title":"","content":"Seriously, you can almost say V6 is already a success with how some people are eager for seeing other WoD 6 lines.<br /> <br /> V6 is in Pr\u00e9 Alpha Playtest. There's no sign of it approaching anything resembling completion. However it is advancing in closed doors right now, it's still far from release even if no other playtests are done.<br /> <br /> Let's get this one thing right first before we get to dream about replicating the method. No one will die from a few more years playing old editions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T14:09:10-07:00","id":1564196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564192#post1564192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure what both of those things have in common but ok.<br /> <br /> So far there was nary a peep about H6 so I would not worry too much about it. Also I doubt that SI will be gone, I am sure it will survive in SOME form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully in the form of crazy preachers, ranting on the street corner about monsters walking among us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T15:48:13-07:00","id":1564197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564194#post1564194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, you can almost say V6 is already a success with how some people are eager for seeing other WoD 6 lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well not exactly eager just morbidly curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T10:42:27-07:00","id":1564216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564194#post1564194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, you can almost say V6 is already a success with how some people are eager for seeing other WoD 6 lines.<br /> <br /> V6 is in Pr\u00e9 Alpha Playtest. There's no sign of it approaching anything resembling completion. However it is advancing in closed doors right now, it's still far from release even if no other playtests are done.<br /> <br /> Let's get this one thing right first before we get to dream about replicating the method. No one will die from a few more years playing old editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Announcing, even if only tentatively, Mage and Changeling was a good marketing move. MtA and CtD fans are starved for content since those games got nothing with Fifth Edition so even if some people loath to see Paradox tackling their beloved systems many others are awaiting M6 and C6. <br /> <br /> In this sense Paradox is doing what they should be. It has been 8 years since WoD5 started so it is due for a revision. And even tho I have low amounts of hope V6 is going to be to my liking I am still interested to see what Paradox is going to cook. And who knows, V6 can always surprise me positively, stranger things have happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T10:56:34-07:00","id":1564217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564216#post1564216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Announcing, even if only tentatively, Mage and Changeling was a good marketing move. MtA and CtD fans are starved for content since those games got nothing with Fifth Edition so even if some people loath to see Paradox tackling their beloved systems many others are awaiting M6 and C6.<br /> <br /> In this sense Paradox is doing what they should be. It has been 8 years since WoD5 started so it is due for a revision. And even tho I have low amounts of hope V6 is going to be to my liking I am still interested to see what Paradox is going to cook. And who knows, V6 can always surprise me positively, stranger things have happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly I've noticed a lot of Mage players seem unclear if they even want a 5th/6th ed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T11:11:21-07:00","id":1564219,"title":"","content":"Well, it's the issue with generalisation. I can say &quot;many Mage fans are looking forward to M6&quot; and you can say &quot;a lot of Mage players seem to be unclear whether they want&quot; a new edition and we will both be correct. It's just a vibe comment, neither of us has solid data, we are just drawing conclusions on what we have seen online or in our immediate friend groups. <br /> <br /> Hell, I could say both of those statement because some people want new Mage game, some don't. People have varied approach to that and different feels on what a new Paradox game can bring. To paraphrase the great philosopher, Bo Burnham, we are just saying our shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T11:28:11-07:00","id":1564221,"title":"","content":"I am curious to see where the promise of M6 and C6 will take us, but I think it too early to make even remotely educated guesses about how they'll be. Those guesses are based on a pack of rules we don't know what it'll look like when released, much less how they can be adapted to other lines.<br /> <br /> V6 may end up being almost exactly like the Playtest. It may also end up throwing the rules all away and making something else entirely. It is not basis for anything resembling a safe bet on how anything else may end up looking like after an already unknown future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T13:06:41-07:00","id":1564222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564221#post1564221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to see where the promise of M6 and C6 will take us, but I think it too early to make even remotely educated guesses about how they'll be. Those guesses are based on a pack of rules we don't know what it'll look like when released, much less how they can be adapted to other lines.<br /> <br /> V6 may end up being almost exactly like the Playtest. It may also end up throwing the rules all away and making something else entirely. It is not basis for anything resembling a safe bet on how anything else may end up looking like after an already unknown future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a prediction right now, if they're using the advent of AI generated content as a justification for the vampires managing to survive the SI, then it's probably going to be hellish on the Changelings.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is in more peril now than it's ever been before, as humanity abandons its capacity for imagination in favor of letting machines do their creative thinking for them.<br /> <br /> What could be more banal than typing a string of prompts into an AI Generator, and then slapping your signature on whatever pale imitation of somebody else's work the machine decides to churn out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T19:40:44-07:00","id":1564224,"title":"","content":"I can state a lot of things, but that can also be said from all previous editions of Changeling. I don't think AI significantly changed Banality even if the way it's used has been bringing down quality, but that's the crushing hand of exploitation, AI is just its latest tool.<br /> <br /> But I do bet they will do something like that and equate AI = Banal as default just like the game always equated science and reason with Banal no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T20:44:25-07:00","id":1564225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564217#post1564217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly I've noticed a lot of Mage players seem unclear if they even want a 5th/6th ed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's me. I'm a Mage fans who thinks, &quot;How about No?&quot;<br /> <br /> I had no interest in seeing what kind of garbage fire M5 would have been. And since it's still Paradox in charge, I'm not that jazzed about a M6 either. What difference would it make? I don't trust them to be able to helm Mage: The Ascension without derailing it or putting all the good/interesting bits in the shredder.<br /> <br /> I'm just...so tired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T20:50:35-07:00","id":1564226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564224#post1564224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can state a lot of things, but that can also be said from all previous editions of Changeling. I don't think AI significantly changed Banality even if the way it's used has been bringing down quality, but that's the crushing hand of exploitation, AI is just its latest tool.<br /> <br /> But I do bet they will do something like that and equate AI = Banal as default just like the game always equated science and reason with Banal no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>On this point, I actually think you could say something about the Plagiarism Machine as being Banal, not because it's scientific, but because using it literally (clinically) shreds your capacity for creativity or original thought. They've done studies about this. User-facing LLMs condition people to abdicate all thinking to the bot. In business, art, education, whatever. When it's used on a wide scale, it actively inhibits cognitive thought and development.<br /> <br /> Technology can very much be a force of creativity and wonder. The Plagiarism Machine is exactly the opposite. It's antithetical to the Changeling condition. A world where &quot;AI&quot; is allowed to proliferate is one where Winter comes. The death of dreams, reduced to grist for the mill of mangled machine-output.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T22:07:45-07:00","id":1564227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564224#post1564224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can state a lot of things, but that can also be said from all previous editions of Changeling. I don't think AI significantly changed Banality even if the way it's used has been bringing down quality, but that's the crushing hand of exploitation, AI is just its latest tool.<br /> <br /> But I do bet they will do something like that and equate AI = Banal as default just like the game always equated science and reason with Banal no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other paw, the Virtual Adepts are probably jumping for joy.<br /> <br /> Is the 'Google Metaverse' still a thing, or did we collectively give up on that? Can't remember the last time I've heard anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T22:18:12-07:00","id":1564228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564226#post1564226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've done studies about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I've actually read some of the papers and thus know this is considerably more nuanced than that, including being also able to do the opposite.<br /> <br /> The effect is similar to people that blindly trust any particular source for fast answers. This is far from a rare phenomenon, think workplace colleagues that rely so heavily on the one person in the office who read all the manuals, so taking their word as gospel is easier. Or that one that asks opinions/help/whatever from anyone and get upset when you try to help them think rather than just throw a ready to use choice.<br /> <br /> AI does facilitate this attitude immensely. That is a genuine problem. But it also let you tackle problems in other ways, a huge variety of them. You can use AI to challenge your arguments, to suggest sources, to rephrase things when the original explanation don't click. Those uses are actually good for your brain as found in many of the very same studies.<br /> <br /> What matters isn't the AI, is if and how the user engage with the process of finding answers and solving problems. A simple habit of asking the machine its sources to verify them makes a huge difference.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah. Not straightforward and the context behind it, a structure of labor that favor the workers seeking easy answers because they're run to exhaustion without being given reason to actually engage with what they do, and all sorts of trivia-based evaluations that reward parroting data without engaging it, this context is the real problem.<br /> <br /> Right now AI amplifies what we let it amplify. And those who benefit from amplifying stupidity can't have it better than if they're left with the system all for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T22:26:43-07:00","id":1564229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564227#post1564227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the 'Google Metaverse' still a thing, or did we collectively give up on that? Can't remember the last time I've heard anything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Virtual Adepts represent, and had always represented, digital counterculture rather than Tech Bros.<br /> <br /> In times of LLMs, the Tradition is probably split between those who reject LLMs as inherently tied to technocratic interests or something worse and those who embrace the Self-hosting AI movement that shares Open License models and work to shrink processing requirements.<br /> <br /> No Virtual Adept who just accepts the private cloud services should be respected, and anyone actually paying a subscription is to be marked for death as a traitor to the Traditions.<br /> <br /> As for Metaverse, I think it died. I've seen the ruckus in the corporate world from the inside, but it seems to have died down completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-20T23:59:39-07:00","id":1564230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564229#post1564229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Virtual Adepts represent, and had always represented, digital counterculture rather than Tech Bros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. I was more referring to the premise of humanity becoming more integrated with virtual reality, which is where the tradition shines most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T01:58:38-07:00","id":1564232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564225#post1564225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's me. I'm a Mage fans who thinks, &quot;How about No?&quot;<br /> <br /> I had no interest in seeing what kind of garbage fire M5 would have been. And since it's still Paradox in charge, I'm not that jazzed about a M6 either. What difference would it make? I don't trust them to be able to helm Mage: The Ascension without derailing it or putting all the good/interesting bits in the shredder.<br /> <br /> I'm just...so tired.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm frankly ambivalent as well, considering i was 'fine' to play mage and vtm revised forever from 2004 I doesn\u2019t really bother me if their isnt a new mage edition full stop, m20 was nice but i really wouldnt want something like werewolf or hunter 5th edition full stop and would be conflicted to something like v5.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather wait out for mage 40 or nothing at all than have a bad mage book with major infighting in the community which would follow. I've already got Awakening which is effectively mage 5th ed anyway. It's not like they're going to fix spheres or combat which is the most immediate concern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T03:03:12-07:00","id":1564234,"title":"","content":"I was honestly really excited about the idea of V6. I thought they would build on the legacy of V20 + V5. But what I have found, personally, doesn\u2019t have the essence that all the other editions had, from the classic editions through V20, V5, and CoD.<br /> <br /> <b>My impressions:</b><ul><li><b>Drama Points:</b> They feel unnecessary. If you use them exactly as described in the rules, players see them and start thinking about and fearing the consequences, and then they play accordingly based on what is on the table. This makes the adventure feel less natural. Also, I don\u2019t like using them as a Storyteller. We stopped using them after the second session.</li> <li><b>Quickening:</b> This takes us quite far away from what Vampire: The Masquerade is supposed to be. Giving out dice to be used on future rolls to build momentum might work well for a vampire in Frenzy or a werewolf giving in to their rage, but for an ordinary vampire, I don't like it. One thing is improving or rewarding the action you are currently taking; another is rewarding future actions. I'm sorry, but it takes me out of the World of Darkness, where we play so that bad things happen to us, where there are consequences, where we will often fail rolls and those failures will create more stories. This mechanic takes me away from everything I enjoy about telling Vampire stories.</li> <li><b>Vitae and Health being combined:</b> I understand what they were trying to do, but our group really hasn't liked it. I will say that we do like Hunger Dice, and we've played with them in V5 and V20 with some changes. Our group had a great time adapting Hunger Dice to V20, and another group has played V5 directly.<br /> <br /> Some of the problems we've encountered: we don't like the automatic healing. I've seen people at the table discussing and doing the math to figure out whether it's worth spending Vitae to activate Rouse abilities and Disciplines, only to fail the roll and end up worse off than they were at the beginning. As a result, in our games, many players preferred not to use certain powers in combat.<br /> <br /> In the end, you get a situation where they want to go hunting just to make sure they always have enough Vitae available. On the other hand, having more mental powers use Willpower makes you lose the feeling that you are <i>just blood</i>. I don't like the fact that a vampire can use magic or Disciplines through Willpower. Mechanically, it feels like you're compensating for certain Vitae costs with Willpower, which is something that had never been done before. I don't like the idea of a vampire being able to rely on something other than Vitae to perform their powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Vitae (Health) and Mana:</b> It might work well in other games, but I really don't like it for Vampire. It feels like a video game, something like Diablo.</li> <li><b>Beast/Humanity Tracker:</b> We've always liked the downward spiral towards the jaws of the Beast. This system needs a <i>very</i> major rethink. I'm sorry, but I could spend hours explaining why I don't think it works and how the system is going to be abused in different situations. I don't understand why they are trying to introduce dynamism into something that shouldn't be dynamic.</li> <li><b>Social Conflict:</b> We haven't really used it, no. Turning a diplomatic action into some kind of counterspell mechanic isn't our thing. In our storytelling-style games, everyone narrates. If you've given a really good performance based on your character's stats, great; if not, you roll the dice to determine the degree of your success against your opponent.</li> <li><b>The System:</b> It's not badly designed. But Vampire has always been about <i>the more dice I roll, the better</i>. I roll a lot of successes and have better actions because I'm older or more powerful, and the opponent does the same, allowing them to act as a proper challenge.<br /> <br /> Reducing dice pools through difficulty can be a very clever idea for other games, but for our group it doesn't <i>feel</i> like Vampire. Where is the possibility of rolling for the player without telling them the difficulty, keeping it secret, and creating fear and uncertainty? Where is the possibility of achieving truly glorious moments, like giving the best live performance of the last decade?</li> <li><b>Maturation:</b> We liked this. The idea is good and interesting, and it's something that should have been integrated several editions ago. We were already using something similar ourselves in V5, in our own way. Now it's all built into the system, which is great.</li> <li><b>Clan Traits:</b> The idea is there, but it could have been implemented in a much simpler way, with simpler powers based around the concepts and identities of the Clans. Instead, they've chosen to give them very powerful abilities to create Clan identity, and the result is that the characters become walking stereotypes. Not good.<br /> <br /> The philosophical Brujah get lost because they are now <i>the combat Clan</i> or <i>the super-strength Clan</i>. I really like the idea behind this system, but not the way it has been implemented. They could have introduced Lore Sheets or something similar that could be expanded upon, tying together Clan, lore, and other elements.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's an Alpha, so maybe they'll tweak it.</li> </ul><br /> I just want to say that this is <b>my opinion, or rather our group's opinion, after playing several sessions</b>. Maybe we've misunderstood or incorrectly applied some rules; there is a significant language barrier for us. It may also be partly our fault because we've been playing Vampire as our favorite game since the mid-90s.<br /> <br /> We've also played many other games, from D&amp;D and Pathfinder to Call of Cthulhu, OSR, PbtA, Trophy Dark, Trophy Gold, and many, many others. More than 30 years of roleplaying gives you a lot of experience.<br /> <br /> I think V6 has become the amalgamation that many people criticize V5 for being. xD<br /> <br /> It uses a lot of mechanics from games that are currently popular, and those mechanics work well for those games. But here, it feels like they're creating a <b>Frankenstein, a Vozhd that doesn't fit together and doesn't feel like Vampire: The Masquerade</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>\u201cA beast I am, lest a beast I become.\u201d</b><br /> <br /> Again, this is just <b>our impression and our opinion</b>, and it is not intended to disrespect anyone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T04:14:06-07:00","id":1564235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564234#post1564234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vitae (Health) and Mana:</b> </div> </div> </div> </div>I am <b>very curious</b> to hear more about how exactly this is going to work.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't blood healing supposed to cost vitae to use? In which case, the vampire spends vitae to repair their Health... which is also linked to their vitae. So you can spontaneously generate vitae without needing to feed?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or does this mean that blood healing has now become a cost free ability that vampires can use to reconstitute themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T04:19:58-07:00","id":1564236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564234#post1564234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Beast/Humanity Tracker:</b> We've always liked the downward spiral towards the jaws of the Beast. This system needs a <i>very</i> major rethink. I'm sorry, but I could spend hours explaining why I don't think it works and how the system is going to be abused in different situations. I don't understand why they are trying to introduce dynamism into something that shouldn't be dynamic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In this regard, I disagree. I think V6's approach to Humanity is probably the best version yet. It veers away from the idea of Humanity being a codified set of ethics that you're expected to follow like religious tenets, and instead presents us with the idea that your Humanity is exactly that; YOUR Humanity.<br /> <br /> It's the conflict between your inner Beast and the person that you were prior to being embraced. What defines Humanity and how the Beast interacts with it becomes a highly personalized aspect that is different for each individual.<br /> <br /> Which I think is far more interesting to explore in regards to future character concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T06:51:52-07:00","id":1564237,"title":"","content":"In V6, <b>Vitae functions almost like automatic regeneration of normal damage</b>. Normal damage that you suffer does not permanently reduce your ability to store Vitae. It simply represents injuries that a vampire\u2019s body can quickly heal by using its own Vitae.<br /> <br /> For example, if a vampire is struck in the head with an axe, the blow may injure them, but their body rapidly regenerates and the wound disappears. Even a much more severe injury, such as having a hand amputated, could eventually regenerate. The idea is that <b>normal damage heals automatically</b>, like an extremely fast supernatural regeneration.<br /> <br /> <b>Aggravated damage is different.</b> It represents wounds that normal regeneration cannot repair. In addition, aggravated damage points <b>occupy spaces in your maximum Vitae pool</b>.<br /> <br /> For example, imagine you have a maximum capacity of <b>15 Vitae</b>. If you have <b>3 points of aggravated damage</b>, those three points take up space. Even if you feed and have enough blood to refill your reserves, <b>you cannot exceed 12 effective Vitae</b> while those 3 aggravated damage points remain.<br /> To recover those lost spaces, you must <b>specifically heal the aggravated damage</b>, and doing so costs considerably more Vitae than ordinary regeneration. As a result, aggravated damage does not just hurt you in the moment; <b>it temporarily reduces your capacity to recover and store Vitae</b> until you manage to heal it.<br /> <br /> <b>In summary:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal damage \u2192 rapid/automatic regeneration \u2192 does not leave a permanent injury.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Aggravated damage \u2192 does not regenerate in the same way \u2192 requires spending Vitae specifically to heal it and occupies part of your Vitae capacity until it is healed.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564236#post1564236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this regard, I disagree. I think V6's approach to Humanity is probably the best version yet. It veers away from the idea of Humanity being a codified set of ethics that you're expected to follow like religious tenets, and instead presents us with the idea that your Humanity is exactly that; YOUR Humanity.<br /> <br /> It's the conflict between your inner Beast and the person that you were prior to being embraced. What defines Humanity and how the Beast interacts with it becomes a highly personalized aspect that is different for each individual.<br /> <br /> Which I think is far more interesting to explore in regards to future character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>I obviously ignore V20 because, in my view, the old Humanity design has been surpassed by both Chronicles of Darkness and V5.</b><br /> <br /> To compare them, V5 bases Humanity on principles, beliefs, and convictions. These do not have to be Christian values. They can be a mafioso's code of honor, Buddhist principles, or even the principles of a Path of Enlightenment such as those used by the Sabbat (which worked very well in my games). This version of Humanity rewards and punishes characters according to the vampire's own internal moral scale, measuring the struggle between their beliefs and the monster dwelling within them that seeks to pull them away from those beliefs, their Humanity. Humanity is gradually lost, and recovering it becomes increasingly difficult. This is why older vampires tend to become more detached and inhuman compared to neonates.<br /> Now, Humanity vs. Beast is presented as a balanced scale, with Beast on one side, Neutral in the center, and Human on the opposite end. It feels more like an Order-Chaos-Neutrality alignment system, similar to Moorcock or D&amp;D. The character moves back and forth across that scale.<br /> If you give in to the Beast and murder several hunters, as happens in the Alpha adventure, you move toward the Beast side one step for each killing. As a result, you gain Discipline bonuses because you reach Monstrous 3, but you also suffer penalties to social interactions and dealings with mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>What happens next?</b><br /> <br /> Players generally do not want to remain trapped on the monstrous side. They know they need to perform more humane or socially positive actions, so they immediately begin trying to correct the imbalance before it becomes worse and move themselves back toward the human side.<br /> Traditionally, Humanity existed in the background. It deteriorated slowly over time. In this new system, because Humanity and Beast are managed through visible trackers and opposing meters, the mechanic has to be pushed into play in a much more direct and explicit way.<ul><li>When a player's vampire has little Vitae, they feed.</li> <li>When a player's vampire has little Willpower, they pursue Ambitions or whatever is necessary to recover it.</li> <li>When a player is dangerously close to the Beast side, they rush to &quot;fix&quot; it in ways that often feel unnatural.</li> <li>When a player is dangerously close to the Humanity side, they may rush to commit monstrous acts because they are uncomfortable with where their character currently sits.</li> </ul>Lo explico de forma un tanto directa, pero esto es esencialmente lo que he experimentado en mis mesas.<br /> <br /> <b>Nadie parece sentirse c\u00f3modo con este sistema en la pr\u00e1ctica.</b> Al principio, a todos les pareci\u00f3 interesante e incluso bastante ingenioso, pero despu\u00e9s de un tiempo de juego empez\u00f3 a crear comportamientos que se sent\u00edan artificiales. En lugar de que la Humanidad sea una lucha interna lenta y gradual, se convierte en un ejercicio de gesti\u00f3n de recursos donde los jugadores monitorean constantemente un par de barras y ajustan su comportamiento para mantenerlas donde quieren. El resultado, al menos en mi experiencia, es que la lucha entre la Humanidad y la Bestia se siente menos org\u00e1nica y m\u00e1s mec\u00e1nica.<br /> <br /> <b>S\u00e9 que esto todav\u00eda es una alfa y que las cosas cambiar\u00e1n, pero les animo a que revisen las tablas que describen c\u00f3mo es su personaje dependiendo de si est\u00e1 en Bestia 1, Bestia 2 o Bestia 3, y de igual manera en Humano 1, Humano 2 o Humano 3.</b><br /> <br /> Cuando leo estas descripciones, lo que veo no es realmente Humanidad, sino m\u00e1s bien una escala deslizante entre <i>monstruo</i> y <i>humano</i> . Mi preocupaci\u00f3n es que esto tiende a animar a los jugadores a gestionar su posici\u00f3n en la balanza en lugar de experimentar la Humanidad como una lucha lenta y tr\u00e1gica que se erosiona gradualmente a lo largo de los siglos .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Combat: Another thing I didn't like, which I forgot to mention in my previous post, is combat. It feels much more restrictive, with conditions being a major focus, and that was one of the things I liked least about CoD. It also feels very similar to games like D&amp;D.</b><br /> <br /> All previous combat systems felt much more narrative than the current one. Because of that, there was much more room to describe scenes at whatever level of fiction or realism the group preferred. Now, like many other aspects of this edition, everything feels so heavily codified that it becomes abstract.<br /> You can place countless environmental elements around a scene: vases, fire hydrants, traffic signs, and so on. Yet it feels like the system is better played by focusing on its rules, distances, and mechanical structure. I don't like that approach. I've played a lot of OSR and D&amp;D, and now it feels much easier and more natural to put Vampire: The Masquerade on a battle map and play with miniatures.<br /> <br /> <b>That is not to my taste.</b><br /> <br /> I also don't like the idea of <b>diablerie through mere physical contact instead of having to bite and drink from another vampire.</b> The traditional act of diablerie is intimate, brutal, and transgressive. Reducing it to simple contact makes it feel less visceral and, in my opinion, less meaningful from both a thematic and narrative perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","user":"Slasher","date":". 09-21-2026, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T07:26:25-07:00","id":1564239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564232#post1564232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm frankly ambivalent as well, considering i was 'fine' to play mage and vtm revised forever from 2004 I doesn\u2019t really bother me if their isnt a new mage edition full stop, m20 was nice but i really wouldnt want something like werewolf or hunter 5th edition full stop and would be conflicted to something like v5.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather wait out for mage 40 or nothing at all than have a bad mage book with major infighting in the community which would follow. I've already got Awakening which is effectively mage 5th ed anyway. It's not like they're going to fix spheres or combat which is the most immediate concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, I don't have any confidence in another mage. Even M20 is a bit blogpost prose to it, I'm not sure how describe it. Very rambling. Still like it though.<br /> <br /> Mage just feels even more tied into owod than even vampire does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T09:39:02-07:00","id":1564241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564230#post1564230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know. I was more referring to the premise of humanity becoming more integrated with virtual reality, which is where the tradition shines most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that no proposition of Metaverse headed by corpos would have their trust, I'd say the VA was violently against that movement. It wasn't a good moment to them, it was a nightmare as it threatened the principle of decentralized and independent reality they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> V6 Playtest Humanity is a fundamental change of theme. I agree this is not VtM anymore. But is the new game worth playing? I think yes, so that's it. No major problem given I have V20 to play.<br /> <br /> And definitively an improvement over V5's Humanity. A system where a sin has the same weight all the way down and the goal is actively to turn characters into mindless beasts for the sake of it is an actual thematic harm, not a deviation. If played as written, it's just horrible.<br /> <br /> <br /> For Mage, here's the thing: M20 isn't going nowhere. Criticizing a bad game is beautiful and good. So is calling on their bullshit when they do unethical stuff like when W5 and H5 were launched (because yes, that level of utter disrespect for the fanbase is indeed unethical).<br /> <br /> But just wishing they don't do things? Sorry for the bluntness, but that's petty. Really petty. This is gate keeping (or wishing to), disregarding the right of others, including the owners of the IP, to enjoy their take on the game. For nothing besides the satisfaction of knowing other people can't have wrong fun.<br /> <br /> So I actually wish they make more games. That they try Changeling and Mage and Demon even if it is for me to furiously denounce all their shit afterwards. Let them makes the errors before I judge them. Let creators create.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T11:53:37-07:00","id":1564246,"title":"","content":"The Brujah haven't been philosopher kings for hundreds of years. The modern day Brujah are synonymous with leather clad, knuckle dragging thugs and miscreants, ranting about their lost glory. They are also the only clan who seems to have a positive memory about their beloved Carthage, while everyone else seems to be in agreement that it was a festering den of demonic worship and human sacrifices.<br /> <br /> As for discipline Maturation, I also really like this change. I see it as a theme of <i>'honing the basics'</i> while you study more advanced techniques. It also reminds me of old school D&amp;D spells, which became progressively stronger as you leveled, instead of needing to upcast them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T13:39:59-07:00","id":1564252,"title":"","content":"The leather clad miscreants are still ideologues and provocateurs that lead mobs with inflammatory discourse laced with Presence, as frequently or more than they solve things with personal strength.<br /> <br /> Ambiguity. The notion that they were in the past those peerless philosophers is dubious, even. But so is the idea that they've fell from grace.<br /> <br /> Do you really think the idea that political thinkers with hundreds of years that regularly Embrace thinkers of the new eras collectively devolved into mindless thugs in an extremely political environment?<br /> <br /> What is said about every clan is a mix of truth and prejudice, and the Brujah reflect what is heard all the time by politically engaged counter culture movements: conservatives and old guard of all sides bashing them as just a shadow of past glories regardless of what they can do, say or accomplish, because those old farts only see glory in their own past.<br /> <br /> Has the Brujah devolved into mere thugs? That is partially true, but also partially false, with the precise proportion depending on the ST. There is a reason why they're a founding Camarilla clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T13:49:59-07:00","id":1564253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564252#post1564252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really think the idea that political thinkers with hundreds of years that regularly Embrace thinkers of the new eras collectively devolved into mindless thugs in an extremely political environment?</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Brujah were emotionless, introspective scholars, who's interactions with the world were driven by cold, calculated logic.<br /> <br /> After Troile took over, they became a clan of hot blooded, passionately tempered rebels. They went from a clan with a plan, to a clan that was just throwing darts at the wall, and seeing which ideas manage to stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/co