hem that seeks to pull them away from those beliefs, their Humanity. Humanity is gradually lost, and recovering it becomes increasingly difficult. This is why older vampires tend to become more detached and inhuman compared to neonates.<br /> Now, Humanity vs. Beast is presented as a balanced scale, with Beast on one side, Neutral in the center, and Human on the opposite end. It feels more like an Order-Chaos-Neutrality alignment system, similar to Moorcock or D&amp;D. The character moves back and forth across that scale.<br /> If you give in to the Beast and murder several hunters, as happens in the Alpha adventure, you move toward the Beast side one step for each killing. As a result, you gain Discipline bonuses because you reach Monstrous 3, but you also suffer penalties to social interactions and dealings with mortals.<br /> <br /> <b>What happens next?</b><br /> <br /> Players generally do not want to remain trapped on the monstrous side. They know they need to perform more humane or socially positive actions, so they immediately begin trying to correct the imbalance before it becomes worse and move themselves back toward the human side.<br /> Traditionally, Humanity existed in the background. It deteriorated slowly over time. In this new system, because Humanity and Beast are managed through visible trackers and opposing meters, the mechanic has to be pushed into play in a much more direct and explicit way.<ul><li>When a player's vampire has little Vitae, they feed.</li> <li>When a player's vampire has little Willpower, they pursue Ambitions or whatever is necessary to recover it.</li> <li>When a player is dangerously close to the Beast side, they rush to &quot;fix&quot; it in ways that often feel unnatural.</li> <li>When a player is dangerously close to the Humanity side, they may rush to commit monstrous acts because they are uncomfortable with where their character currently sits.</li> </ul>Lo explico de forma un tanto directa, pero esto es esencialmente lo que he experimentado en mis mesas.<br /> <br /> <b>Nadie parece sentirse c\u00f3modo con este sistema en la pr\u00e1ctica.</b> Al principio, a todos les pareci\u00f3 interesante e incluso bastante ingenioso, pero despu\u00e9s de un tiempo de juego empez\u00f3 a crear comportamientos que se sent\u00edan artificiales. En lugar de que la Humanidad sea una lucha interna lenta y gradual, se convierte en un ejercicio de gesti\u00f3n de recursos donde los jugadores monitorean constantemente un par de barras y ajustan su comportamiento para mantenerlas donde quieren. El resultado, al menos en mi experiencia, es que la lucha entre la Humanidad y la Bestia se siente menos org\u00e1nica y m\u00e1s mec\u00e1nica.<br /> <br /> <b>S\u00e9 que esto todav\u00eda es una alfa y que las cosas cambiar\u00e1n, pero les animo a que revisen las tablas que describen c\u00f3mo es su personaje dependiendo de si est\u00e1 en Bestia 1, Bestia 2 o Bestia 3, y de igual manera en Humano 1, Humano 2 o Humano 3.</b><br /> <br /> Cuando leo estas descripciones, lo que veo no es realmente Humanidad, sino m\u00e1s bien una escala deslizante entre <i>monstruo</i> y <i>humano</i> . Mi preocupaci\u00f3n es que esto tiende a animar a los jugadores a gestionar su posici\u00f3n en la balanza en lugar de experimentar la Humanidad como una lucha lenta y tr\u00e1gica que se erosiona gradualmente a lo largo de los siglos .<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Combat: Another thing I didn't like, which I forgot to mention in my previous post, is combat. It feels much more restrictive, with conditions being a major focus, and that was one of the things I liked least about CoD. It also feels very similar to games like D&amp;D.</b><br /> <br /> All previous combat systems felt much more narrative than the current one. Because of that, there was much more room to describe scenes at whatever level of fiction or realism the group preferred. Now, like many other aspects of this edition, everything feels so heavily codified that it becomes abstract.<br /> You can place countless environmental elements around a scene: vases, fire hydrants, traffic signs, and so on. Yet it feels like the system is better played by focusing on its rules, distances, and mechanical structure. I don't like that approach. I've played a lot of OSR and D&amp;D, and now it feels much easier and more natural to put Vampire: The Masquerade on a battle map and play with miniatures.<br /> <br /> <b>That is not to my taste.</b><br /> <br /> I also don't like the idea of <b>diablerie through mere physical contact instead of having to bite and drink from another vampire.</b> The traditional act of diablerie is intimate, brutal, and transgressive. Reducing it to simple contact makes it feel less visceral and, in my opinion, less meaningful from both a thematic and narrative perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T20:49:04-07:00","id":1564260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564253#post1564253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original Brujah were emotionless, introspective scholars, who's interactions with the world were driven by cold, calculated logic.<br /> <br /> After Troile took over, they became a clan of hot blooded, passionately tempered rebels. They went from a clan with a plan, to a clan that was just throwing darts at the wall, and seeing which ideas manage to stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to themselves, and they're not the members of the clan that gave it fame as philosophers, if they're members of the clan at all, because the True Brujah don't have actual evidence of their claims.<br /> <br /> Even if taken as truth, the Brujah curse would be from \u22483000 BCE or earlier. The clan built its fame as philosopher kings from 2000 BCE, with most of their greatest being from 700 BCE to 300 AD.<br /> <br /> So their fame is entirely built on vampires from more than a thousand years after they became cursed with anger, none of them ever hinted to be from the True Brujah line. And, you know, it is cursed with anger because philosophers are known to be passionate, especially political ones.<br /> <br /> Who's said to be an emotionless scholar is [Brujah] himself, and even then intolerant to the idea of any childe of his holding just a copy of his ideas.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26793_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26793\" data-vbnamecard=\"26793\">Slasher</a> setting aside differences in taste/understanding of the themes of the game, I think one perspective to consider for this new Humanity Scale is exactly the otherness of the impulses being discussed.<br /> <br /> The Beast is an alien thing. The game has always been clear that the vampire doesn't feel it as a normal personality trait, but something inside growling and fighting for dominance. It's a Thing sending urges the character struggle to control, but ultimately aren't really theirs. Even if their actions and emotions feed or deny this thing, the thing itself is not them and loosing Humanity is loosing your own unique Self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T21:37:52-07:00","id":1564261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564257#post1564257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you give in to the Beast and murder several hunters, as happens in the Alpha adventure, you move toward the Beast side one step for each killing. As a result, you gain Discipline bonuses because you reach Monstrous 3, but you also suffer penalties to social interactions and dealings with mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the idea that killing in and of itself is a violation against Humanity.<br /> <br /> Since when have humans ever been afraid of killing things? It's our favorite pasttime!<br /> <br /> In fact, we love killing so much, we had to come up with a system of rules for it, to ensure we didn't go overboard!<br /> <br /> What triggers a Humanity break should not be the deed, but the motivations behind said deed, and how it was carried out.<br /> <br /> There is a right way and a wrong way to dispose of your enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>Right Way:</b> bullet to the back of the head, execution style.<br /> <br /> <b>Wrong Way:</b> Beating them to death with the severed limbs of their allies.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> Very strongly agree with you on the idea how Diablerie is performed now.<br /> <br /> They took what vampires consider to be the most heinous crime imaginable, and turned it into something sensual! Dare I say, even romantic in its own way!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T22:01:09-07:00","id":1564262,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Brujah, for all we know is that the antidulivan might have been going through a prolonged period of mental breakdown and Trolie could be an effect of the process. Mental instability isn't just strictly a Malkavian curse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-21T23:35:31-07:00","id":1564265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564261#post1564261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when have humans ever been afraid of killing things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since at least some hundreds of thousands of years ago.<br /> <br /> Let's set aside genre and whatnot to talk reality:<br /> <br /> Despite the high level of violence in our history, humans have a built-in psychological barrier against killing other humans, and a tendency to generalize human identification.<br /> <br /> While it's not an absolute, far from it, it is quite effective. For most people killing is legitimately hard, and this difficulty extends to anything that reminds humans strongly enough to your psyche. Enough pressure will pierce the barrier, but not without trauma and not remove it, the barrier is still there.<br /> <br /> Historically most casualties of wars and other forms of violence are due post-battle infection of wounds, not lethal injuries. The actual rate of death blows was relatively low. Even the rate of death from infection wasn't that big, in most battles the majority of soldiers in the losing side would survive, either recovered or taken as hostages by the winners.<br /> <br /> No one ever liked to kill without a good deal of mental illness. The reason ruthless generals and battles of annihilation became famous is precisely because they were the rare exception. The trope of &quot;killing costs your soul&quot; is old and reflects the descriptions given by veteran soldiers of the feeling and trauma of killing. And many indirect methods are favored because they create a psychological disconnect between actions and consequence.<br /> <br /> In fact the current US Armed Forces are the most lethal in recorded history by proportion of direct deliberate deaths per thousand enemies engaged and that's a matter of study of several scientific papers. The reason is the systematic implementation of equipment and procedures that create emotional disconnection, a result of decades of internal psychology research. But the price was the rise of PTSD, it is also maybe they most mentally ill veterans in the world, and that's something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T01:33:48-07:00","id":1564266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564234#post1564234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Beast/Humanity Tracker:</b> We've always liked the downward spiral towards the jaws of the Beast. This system needs a <i>very</i> major rethink. I'm sorry, but I could spend hours explaining why I don't think it works and how the system is going to be abused in different situations. I don't understand why they are trying to introduce dynamism into something that shouldn't be dynamic<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I personally think V6 version of Humanity is actually more suitable for WtA than VtM and I generally hope that White wolf decides to stick with this system for W6 or at least a enterprising ST decides to back port it to W5 as a replacement for the Hauglosk and Harano bars.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T05:05:40-07:00","id":1564270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564241#post1564241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Mage, here's the thing: M20 isn't going nowhere. Criticizing a bad game is beautiful and good. So is calling on their bullshit when they do unethical stuff like when W5 and H5 were launched (because yes, that level of utter disrespect for the fanbase is indeed unethical).<br /> <br /> But just wishing they don't do things? Sorry for the bluntness, but that's petty. Really petty. This is gate keeping (or wishing to), disregarding the right of others, including the owners of the IP, to enjoy their take on the game. For nothing besides the satisfaction of knowing other people can't have wrong fun.<br /> <br /> So I actually wish they make more games. That they try Changeling and Mage and Demon even if it is for me to furiously denounce all their shit afterwards. Let them makes the errors before I judge them. Let creators create.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is along my lines if thinking. Are we better off when Paradox puts out bad interpretations of WoD systems than none? It's arguable but I'd say that we are. Even if one thinks that V5 is the abomination that should burn in the fires of Hell it still brings new people to the World of Darkness and some of them wil discover all those books that made us love the setting ages ago. And among the deluge of mediocre material there will be some Cults of the Blood Gods or Courts of the Damned, good and interesting books that might be useful even for seasoned players.<br /> <br /> As You say, the Legacy editions are not going anywhere and V6 or D7 is not going to stop us from enjoying all those previous books and play our magick wielding Ahrimane/Get of Fenris abominations. And At worst, Paradox will give us shit to complain till we draw our final breats. Win-win <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T12:08:31-07:00","id":1564273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564270#post1564270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is along my lines if thinking. Are we better off when Paradox puts out bad interpretations of WoD systems than none? It's arguable but I'd say that we are. Even if one thinks that V5 is the abomination that should burn in the fires of Hell it still brings new people to the World of Darkness and some of them wil discover all those books that made us love the setting ages ago. And among the deluge of mediocre material there will be some Cults of the Blood Gods or Courts of the Damned, good and interesting books that might be useful even for seasoned players.<br /> <br /> As You say, the Legacy editions are not going anywhere and V6 or D7 is not going to stop us from enjoying all those previous books and play our magick wielding Ahrimane/Get of Fenris abominations. And At worst, Paradox will give us shit to complain till we draw our final breats. Win-win <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but feel like anyone who comes here from 5th edition is going to be in for an extremely rude awakening, when they start examining previous editions of the game. Largely due to the fact that 5th edition was trying to sanitize everything and apologize for its previous editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, boy, 5th edition World of Darkness was pretty neat. Let's see what this 'Freak Legion' book has in it.... OH, GOOD HEAVENS!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 09-22-2026, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T12:15:32-07:00","id":1564274,"title":"","content":"Ahh fomori... <br /> <i>In hatred of thy soul</i><br /> <i>See thine flesh revolt</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T13:20:49-07:00","id":1564276,"title":"","content":"I do find it amusing that after all of the name changes and the &quot;Fianna is just a word!&quot; business... W5 forgot to change fomori to something else, like the old standby of mockery. So it still has that sticking out like a sore thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T14:08:44-07:00","id":1564278,"title":"","content":"Nothing beats changing Eldar to Aeldari in 40k.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh we're not Kindred, we're <b>Cainedrarie</b>... &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T15:57:03-07:00","id":1564281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564273#post1564273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Oh, boy, 5th edition World of Darkness was pretty neat. Let's see what this 'Freak Legion' book has in it.... OH, GOOD HEAVENS!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, anyone who never read a Black Dog book is in for a rude awakening with Freak Legion.<br /> <br /> And anyone reading this and having ideas: you genuinely are better off not opening that thing. It doesn't have forbidden secrets or desires, nor good rules, it's just shock for the sake of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T17:00:32-07:00","id":1564285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562353-faq-on-6th-edition?p=1564281#post1564281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, anyone who never read a Black Dog book is in for a rude awakening with Freak Legion.<br /> <br /> And anyone reading this and having ideas: you genuinely are better off not opening that thing. It doesn't have forbidden secrets or desires, nor good rules, it's just shock for the sake of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it had some attempts at social commentary mixed in there with the material that would be at home in Overfiend. And by that, I don't just meant, tentacles or crimes that someone might associate with tentacles, but... (spoiled for worse things, do not open)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The fact that Throwbacks are implied to kill their victims or occasional partners during sex, in spectacular and grotesque splatter fashion, which is a thing that happens in Urotsukidouji often enough that it's even more off-putting than the &quot;default&quot; of tentacles without consent or humanity.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But if you're looking for Normalites or Sicklungs and their attendant social commentary, they're in the W20 Book of the Wyrm without the Throwback fomori, so, as you note, Freak Legion is pretty much only on a buy list if you're looking to complete a collection, or you were living in the pre-W20 era and were looking for possessed material beyond Possessed (itself tainted by its author's crimes, one of which was much more current when that book was written, and puts certain parts of it into a much harsher perspective).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T17:18:25-07:00","id":1564286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"